                         <!-- ========== 2 DISPLAY CAMPAIGN STRUCTURE & COMPONENTS ========== -->
<div class="section" id="topic-2">
    <div class="card mb-4 border">
        <div class="card-header bg-white py-3">
            <h2 class="mb-0">2 Display Campaign Structure & Components</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            
            <div class="alert alert-light border mb-4">
                <strong> Build for clarity and control.</strong> A well‑organised display campaign makes optimisation easier and performance more predictable. Understand the hierarchy and key components before launching.
            </div>
            
            <p>Google Ads display campaigns follow the same three‑layer structure as search campaigns, but the components differ slightly in their options and settings. Proper campaign structure is the foundation of profitable display advertising.</p>

            <!-- ==================== VISUAL HIERARCHY ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Visual Hierarchy of Google Ads Structure</h3>
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded mb-0" style="font-family: monospace;">
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                         GOOGLE ADS ACCOUNT                              │
│                    (Billing, Users, Access Levels)                      │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                    │
                                    ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                           CAMPAIGN LEVEL                                │
│  • Budget & Bidding Strategy    • Location & Language                   │
│  • Ad Scheduling                • Frequency Caps                        │
│  • Content Exclusions           • Campaign Type (Display)               │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                    │
                                    ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                           AD GROUP LEVEL                                │
│  • Targeting Method (Audience, Topic, Placement, Keyword)              │
│  • Bid Adjustments              • Ad Rotation                           │
│  • Default Bids                                                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                    │
                                    ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                              AD LEVEL                                   │
│  • Final URL                    • Headlines (Short & Long)              │
│  • Descriptions                 • Images (1:1 & 1.91:1)                 │
│  • Logo                         • Business Name                         │
│  • CTA Button                   • Tracking Templates                     │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</pre>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 1: CAMPAIGN LEVEL ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Campaign Level – Strategic Foundation</h3>
            
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-md-12">
                    <div class="card mb-4">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h4> Campaign Naming Convention</h4>
                            <p>Use a consistent naming convention for easy reporting and management:</p>
                            <div class="alert alert-secondary">
                                <strong>Format:</strong> [Campaign Type] - [Goal] - [Targeting] - [Date]
                                <br>
                                <strong>Examples:</strong>
                                <ul class="mb-0 mt-2">
                                    <li><code>GDN - Awareness - Affinity_Fashion - 2025</code></li>
                                    <li><code>GDN - Remarketing - Cart_Abandoners - 30_Days</code></li>
                                    <li><code>GDN - Consideration - InMarket_Automotive - 2025</code></li>
                                    <li><code>GDN - Conversions - Custom_Intent_Software - Q1</code></li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Campaign Settings Table -->
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Setting</th>
                            <th>Options</th>
                            <th>Best Practice</th>
                            <th>Impact</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Budget</strong></td>
                            <td>Daily budget (campaign or shared)</td>
                            <td>Start with $20-50/day for prospecting, $10-20/day for remarketing</td>
                            <td>Controls daily spend limit</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Bidding Strategies</strong></td>
                            <td>Maximize clicks, Maximize conversions, Target CPA, Target ROAS, vCPM</td>
                            <td>Start with Maximize clicks (collect data) → Switch to Target CPA after 30 conversions</td>
                            <td>Determines how Google spends your budget</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Location Targeting</strong></td>
                            <td>"Presence" vs "Presence or interest"</td>
                            <td>Use <strong>"Presence"</strong> to target people physically in your location</td>
                            <td>Prevents serving ads to searchers outside your target area</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Language Targeting</strong></td>
                            <td>Select languages your customers speak</td>
                            <td>Choose the language of your ads & landing page</td>
                            <td>Ensures ads shown to users with matching language settings</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Ad Scheduling</strong></td>
                            <td>Set specific hours/days for ads to run</td>
                            <td>Schedule during business hours or peak conversion times (analyze GA4 data)</td>
                            <td>Prevents wasted spend on non-converting hours</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Frequency Caps</strong></td>
                            <td>Max impressions per user/day/week/month</td>
                            <td>Prospecting: 3-5/day, Remarketing: 1-2/day</td>
                            <td>Prevents ad fatigue & brand hatred</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-warning mt-2">
                <strong> Critical Warning:</strong> Never use "Presence or interest" for location targeting unless you explicitly want to reach people interested in your location (e.g., vacation rentals, relocation services). Otherwise, you'll waste budget on users searching about your city from across the world.
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 2: CONTENT EXCLUSIONS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Content Exclusions – Protecting Your Brand</h3>
            
            <div class="row mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card">
                        <div class="card-header bg-danger text-white"> Exclude These Content Types</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Sexual content</strong> - Explicit or suggestive material</li>
                                <li><strong>Tragedy & conflict</strong> - Death, violence, terrorist acts</li>
                                <li><strong>Profanity & vulgar language</strong> - Offensive content</li>
                                <li><strong>Parked domains</strong> - Inactive/dead websites</li>
                                <li><strong>Error pages</strong> - 404 pages, redirects</li>
                                <li><strong>Digitally manipulated media</strong> - Fake news, deepfakes</li>
                                <li><strong>Gambling & casinos</strong> - Unless you're a gambling advertiser</li>
                                <li><strong>Weapons & military</strong> - For most brands</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white"> How to Configure Exclusions</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>At Campaign Level:</strong></p>
                            <ol>
                                <li>Navigate to Campaign Settings → Content exclusions</li>
                                <li>Select sensitive content categories</li>
                                <li>Choose content type (Audio, Video, Text, Display)</li>
                                <li>Apply to specific campaigns or entire account</li>
                            </ol>
                            <p><strong>At Account Level:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Shared library → Content exclusions → Create exclusion list</li>
                                <li>Apply to multiple campaigns simultaneously</li>
                                <li>Dynamic exclusions via scripts & automation</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-info small mt-2">
                                 <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Regularly review placement reports and add underperforming or irrelevant sites as negative placements.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 3: AD GROUP LEVEL ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Ad Group Level – Targeting Themes</h3>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white"> Ad Group Naming Convention</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Name ad groups based on targeting method & theme:</p>
                            <div class="alert alert-secondary">
                                <strong>Examples:</strong>
                                <ul class="mb-0">
                                    <li><code>Audience - InMarket - Running Shoes</code></li>
                                    <li><code>Placement - TechCrunch_Technology</code></li>
                                    <li><code>Topic - Automotive_Industry</code></li>
                                    <li><code>Remarketing - Cart_Abandoners_14_Days</code></li>
                                    <li><code>Custom_Intent - CRM_Software_Search</code></li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                            <p class="mt-2">This makes reporting & optimization much easier!</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white"> Bid Adjustments</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Adjust bids for specific audience segments based on performance:</p>
                            <div class="table-responsive">
                                <table class="table table-sm">
                                    <thead class="table-light">
                                        <tr><th>Adjustment Type</th><th>Recommended Range</th><th>When to Use</th></tr>
                                    </thead>
                                    <tbody>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Device (Mobile)</td>
                                            <td>+20% to +50%</td>
                                            <td>Mobile converts better</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Device (Desktop)</td>
                                            <td>-10% to -20%</td>
                                            <td>Desktop underperforms</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Location</td>
                                            <td>+10% to +30%</td>
                                            <td>High-performing regions</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Ad Schedule</td>
                                            <td>+15% to +25%</td>
                                            <td>Peak conversion hours</td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </tbody>
                                </table>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Ad Group Targeting Methods -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-3"> Targeting Methods Available at Ad Group Level</h4>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-3">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white"> Audiences</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Target specific user segments based on behavior & interests</p>
                            <strong>Types:</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Affinity (broad interests)</li>
                                <li>In-market (purchase intent)</li>
                                <li>Custom (URLs, keywords, apps)</li>
                                <li>Remarketing (past visitors)</li>
                                <li>Customer Match (email lists)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-3">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white"> Topics</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Show ads on pages about specific topics</p>
                            <strong>Examples:</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Arts & Entertainment</li>
                                <li>Autos & Vehicles</li>
                                <li>Beauty & Fitness</li>
                                <li>Business & Industrial</li>
                                <li>Technology & Computing</li>
                            </ul>
                            <span class="badge bg-secondary">Broad reach, contextual</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-3">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark"> Placements</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Manually select specific websites, apps, or YouTube channels</p>
                            <strong>Examples:</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li><code>nytimes.com</code></li>
                                <li><code>youtube.com/channel/UC...</code></li>
                                <li><code>cnn.com</code></li>
                                <li><code>techcrunch.com</code></li>
                            </ul>
                            <span class="badge bg-secondary">Precision targeting</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-3">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-danger text-white"> Keywords</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Target pages with specific keywords (contextual, not search)</p>
                            <strong>Examples:</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li>"running shoes"</li>
                                <li>"best CRM software"</li>
                                <li>"project management tools"</li>
                            </ul>
                            <span class="badge bg-secondary">Contextual relevance</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 4: AD ROTATION ==================== -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-3"> Ad Rotation Settings</h4>
            
            <div class="alert alert-info mb-4">
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <strong> "Optimize" (Default & Recommended)</strong>
                        <ul class="mb-0 mt-2">
                            <li>Google shows best-performing ads more often</li>
                            <li>Uses machine learning to predict CTR & conversions</li>
                            <li>Ideal for most campaigns (goals: conversions, traffic)</li>
                            <li>Requires sufficient conversion data (minimum 30-50 conversions)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <strong> "Rotate Indefinitely"</strong>
                        <ul class="mb-0 mt-2">
                            <li>Show all ads equally, regardless of performance</li>
                            <li><strong>Only for A/B testing</strong> with equal impression distribution</li>
                            <li>Use for 2-4 weeks, then analyze results</li>
                            <li>Switch back to "Optimize" after identifying winners</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 5: AD LEVEL (RESPONSIVE DISPLAY ADS) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Ad Level – Responsive Display Ads (RDA)</h3>
            
            <div class="alert alert-primary mb-4">
                <strong> Why Responsive Display Ads?</strong> RDAs are Google's recommended format for display campaigns because they:
                <ul class="mb-0 mt-2">
                    <li> Automatically optimize for any ad size & placement</li>
                    <li> Test thousands of combinations using machine learning</li>
                    <li> Increase conversions by up to 50% vs static image ads</li>
                    <li> Reduce creative production time & cost</li>
                    <li> Work across all GDN placements (websites, apps, YouTube)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <!-- RDA Components Table -->
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Component</th>
                            <th>Requirements</th>
                            <th>Best Practices</th>
                            <th>Character Limit</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Final URL</strong></td>
                            <td>Landing page URL</td>
                            <td>Match ad content to landing page; ensure mobile-optimized</td>
                            <td>N/A</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Short Headline</strong></td>
                            <td>Minimum 1, recommended 3-5</td>
                            <td>Include benefit, offer, or CTA; test variations</td>
                            <td>30 characters</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Long Headline</strong></td>
                            <td>Optional, recommended 1-2</td>
                            <td>More descriptive; used in larger ad sizes</td>
                            <td>90 characters</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Descriptions</strong></td>
                            <td>Minimum 1, recommended 3-5</td>
                            <td>Highlight USPs, features, urgency, or CTA</td>
                            <td>90 characters</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Images</strong></td>
                            <td>Minimum 2 (1 landscape + 1 square)</td>
                            <td>Landscape (1.91:1): 1200x628<br>Square (1:1): 1200x1200</td>
                            <td>N/A</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Logo</strong></td>
                            <td>Required</td>
                            <td>Square (1:1) ratio, transparent background, min 128x128</td>
                            <td>N/A</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Business Name</strong></td>
                            <td>Required</td>
                            <td>Use exact brand name, consistent with landing page</td>
                            <td>25 characters</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>CTA Text</strong></td>
                            <td>Optional (Google may auto-apply)</td>
                            <td>Choose from pre-set options: "Shop Now", "Sign Up", "Learn More", "Get Quote", "Subscribe"</td>
                            <td>Varies</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <!-- Image Specifications -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Image Specifications for Responsive Display Ads</h4>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white"> Landscape (1.91:1)</div>
                        <div class="card-body text-center">
                            <span class="badge bg-success mb-2">Recommended</span>
                            <p><strong>1200 x 628 pixels</strong></p>
                            <p>Minimum: 600 x 314</p>
                            <p>Maximum: 5000 x 5000</p>
                            <hr>
                            <small>Best for: Most placements, YouTube banners</small>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">🔲 Square (1:1)</div>
                        <div class="card-body text-center">
                            <span class="badge bg-success mb-2">Recommended</span>
                            <p><strong>1200 x 1200 pixels</strong></p>
                            <p>Minimum: 300 x 300</p>
                            <p>Maximum: 5000 x 5000</p>
                            <hr>
                            <small>Best for: Social feeds, mobile placements</small>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-info text-white"> Thumbnail (4:3)</div>
                        <div class="card-body text-center">
                            <span class="badge bg-secondary mb-2">Optional</span>
                            <p><strong>128 x 128 pixels (min)</strong></p>
                            <p>Used for small placements</p>
                            <hr>
                            <small>Best for: Small ad slots, non-critical placements</small>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Creative Asset Checklist -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Responsive Display Ad Asset Checklist</h4>
            
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h5>Minimum Requirements:</h5>
                            <ul class="mb-0">
                                <li>□ 1 short headline</li>
                                <li>□ 1 description</li>
                                <li>□ 1 landscape image (1.91:1)</li>
                                <li>□ 1 square image (1:1)</li>
                                <li>□ 1 logo</li>
                                <li>□ Business name</li>
                                <li>□ Final URL</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h5>Recommended for Best Performance:</h5>
                            <ul class="mb-0">
                                <li>□ 5 short headlines</li>
                                <li>□ 1-2 long headlines</li>
                                <li>□ 5 descriptions</li>
                                <li>□ 3-5 landscape images</li>
                                <li>□ 3-5 square images</li>
                                <li>□ 1 logo (transparent background)</li>
                                <li>□ All images high resolution (1200x628/1200x1200)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="alert alert-primary mt-3 mb-0">
                        <strong> Pro Tip:</strong> The more assets you provide, the more combinations Google can test. Advertisers using 5+ headlines and 5+ descriptions see <strong>15-30% higher CTR</strong> and <strong>10-20% lower CPA</strong> compared to minimum requirements.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 6: HEADLINE & DESCRIPTION BEST PRACTICES ==================== -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4">✍ Headline & Description Best Practices</h4>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white"> Strong CTAs</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul>
                                <li>"Shop Now & Save 20%"</li>
                                <li>"Get Free Quote Today"</li>
                                <li>"Start Your Free Trial"</li>
                                <li>"Download The Guide"</li>
                                <li>"Book Your Appointment"</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark"> Benefit-Focused</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul>
                                <li>"Boost Sales by 40%"</li>
                                <li>"Save 10 Hours Per Week"</li>
                                <li>"Earn 5% Cash Back"</li>
                                <li>"Join 10,000+ Happy Customers"</li>
                                <li>"Get Results in 30 Days"</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-danger text-white"> Urgency & FOMO</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul>
                                <li>"Limited Time Offer"</li>
                                <li>"Only 5 Left in Stock"</li>
                                <li>"Sale Ends Tonight"</li>
                                <li>"Don't Miss Out"</li>
                                <li>"Today Only: Free Shipping"</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-danger mb-4">
                <strong> Avoid These Headline Mistakes:</strong>
                <ul class="mb-0">
                    <li> Clickbait (misleading claims)</li>
                    <li> All caps ("SHOP NOW!!!")</li>
                    <li> Generic statements ("We Sell Quality Products")</li>
                    <li> No clear value proposition</li>
                    <li> Missing the brand name (for retargeting)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 7: TRACKING TEMPLATES ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Tracking Templates & UTM Parameters</h3>
            
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>Add tracking templates to measure campaign performance accurately in Google Analytics.</p>
                    <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded mb-0">
{lpurl}?utm_source=google&utm_medium=cpc&utm_campaign={campaignid}&utm_content={adgroupid}&utm_term={creative}</pre>
                    
                    <div class="row mt-3">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <strong>UTM Parameter Breakdown:</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li><code>utm_source=google</code> - Traffic source</li>
                                <li><code>utm_medium=cpc</code> - Marketing medium</li>
                                <li><code>utm_campaign={campaignid}</code> - Campaign identifier</li>
                                <li><code>utm_content={adgroupid}</code> - Ad group identifier</li>
                                <li><code>utm_term={creative}</code> - Creative version</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <strong>Available ValueTrack Parameters:</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li><code>{campaignid}</code> - Campaign ID</li>
                                <li><code>{adgroupid}</code> - Ad group ID</li>
                                <li><code>{creative}</code> - Creative/Ad ID</li>
                                <li><code>{device}</code> - Device type (c/m/t)</li>
                                <li><code>{network}</code> - Network (g/display/youtube)</li>
                                <li><code>{placement}</code> - Website where ad appeared</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 8: OPTIMIZATION SCORECARD ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Display Campaign Optimization Scorecard</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <div class="text-center p-3 bg-light rounded">
                                <span class="display-6"></span>
                                <p class="fw-bold mt-2">Campaign Level</p>
                                <small class="text-muted">Budget, bidding, scheduling, exclusions</small>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <div class="text-center p-3 bg-light rounded">
                                <span class="display-6"></span>
                                <p class="fw-bold mt-2">Ad Group Level</p>
                                <small class="text-muted">Targeting methods, bid adjustments</small>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <div class="text-center p-3 bg-light rounded">
                                <span class="display-6"></span>
                                <p class="fw-bold mt-2">Ad Level</p>
                                <small class="text-muted">Creative assets, headlines, CTAs</small>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <div class="text-center p-3 bg-light rounded">
                                <span class="display-6"></span>
                                <p class="fw-bold mt-2">Tracking Level</p>
                                <small class="text-muted">UTMs, conversions, analytics</small>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 9: COMMON STRUCTURE MISTAKES ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> 8 Common Display Campaign Structure Mistakes</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Mistake</th>
                            <th>Consequence</th>
                            <th>Fix</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Mixing targeting types in one ad group</td>
                            <td>Unclear performance data, difficult optimization</td>
                            <td>Create separate ad groups for each targeting method</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Too few ad assets</td>
                            <td>Limited AI optimization, lower CTR</td>
                            <td>Add 5+ headlines, 5+ descriptions, 5+ images</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No frequency caps</td>
                            <td>Ad fatigue, brand hatred, wasted impressions</td>
                            <td>Set 3-5 impressions per user/day</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Using default location targeting</td>
                            <td>Ads shown to irrelevant searchers worldwide</td>
                            <td>Switch to "Presence" for targeted campaigns</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Ignoring content exclusions</td>
                            <td>Ads on inappropriate sites, brand safety risk</td>
                            <td>Exclude sensitive categories & review placements weekly</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>One ad group per campaign</td>
                            <td>Can't optimize different targeting themes separately</td>
                            <td>Create 3-10 ad groups per campaign by theme</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No bid adjustments</td>
                            <td>Overpaying for underperforming segments</td>
                            <td>Adjust bids for devices, locations, schedules</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Missing tracking parameters</td>
                            <td>Can't measure performance by ad/placement</td>
                            <td>Add UTM tracking templates at campaign level</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 10: QUICK REFERENCE ==================== -->
            <div class="alert alert-info mt-4">
                <h3 class="fw-bold"> Display Campaign Structure Summary</h3>
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <strong>Campaign Level:</strong>
                        <ul class="small mb-0">
                            <li>Budget & bidding strategy</li>
                            <li>Location & language</li>
                            <li>Ad scheduling & frequency caps</li>
                            <li>Content exclusions</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <strong>Ad Group Level:</strong>
                        <ul class="small mb-0">
                            <li>Targeting method (1 per ad group)</li>
                            <li>Bid adjustments</li>
                            <li>Ad rotation settings</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <strong>Ad Level:</strong>
                        <ul class="small mb-0">
                            <li>5+ headlines</li>
                            <li>5+ descriptions</li>
                            <li>3-5 landscape images</li>
                            <li>3-5 square images</li>
                            <li>Logo & business name</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-success mt-3">
                <strong> Next Steps:</strong> Now that you understand display campaign structure:
                <ul class="mb-0 mt-2">
                    <li>🔹 <strong>Topic 10.3:</strong> Remarketing & Audience Strategies</li>
                    <li>🔹 <strong>Topic 10.4:</strong> Display Campaign Optimization Techniques</li>
                    <li>🔹 <strong>Topic 10.5:</strong> Creative Best Practices & A/B Testing</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
