                         <!-- ========== 3 HOW TO CREATE A DISPLAY CAMPAIGN ========== -->
<div class="section" id="topic-3">
    <div class="card mb-4 border">
        <div class="card-header bg-white py-3">
            <h2 class="mb-0">3 How to Create a Display Campaign | Complete Step-by-Step Guide</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            
            <div class="alert alert-light border mb-4">
                <strong> Step‑by‑step walkthrough by Himanshu Shekhar.</strong> Follow this comprehensive guide to set up your first Google Display campaign from scratch – including targeting, bidding, creative assets, and common pitfalls to avoid.
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== INTRODUCTION ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-3"> What is a Display Campaign?</h3>
            <div class="alert alert-info mb-4">
                <p>A <strong>Display Campaign</strong> allows you to advertise in the form of images across websites, apps, and Google-owned properties such as:</p>
                <ul class="mb-0">
                    <li> <strong>YouTube</strong> - Video pre-roll and banner ads</li>
                    <li> <strong>Google Play Store</strong> - App promotion ads</li>
                    <li> <strong>Gmail</strong> - Sponsored ads in Promotions tab</li>
                    <li> <strong>Google Discover</strong> - Feed ads on mobile devices</li>
                    <li> <strong>30-35 million partner websites and applications</strong></li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-secondary mb-4">
                <strong> Example of a Display Advertisement:</strong>
                <p class="mt-2">If you open Google News or any news website, you will notice banner-style advertisements appearing on the page. Those are Display Ads. If you want to advertise in this way, you need to create a Display Campaign in Google Ads.</p>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== WHY USE DISPLAY CAMPAIGNS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Why Do We Use Display Campaigns?</h3>
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h4 class="text-primary">Main Purposes:</h4>
                            <ul>
                                <li> <strong>Sales & Lead Generation</strong> - Drive direct conversions</li>
                                <li> <strong>Brand Awareness</strong> - Build recognition and recall</li>
                                <li> <strong>Consideration Campaigns</strong> - Influence purchase decisions</li>
                                <li> <strong>Remarketing</strong> - Re-engage past website visitors</li>
                                <li> <strong>Audience Research</strong> - Test new market segments</li>
                                <li> <strong>Reach People Beyond Search</strong> - Target users while browsing content</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h4 class="text-success">Major Benefits:</h4>
                            <ul>
                                <li> <strong>Reach Across Multiple Platforms</strong> - Websites, apps, YouTube, Gmail</li>
                                <li> <strong>Reach New Users</strong> - Connect with passive browsers</li>
                                <li> <strong>Gmail Advertising</strong> - Sponsored ads in Promotions tab</li>
                                <li> <strong>Cost-Effective</strong> - Lower CPC than search ads</li>
                                <li> <strong>Visual Storytelling</strong> - Engage with images and videos</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== PRE-LAUNCH CHECKLIST ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Pre‑Launch Checklist (Must Complete Before Starting)</h3>
            
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="form-check mb-2">
                                <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="check1">
                                <label class="form-check-label" for="check1">Conversion tracking installed and recording (if your goal is conversions)</label>
                            </div>
                            <div class="form-check mb-2">
                                <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="check2">
                                <label class="form-check-label" for="check2">Audience lists defined (for remarketing campaigns)</label>
                            </div>
                            <div class="form-check mb-2">
                                <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="check3">
                                <label class="form-check-label" for="check3">Creative assets ready (images, logos, headlines, descriptions)</label>
                            </div>
                            <div class="form-check mb-2">
                                <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="check4">
                                <label class="form-check-label" for="check4">Landing page URL works and is mobile‑friendly</label>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="form-check mb-2">
                                <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="check5">
                                <label class="form-check-label" for="check5">Budget and bid strategy aligned with business goals</label>
                            </div>
                            <div class="form-check mb-2">
                                <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="check6">
                                <label class="form-check-label" for="check6">Target audience defined (demographics, interests)</label>
                            </div>
                            <div class="form-check mb-2">
                                <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="check7">
                                <label class="form-check-label" for="check7">UTM tracking parameters prepared</label>
                            </div>
                            <div class="form-check mb-2">
                                <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" id="check8">
                                <label class="form-check-label" for="check8">Competitor research completed for placements</label>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== STEP 1: CREATE CAMPAIGN ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 1: Create a New Campaign</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-8">
                            <ol class="mb-0">
                                <li><strong>Log into Google Ads</strong> - Go to ads.google.com</li>
                                <li><strong>Click the colorful "+ New Campaign" button</strong> (blue circle with plus icon)</li>
                                <li><strong>Select Campaign Goal:</strong>
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>Sales, Leads, Website traffic, Brand awareness and reach</li>
                                        <li>Or choose <strong>"Create a campaign without a goal's guidance"</strong> (gives you full control over all settings)</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </li>
                                <li><strong>Select "Display" as campaign type</strong></li>
                                <li><strong>Choose "Standard display campaign"</strong> (full control) or "Smart display campaign" (automated targeting & bidding)</li>
                                <li><strong>Click "Continue"</strong> to proceed</li>
                            </ol>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <div class="alert alert-primary text-center">
                                <strong> Himanshu's Tip:</strong>
                                <p class="mb-0 mt-2">I recommend selecting "Create a campaign without goal guidance" because Display Campaigns can also appear inside Sales Campaigns. If you choose Sales Campaign, you will find Display Campaign option below, but there are limitations in options there.</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== STEP 2: BASIC SETTINGS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 2: Basic Campaign Settings</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <ol>
                        <li><strong>Enter your website URL</strong> - The domain you want to promote</li>
                        <li><strong>Give your campaign a name</strong> - Use descriptive naming (e.g., "Display Demo - Himanshu - March 2025")</li>
                        <li><strong>Location Targeting</strong> - Choose where your ads will appear:
                            <ul>
                                <li> Countries (e.g., India, USA, UK)</li>
                                <li> States (e.g., Maharashtra, California)</li>
                                <li> Cities (e.g., Mumbai, Delhi, Bangalore)</li>
                                <li> PIN codes (e.g., 400001, 110001)</li>
                                <li> Specific radius areas (e.g., 10km around your store)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li><strong>Location Options (Critical Setting!)</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Presence:</strong> Ads shown to people currently IN your targeted location → <span class="badge bg-success">Recommended for most campaigns</span></li>
                                <li><strong>Interest:</strong> Ads shown to people interested in that location (e.g., someone in Mumbai searching for "flats in Gujarat" sees Gujarat property ads)</li>
                                <li><strong>Presence or interest:</strong> Shows to both groups</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li><strong>Language Targeting</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li>If advertising in countries like Russia or Italy, target local languages</li>
                                <li><strong>Best recommendation:</strong> Keep "All Languages" selected unless you have specific language requirements</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== STEP 3: MORE SETTINGS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 3: More Settings (Important Options)</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Setting</th>
                            <th>What It Does</th>
                            <th>Recommended Setting</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Ad Rotation</strong></td>
                            <td>Controls how often different ads are shown</td>
                            <td>"Optimize" (Google shows best-performing ads)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Ad Schedule</strong></td>
                            <td>Set specific days/times for ads to run</td>
                            <td>Schedule during business hours or peak conversion times</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Device Targeting</strong></td>
                            <td>Choose which devices see your ads</td>
                            <td>Target Computers, Mobile, Tablets based on your audience</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Operating Systems</strong></td>
                            <td>Target specific OS (Windows, iOS, Android)</td>
                            <td>Use for app promotions or platform-specific offers</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Device Models</strong></td>
                            <td>Target specific phone/tablet models</td>
                            <td>Example: Target only Samsung Galaxy users</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Mobile Networks</strong></td>
                            <td>Target users by telecom provider</td>
                            <td>Use for carrier-specific promotions (Airtel, Jio, Vodafone)</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-info mb-4">
                <strong> Himanshu's Pro Tip:</strong> You can target very specifically - for example, target only ASUS devices or only iPhone users. This helps avoid wasting budget on irrelevant device types.
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== STEP 4: NETWORK & CONTENT EXCLUSIONS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 4: Network Targeting & Content Exclusions</h3>
            
            <div class="row mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white"> Network Targeting</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Target users based on the telecom/network provider they use.</p>
                            <strong>Options include:</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li> All networks</li>
                                <li> Specific mobile carriers (Airtel, Jio, Vi, BSNL)</li>
                                <li> WiFi networks</li>
                                <li> Broadband providers</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2">
                                Useful for carrier-specific promotions or regional targeting.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-danger text-white"> Content Exclusions (Brand Safety)</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Prevent ads from appearing on certain types of content:</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li> Sensitive social issues</li>
                                <li> Mature audiences (sexual content, violence)</li>
                                <li> Tragedy & conflict</li>
                                <li> Parked domains</li>
                                <li> Error pages (404, redirects)</li>
                                <li> Embedded videos</li>
                                <li> Below-the-fold placements</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-warning small mt-2">
                                <strong> Himanshu's Note:</strong> I don't recommend using many exclusions for branding campaigns because Display Campaigns are mainly used for brand awareness, not lead generation. Too many exclusions limit reach.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== STEP 5: ABOVE THE FOLD VS BELOW THE FOLD ==================== -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-3">📄 Understanding Above the Fold vs Below the Fold</h4>
            
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="text-center p-3 border rounded bg-white">
                                <span class="display-4"></span>
                                <h4 class="text-success">Above the Fold</h4>
                                <p>The visible top portion of a webpage that users see immediately without scrolling.</p>
                                <span class="badge bg-success">Higher visibility, Higher cost</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="text-center p-3 border rounded bg-white">
                                <span class="display-4"></span>
                                <h4 class="text-warning">Below the Fold</h4>
                                <p>The part users see after scrolling down the page.</p>
                                <span class="badge bg-warning">Lower visibility, Lower cost</span>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                        <strong> Tip:</strong> If you exclude below-the-fold placements, your ads will only appear in visible top areas. This is great for awareness campaigns!
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== STEP 6: BUDGET & BIDDING ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 5: Budget & Bidding Strategy</h3>
            
            <div class="row mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-12">
                    <div class="card">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h4> Budget Settings:</h4>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Daily Budget:</strong> Set how much you want to spend per day (e.g., ₹100, ₹500, ₹1000)</li>
                                <li><strong>Campaign Budget Optimization (CBO):</strong> Distribute budget across ad groups automatically</li>
                            </ul>
                            
                            <h4 class="mt-3"> Bidding Strategies Explained:</h4>
                            <div class="table-responsive">
                                <table class="table table-bordered">
                                    <thead class="table-dark">
                                        <tr>
                                            <th>Strategy</th>
                                            <th>What It Does</th>
                                            <th>Best For</th>
                                            <th>When to Use</th>
                                        </tr>
                                    </thead>
                                    <tbody>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td><strong>Conversions</strong></td>
                                            <td>Google maximizes conversion actions</td>
                                            <td>Lead generation, sales</td>
                                            <td>After conversion tracking setup</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td><strong>Conversion Value</strong></td>
                                            <td>Maximizes total conversion value (ROAS)</td>
                                            <td>E-commerce, high-value sales</td>
                                            <td>When conversion values are tracked</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td><strong>vCPM (Viewable CPM)</strong></td>
                                            <td>Pay per 1,000 viewable impressions</td>
                                            <td>Brand awareness</td>
                                            <td>Budget: ₹60-100 CPM initially</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td><strong>Maximize Clicks</strong></td>
                                            <td>Gets most clicks within budget</td>
                                            <td>Website traffic, testing</td>
                                            <td>When starting new campaigns</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td><strong>Manual CPC</strong></td>
                                            <td>Full control over click costs</td>
                                            <td>Experienced advertisers</td>
                                            <td>When you have historical data</td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </tbody>
                                </table>
                            </div>
                            
                            <div class="alert alert-primary mt-3">
                                <strong> Himanshu's CPM Explanation:</strong> Display Campaigns commonly use CPM (Cost Per Thousand Impressions). You pay when your ad is shown to 1,000 people. For example, if your ad gets 1,000 impressions, Google charges you based on your CPM bid.
                            </div>
                            
                            <div class="alert alert-info mt-2">
                                <strong> Understanding Conversion:</strong> Conversion does not always mean sales. A conversion can be:
                                <ul class="mb-0 mt-2">
                                    <li>✓ A click on your ad</li>
                                    <li>✓ A lead form submission</li>
                                    <li>✓ A phone call</li>
                                    <li>✓ Website traffic</li>
                                    <li>✓ A purchase</li>
                                </ul>
                                Basically, whatever objective your ad is trying to achieve is considered a conversion.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== STEP 7: AUDIENCE TARGETING ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 6: Audience Targeting (Critical for Success)</h3>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white"> Demographics</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Target based on user characteristics:</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li> <strong>Age:</strong> 18-24, 25-34, 35-44, 45-54, 55-65, 65+</li>
                                <li>👫 <strong>Gender:</strong> Male, Female, Unknown</li>
                                <li>👪 <strong>Parental Status:</strong> Parent, Not a parent</li>
                                <li> <strong>Household Income:</strong> Top 10%, 11-20%, 21-30%, etc.</li>
                                <li> <strong>Education:</strong> In college, College graduate, etc.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2">
                                <strong>Example:</strong> For nail polish → Target female audiences only.<br>
                                For diaper brand → Target young parents, ages 25-44, both genders.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">❤ Affinity Audiences</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Interest-based targeting for people with long-term passions.</p>
                            <strong>Examples:</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li> Fitness Buffs</li>
                                <li> Foodies & Home Chefs</li>
                                <li> Tech Enthusiasts</li>
                                <li> Frequent Travelers</li>
                                <li> Gamers</li>
                            </ul>
                            <span class="badge bg-secondary">Best for: Top-of-funnel awareness</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark"> In-Market Audiences</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>People actively researching or planning to buy.</p>
                            <strong>Examples:</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li> Running Shoes</li>
                                <li> Laptops & Computers</li>
                                <li> New Vehicles</li>
                                <li> Real Estate</li>
                                <li> Credit Cards</li>
                            </ul>
                            <span class="badge bg-secondary">Best for: Bottom-of-funnel conversions</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== STEP 8: KEYWORD & CONTENT TARGETING ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 7: Keyword & Content Targeting</h3>
            
            <div class="alert alert-info mb-4">
                <strong> Important Note:</strong> In Display Ads, keywords do NOT trigger searches. Instead, they determine the types of web pages where ads appear. Google shows your ads on pages containing those topics.
            </div>
            
            <div class="row mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">🔍 Keyword Targeting</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Target pages containing specific keywords:</p>
                            <strong>Example Keywords:</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Makeup, Beauty, Fashion</li>
                                <li>Female, Women, Style</li>
                                <li>Travel, Vacation, Holiday</li>
                                <li>Fitness, Gym, Workout</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2">
                                Your ads appear on pages containing these topics. Useful for highly targeted campaigns.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white"> Topic Targeting</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Select broad content categories:</p>
                            <strong>Examples:</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li> Auto & Vehicles</li>
                                <li> Bikes & Accessories</li>
                                <li>🚚 Commercial Vehicles</li>
                                <li> Real Estate</li>
                                <li> Business Services</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2">
                                Google shows ads only on websites related to those topics.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== STEP 9: PLACEMENT TARGETING (POWERFUL STRATEGY) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 8: Placement Targeting (Competitor Strategy)</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p><strong>What is Placement Targeting?</strong> You can specifically target:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li> <strong>YouTube channels</strong> - Your own channel or competitor channels</li>
                        <li> <strong>Specific websites</strong> - e.g., Gadget360, GadgetsToUse, TechCrunch</li>
                        <li> <strong>Mobile applications</strong> - Specific apps where your audience spends time</li>
                        <li> <strong>Specific YouTube videos</strong> - Target individual popular videos</li>
                    </ul>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-success mt-3">
                        <strong> Himanshu's Best Strategy:</strong> This is one of the best strategies for competitor targeting! For example, if you target the T-Series YouTube channel, your ads can appear on T-Series videos. This puts your brand directly in front of your competitor's audience.
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="row mt-3">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="alert alert-info">
                                <strong> Example Placement Targets:</strong>
                                <ul class="mb-0">
                                    <li>Competitor YouTube channels</li>
                                    <li>Industry news websites</li>
                                    <li>Review sites in your niche</li>
                                    <li>Popular blogs in your industry</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="alert alert-warning">
                                <strong> Himanshu's Note:</strong> Placement targeting is extremely powerful for targeted marketing. You can show ads only on websites you trust and want to be associated with.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

           <!-- ==================== STEP 10: AD CREATION ==================== -->
<h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 9: Ad Creation - Responsive Display Ads</h3>

<div class="card mb-4">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h4> What You Need to Upload:</h4>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Final URL</strong> - Landing page (e.g., himanshu.com/digital-marketing-course)</li>
            <li><strong>Business Name</strong> - Your brand name (max 25 chars)</li>
            <li><strong>Images</strong> - Up to 15 images (landscape 1.91:1, square 1:1, 16:9 optional)</li>
            <li><strong>Logo</strong> - Square (1:1) with transparent background (min 128x128)</li>
            <li><strong>Videos</strong> - Optional, up to ~30 seconds (YouTube videos supported)</li>
            <li><strong>Headlines</strong> - Short (30 chars) and long (90 chars)</li>
            <li><strong>Descriptions</strong> - 90 characters each</li>
        </ul>
        
        <h4 class="mt-3"> Image Sources:</h4>
        <ul>
            <li> Upload your own images</li>
            <li> Use landing page images (Google extracts automatically)</li>
            <li> Use free stock images (Unsplash, Pexels)</li>
            <li> Professional photography</li>
        </ul>
        
        <div class="alert alert-primary mt-3">
            <strong> Himanshu's Pro Tip:</strong> Google automatically creates different ad sizes and layouts from your uploaded assets. The more assets you provide, the more combinations Google can test!
        </div>
        
        <h4 class="mt-3"> Complete Image Size Requirements:</h4>
        <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                <thead class="table-dark">
                    <tr>
                        <th>Format</th>
                        <th>Aspect Ratio</th>
                        <th>Recommended Size</th>
                        <th>Minimum Size</th>
                        <th>Maximum Size</th>
                        <th>Use Case</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Landscape (Recommended)</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>1.91:1</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>1200 x 628</strong></td>
                        <td>600 x 314</td>
                        <td>5000 x 5000</td>
                        <td>Most placements, YouTube banners, standard display</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Square (Recommended)</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>1:1</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>1200 x 1200</strong></td>
                        <td>300 x 300</td>
                        <td>5000 x 5000</td>
                        <td>Social feeds, mobile placements, Gmail ads</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="table-info">
                        <td><strong>16:9 (Widescreen)</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>16:9</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>1280 x 720</strong> or <strong>1920 x 1080</strong></td>
                        <td>640 x 360</td>
                        <td>3840 x 2160 (4K)</td>
                        <td>YouTube video thumbnails, video companion banners, TV screens, hero images</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>Portrait (Optional)</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>4:5</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>960 x 1200</strong></td>
                        <td>320 x 400</td>
                        <td>5000 x 5000</td>
                        <td>Mobile stories, vertical placements, Instagram-like formats</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="table-secondary">
                        <td><strong>Leaderboard</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>728 x 90</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>728 x 90</strong></td>
                        <td>728 x 90 (fixed)</td>
                        <td>728 x 90 (fixed)</td>
                        <td>Top of websites, header placements</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr class="table-secondary">
                        <td><strong>Skyscraper</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>160 x 600</strong></td>
                        <td><strong>160 x 600</strong></td>
                        <td>160 x 600 (fixed)</td>
                        <td>160 x 600 (fixed)</td>
                        <td>Sidebar placements, right column</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>

        <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
            <strong> Understanding 16:9 Aspect Ratio:</strong>
            <ul class="mb-0">
                <li><strong>Common Sizes:</strong> 1280x720 (HD), 1920x1080 (Full HD), 2560x1440 (2K), 3840x2160 (4K)</li>
                <li><strong>Best For:</strong> YouTube video thumbnails, video companion banners, hero images, TV screens, desktop wallpapers</li>
                <li><strong>When to Use:</strong> Use 16:9 images when you have high-quality widescreen photos or when your brand imagery works better in widescreen format</li>
                <li><strong>Recommendation:</strong> Upload 1.91:1 landscape images (1200x628) as your primary format, as they fit in more placements and are more versatile</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="alert alert-secondary mt-2">
            <strong> Aspect Ratio Comparison:</strong>
            <div class="row mt-2">
                <div class="col-md-3 text-center">
                    <div style="width:100%; background:#e0e0e0; padding:20px; border-radius:5px;">
                        1.91:1 (Landscape)<br>
                        <small>Most versatile</small>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-3 text-center">
                    <div style="width:100%; background:#d0d0d0; padding:20px; border-radius:5px;">
                        1:1 (Square)<br>
                        <small>Social media</small>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-3 text-center">
                    <div style="width:100%; background:#c8c8c8; padding:20px; border-radius:5px;">
                        16:9 (Widescreen)<br>
                        <small>YouTube/Video</small>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-3 text-center">
                    <div style="width:100%; background:#e8e8e8; padding:20px; border-radius:5px;">
                        4:5 (Portrait)<br>
                        <small>Mobile stories</small>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="alert alert-warning mt-2">
            <strong> Important Tip:</strong> While 16:9 images are supported, <strong>1.91:1 (1200x628)</strong> remains the most versatile aspect ratio because it fits into the highest number of ad placements across the Google Display Network. Always prioritize uploading 1.91:1 and 1:1 images first, then add 16:9 images as supplemental assets.
        </div>
        
        <h4 class="mt-3"> Headline & Description Examples:</h4>
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="card">
                    <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">Short Headlines (30 chars)</div>
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <ul class="small">
                            <li>"Learn Digital Marketing"</li>
                            <li>"Free Consultation"</li>
                            <li>"Enroll Today!"</li>
                            <li>"Limited Offer"</li>
                            <li>"Expert Guidance"</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="card">
                    <div class="card-header bg-info text-white">Long Headlines (90 chars)</div>
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <ul class="small">
                            <li>"Master Digital Marketing in 3 Months"</li>
                            <li>"Join 10,000+ Successful Students"</li>
                            <li>"Get Certified & Start Your Career Today"</li>
