                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        
        <h4 class="mt-3"> Ad Strength Check:</h4>
        <div class="alert alert-success">
            <strong>Your Ad Strength should be "Excellent"!</strong> All indicators should show blue checkmarks. Google will show you which areas need improvement.
            <ul class="mt-2 mb-0">
                <li>✔ At least 3-5 short headlines</li>
                <li>✔ At least 3-5 descriptions</li>
                <li>✔ At least 2 landscape images (1.91:1)</li>
                <li>✔ At least 2 square images (1:1)</li>
                <li>✔ 1 logo (transparent background)</li>
                <li>✔ Business name</li>
                <li>✔ Final URL</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        
        <div class="alert alert-warning mt-2">
            <strong> Himanshu's Note:</strong> If images appear cropped, it usually means the image dimensions are incorrect. Always use the recommended sizes:
            <ul class="mb-0 mt-2">
                <li>✓ Landscape: 1200 x 628 pixels (1.91:1) - <strong>Most Important</strong></li>
                <li>✓ Square: 1200 x 1200 pixels (1:1) - <strong>Very Important</strong></li>
                <li>✓ 16:9: 1920 x 1080 or 1280 x 720 - <strong>Optional but beneficial</strong></li>
                <li>✓ Logo: Square with transparent background</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        
        <div class="alert alert-primary mt-2">
            <strong> Himanshu's Pro Strategy for Creatives:</strong>
            <ul class="mb-0 mt-2">
                <li> <strong>Minimum Upload:</strong> 3 landscape + 3 square images</li>
                <li> <strong>Recommended Upload:</strong> 5 landscape + 5 square + 2-3 16:9 images + 1 video</li>
                <li> <strong>Headlines:</strong> 5 short headlines + 2-3 long headlines</li>
                <li> <strong>Descriptions:</strong> 5 descriptions for maximum testing</li>
                <li> <strong>Refresh:</strong> Update creatives every 4-6 weeks to prevent ad fatigue</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

            <!-- ==================== STEP 11: CTA BUTTONS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 10: Call-To-Action (CTA) Buttons</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>Choose from pre-set CTA options that appear with your banner ad:</p>
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <span class="badge bg-primary p-2 d-block mb-2">Book Now</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <span class="badge bg-success p-2 d-block mb-2">Learn More</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <span class="badge bg-warning p-2 d-block mb-2">Sign Up</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <span class="badge bg-danger p-2 d-block mb-2">Shop Now</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <span class="badge bg-info p-2 d-block mb-2">Get Quote</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <span class="badge bg-secondary p-2 d-block mb-2">Subscribe</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <span class="badge bg-dark p-2 d-block mb-2">Download</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <span class="badge bg-light text-dark p-2 d-block mb-2">Contact Us</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <p class="mt-3">The CTA appears with your banner ad and encourages user action.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== STEP 12: REVIEW & PUBLISH ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 11: Review & Publish Campaign</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p><strong>Before publishing, review all settings:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li> Campaign name and goals</li>
                        <li> Location and language targeting</li>
                        <li> Budget and bidding strategy</li>
                        <li> Audience targeting selections</li>
                        <li> Ad creatives (images, headlines, descriptions)</li>
                        <li> Ad strength (should be "Excellent")</li>
                        <li> Conversion tracking (if applicable)</li>
                        <li> Content exclusions</li>
                    </ul>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-danger mt-3">
                        <strong> Common Errors That Prevent Publishing:</strong>
                        <ul class="mb-0">
                            <li>Missing location targeting</li>
                            <li>Budget issues (budget too low)</li>
                            <li>Bidding setup errors</li>
                            <li>Incomplete ad assets (missing images or headlines)</li>
                            <li>Invalid landing page URL</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-success mt-3">
                        <strong> Himanshu's Tip:</strong> Removing errors is easy. The real challenge is properly understanding and configuring the campaign. Take your time during setup!
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                        <strong> After Publishing:</strong>
                        <ul class="mb-0">
                            <li>Wait 2-3 days before making major changes</li>
                            <li>The display network needs time to learn which placements work best</li>
                            <li>Monitor placement reports weekly</li>
                            <li>Check ad strength and performance metrics</li>
                            <li>Use "Optimization score" recommendations (but evaluate carefully)</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== DISPLAY VS SEARCH DIFFERENCES ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> How Display Campaigns Differ from Search Campaigns</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Aspect</th>
                            <th>Display Campaigns</th>
                            <th>Search Campaigns</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Where ads appear</strong></td>
                            <td>Websites, apps, YouTube, Gmail</td>
                            <td>Google Search results only</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>User intent</strong></td>
                            <td>Passive browsing (creating demand)</td>
                            <td>Active searching (capturing demand)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Targeting method</strong></td>
                            <td>Audiences, topics, placements, keywords</td>
                            <td>Keywords with match types</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Ad formats</strong></td>
                            <td>Images, video, responsive, Gmail</td>
                            <td>Text only (headlines, descriptions)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Bidding</strong></td>
                            <td>CPM, vCPM, Target CPA, Target ROAS</td>
                            <td>CPC, Target CPA, Target ROAS</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Best for</strong></td>
                            <td>Awareness, remarketing, branding</td>
                            <td>Conversions, leads, sales</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            
            <!-- ==================== CREATIVE TIPS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Himanshu's Creative Tips for Display Ads</h3>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body text-center">
                            <span class="display-4"></span>
                            <h4>Use High-Quality Images</h4>
                            <p>Blurry or pixelated images hurt brand perception. Always use high-resolution images (1200x628+).</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body text-center">
                            <span class="display-4"></span>
                            <h4>Clear Value Proposition</h4>
                            <p>Tell users what they'll get. "Learn Digital Marketing" is better than "Click Here".</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body text-center">
                            <span class="display-4"></span>
                            <h4>Strong Call-to-Action</h4>
                            <p>Use action-oriented CTAs like "Enroll Now", "Get Started", "Download Free Guide".</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body text-center">
                            <span class="display-4"></span>
                            <h4>Test Multiple Variations</h4>
                            <p>Create multiple headlines and descriptions. Let Google's AI find the winning combinations.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body text-center">
                            <span class="display-4"></span>
                            <h4>Consistent Branding</h4>
                            <p>Use your brand colors, logo, and fonts consistently across all creatives.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body text-center">
                            <span class="display-4"></span>
                            <h4>Mobile-First Design</h4>
                            <p>60%+ of display impressions happen on mobile. Ensure your ads look great on all devices.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SUMMARY ==================== -->
            <div class="alert alert-success mt-4">
                <h3 class="fw-bold"> Summary: Himanshu Shekhar's Display Campaign Guide</h3>
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <p><strong>When to Use Display Ads:</strong></p>
                        <ul class="small">
                            <li> Brand awareness campaigns</li>
                            <li> Remarketing campaigns</li>
                            <li> Audience research</li>
                            <li> Reaching new audiences</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <p><strong>Key Settings to Master:</strong></p>
                        <ul class="small">
                            <li> Location targeting (Presence vs Interest)</li>
                            <li> Content exclusions (brand safety)</li>
                            <li> vCPM bidding for awareness</li>
                            <li> Placement targeting for competitors</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-4">
                        <p><strong>Creative Requirements:</strong></p>
                        <ul class="small">
                            <li> 5+ headlines, 5+ descriptions</li>
                            <li> 3-5 landscape images (1200x628)</li>
                            <li> 3-5 square images (1200x1200)</li>
                            <li> Logo with transparent background</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-primary mt-3">
                <strong> Key Takeaway:</strong> Display Campaigns are perfect for building brand awareness and reaching new audiences. Unlike Search Campaigns where people are actively searching, Display Campaigns help you create demand for your products and services.
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                <strong> Himanshu Shekhar's Final Word:</strong> If you want to learn Digital Marketing, you can fill out the form link given in the description. Our coordinators will contact you and answer all your queries.
            </div>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
