                         <div class="section" id="topic-4">
    <div class="card mb-4 border">
        <div class="card-header bg-white py-3">
            <h2 class="mb-0">4 Display Ads Keyword Research & Targeting</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">

            <div class="alert alert-light border mb-4">
                <strong>Keywords in display advertising work differently than in search.</strong> Instead of triggering your ads when someone searches, display keywords help Google understand which web pages are relevant to your products or services. This guide covers everything from basic keyword research to advanced targeting strategies for the Google Display Network.
            </div>

            <p>Keyword research for display campaigns is fundamentally different from search campaigns. In search, keywords are user-driven - people type what they want. In display, keywords are content-driven - they describe the types of web pages where you want your ads to appear. This distinction is critical for campaign success.</p>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 1: UNDERSTANDING DISPLAY KEYWORDS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Understanding Display Keywords: A Complete Overview</h3>

            <div class="alert alert-info mb-4">
                <strong>Definition:</strong> Display keywords are phrases that describe the content of websites, articles, and videos where you want your ads to appear. Google analyzes page content and matches it with your keywords to determine ad placement.
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Search Keywords vs Display Keywords</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h5>Search Keywords</h5>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Trigger ads when users search on Google</li>
                                <li>Reflect user intent and demand</li>
                                <li>Directly target what users are looking for</li>
                                <li>High intent, lower volume</li>
                                <li>Example: "buy running shoes online"</li>
                            </ul>
                            <hr>
                            <h5>Display Keywords</h5>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Target pages containing specific topics</li>
                                <li>Reflect content context and user interests</li>
                                <li>Indirectly reach users through content consumption</li>
                                <li>Low intent, high volume</li>
                                <li>Example: "marathon training tips"</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Why Display Keywords Matter</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Contextual Relevance:</strong> Ensures your ads appear on relevant websites</li>
                                <li><strong>Audience Quality:</strong> Reaches users interested in related topics</li>
                                <li><strong>Brand Safety:</strong> Helps avoid inappropriate content placements</li>
                                <li><strong>Cost Efficiency:</strong> Reduces wasted spend on irrelevant traffic</li>
                                <li><strong>Performance Improvement:</strong> Higher CTR through better targeting</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-3 mb-0">
                                <strong>Key Insight:</strong> Display keywords help you reach users who are "in the mindset" of your product category, even if they're not actively searching for it.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 2: HOW DISPLAY KEYWORDS WORK ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">How Display Keywords Actually Work</h3>

            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded mb-0"><code class="language-bash">
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    DISPLAY KEYWORD MATCHING PROCESS                     │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                         │
│  1. Google crawls a webpage                                             │
│         ↓                                                               │
│  2. Analyzes content: title, body text, headings, meta tags             │
│         ↓                                                               │
│  3. Identifies main topics and themes                                   │
│         ↓                                                               │
│  4. Checks your display campaign keywords                               │
│         ↓                                                               │
│  5. If keywords match the page content → your ad is eligible            │
│         ↓                                                               │
│  6. Auction determines if your ad is shown                              │
│                                                                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                    </code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Content Analysis</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Google uses advanced natural language processing to analyze:</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Page title and headings</li>
                                <li>Body text and article content</li>
                                <li>Meta descriptions and tags</li>
                                <li>Image alt text and captions</li>
                                <li>URL structure and domain authority</li>
                                <li>User engagement signals</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Matching Types</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Display keywords use context matching:</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Exact Match:</strong> Page contains exact phrase</li>
                                <li><strong>Phrase Match:</strong> Page contains similar phrase</li>
                                <li><strong>Broad Match:</strong> Page contains related concepts</li>
                                <li><strong>Automatic Matching:</strong> Google finds related content</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                <strong>Important:</strong> Display keywords work differently than search match types. They focus on content relevance rather than specific search queries.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Placement Examples</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Keyword: "Digital Marketing Course"</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Blog post: "10 Digital Marketing Skills You Need"</li>
                                <li>Article: "How to Start a Career in Marketing"</li>
                                <li>Video: "Digital Marketing Tutorial for Beginners"</li>
                                <li>Website: "Best Online Marketing Courses"</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                <strong>Reach:</strong> Your ads appear on any page discussing digital marketing topics.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 3: KEYWORD RESEARCH METHODOLOGY ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Display Keyword Research Methodology</h3>

            <div class="alert alert-info mb-4">
                <strong>Strategic Approach:</strong> Effective display keyword research requires thinking about what content your target audience consumes, not just what they search for.
            </div>

            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Step 1: Understand Your Target Audience</h4>
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h5>Audience Persona Development</h5>
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Persona Element</th>
                                    <th>Questions to Ask</th>
                                    <th>Keywords to Consider</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Demographics</strong></td>
                                    <td>Age, location, income, education?</td>
                                    <td>Location-based, lifestyle keywords</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Interests</strong></td>
                                    <td>Hobbies, passions, activities?</td>
                                    <td>Affinity-based keywords</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Pain Points</strong></td>
                                    <td>Problems they're trying to solve?</td>
                                    <td>Problem-focused keywords</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Content Consumption</strong></td>
                                    <td>What blogs, videos, sites do they visit?</td>
                                    <td>Topic and placement keywords</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <div class="alert alert-success mt-3 mb-0">
                        <strong>Example:</strong> For a luxury watch brand, target keywords like "luxury lifestyle," "mens fashion," "watch collectors," and "high-end accessories" to reach premium content consumers.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Step 2: Generate Keyword Ideas</h4>
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                            <h5 class="mb-0">Brainstorming Techniques</h5>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul>
                                <li>List product features and benefits</li>
                                <li>Identify related categories and topics</li>
                                <li>Consider synonyms and variations</li>
                                <li>Think about audience interests</li>
                                <li>Review website content topics</li>
                                <li>Analyze competitor content themes</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                            <h5 class="mb-0">Keyword Categories</h5>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Product Keywords:</strong> What you sell</li>
                                <li><strong>Category Keywords:</strong> Industry topics</li>
                                <li><strong>Interest Keywords:</strong> Hobbies and passions</li>
                                <li><strong>Life Event Keywords:</strong> Major life changes</li>
                                <li><strong>Problem Keywords:</strong> Pain points and challenges</li>
                                <li><strong>Educational Keywords:</strong> Learning and research</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
                            <h5 class="mb-0">Example Keyword Lists</h5>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>For an Online Course Platform:</strong></p>
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li>Learn digital marketing</li>
                                <li>Online education courses</li>
                                <li>Career advancement skills</li>
                                <li>Professional development</li>
                                <li>Remote learning resources</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 4: TOOLS FOR DISPLAY KEYWORD RESEARCH ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Tools for Display Keyword Research</h3>

            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Tool</th>
                            <th>Purpose</th>
                            <th>Best For</th>
                            <th>Cost</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Google Keyword Planner</strong></td>
                            <td>Search volume, competition, keyword ideas</td>
                            <td>Initial research and baseline data</td>
                            <td>Free with Google Ads account</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Google Ads Display Planner</strong></td>
                            <td>Display-specific keyword suggestions</td>
                            <td>Targeted display keyword generation</td>
                            <td>Free</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>SEMrush</strong></td>
                            <td>Competitor analysis, keyword research</td>
                            <td>Competitive intelligence</td>
                            <td>Paid</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Ahrefs</strong></td>
                            <td>Content analysis, keyword difficulty</td>
                            <td>Content-oriented keyword research</td>
                            <td>Paid</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>AnswerThePublic</strong></td>
                            <td>Question-based keyword ideas</td>
                            <td>Audience intent discovery</td>
                            <td>Free/Paid</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Google Trends</strong></td>
                            <td>Seasonal and trend analysis</td>
                            <td>Timing and seasonality</td>
                            <td>Free</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 5: ADVANCED KEYWORD TARGETING STRATEGIES ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Advanced Keyword Targeting Strategies</h3>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Competitor Keyword Strategy</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h5>How to Find Competitor Keywords</h5>
                            <ol>
                                <li>Identify top 3-5 competitors</li>
                                <li>Visit their websites and analyze content</li>
                                <li>Use SEMrush or Ahrefs to see their display keywords</li>
                                <li>Identify content categories they target</li>
                                <li>Find gaps and opportunities they're missing</li>
                            </ol>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-3 mb-0">
                                <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Target competitor keywords while adding your unique value proposition to attract their audience.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Long-Tail Keyword Strategy</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h5>Benefits of Long-Tail Keywords</h5>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Lower competition and cost</li>
                                <li>Higher relevance and engagement</li>
                                <li>Better targeting precision</li>
                                <li>Improved conversion rates</li>
                                <li>Reduced wasted impressions</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-3 mb-0">
                                <strong>Example:</strong> "Best organic coffee beans for espresso" targets specific content and high-intent audience.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Seasonal and Trending Keywords</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h5>Seasonal Opportunity Examples</h5>
                            <div class="table-responsive">
                                <table class="table table-sm">
                                    <thead class="table-light">
                                        <tr>
                                            <th>Season</th>
                                            <th>Keyword Ideas</th>
                                            <th>Industries</th>
                                        </tr>
                                    </thead>
                                    <tbody>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Holiday</td>
                                            <td>Gift ideas, holiday shopping</td>
                                            <td>Retail, e-commerce</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Summer</td>
                                            <td>Vacation planning, summer style</td>
                                            <td>Travel, fashion</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Back to School</td>
                                            <td>School supplies, education tips</td>
                                            <td>Education, retail</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>New Year</td>
                                            <td>New year resolutions, goal setting</td>
                                            <td>Fitness, personal development</td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </tbody>
                                </table>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-danger text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Topic vs Keyword Targeting</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h5>Understanding the Difference</h5>
                            <div class="table-responsive">
                                <table class="table table-sm">
                                    <thead class="table-light">
                                        <tr>
                                            <th>Aspect</th>
                                            <th>Topic Targeting</th>
                                            <th>Keyword Targeting</th>
                                        </tr>
                                    </thead>
                                    <tbody>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Reach</td>
                                            <td>Broader</td>
                                            <td>Narrower</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Relevance</td>
                                            <td>High-level</td>
                                            <td>Specific</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Precision</td>
                                            <td>Medium</td>
                                            <td>High</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Cost</td>
                                            <td>Lower</td>
                                            <td>Higher</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Best Use</td>
                                            <td>Awareness campaigns</td>
                                            <td>Consideration campaigns</td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </tbody>
                                </table>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== SECTION 6: KEYWORD GROUPING AND ORGANIZATION ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Keyword Grouping and Organization</h3>
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h4 class="fw-semibold">Ad Group Organization Strategy</h4>
                    <p>Proper keyword organization improves campaign performance and makes optimization easier. Group keywords by themes and intent.</p>
                    <div class="row g-4 mt-3">
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <div class="card h-100">
                                <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                                    <h5 class="mb-0">Product-Focused Groups</h5>
                                </div>
                                <div class="card-body small">
                                    <p><strong>Keywords:</strong> Specific product names and features</p>
                                    <p><strong>Example:</strong> "running shoes," "sports footwear," "athletic sneakers"</p>
                                    <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                        Best For: Product-specific campaigns
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <div class="card h-100">
                                <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                                    <h5 class="mb-0">Benefit-Focused Groups</h5>
                                </div>
                                <div class="card-body small">
                                    <p><strong>Keywords:</strong> Problems solved, value delivered</p>
                                    <p><strong>Example:</strong> "improve fitness," "run faster," "avoid injuries"</p>
                                    <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                        Best For: Consideration campaigns
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <div class="card h-100">
                                <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
                                    <h5 class="mb-0">Audience-Focused Groups</h5>
                                </div>
                                <div class="card-body small">
                                    <p><strong>Keywords:</strong> User demographics and interests</p>
                                    <p><strong>Example:</strong> "marathon training," "beginner running," "women's fitness"</p>
                                    <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                        Best For: Audience targeting campaigns
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== SECTION 7: ADDING KEYWORDS TO DISPLAY CAMPAIGNS - STEP BY STEP ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Step-by-Step: How to Add Keywords to a Display Campaign</h3>
            <div class="alert alert-info mb-4">
                <strong>Complete Walkthrough:</strong> Adding keywords to display campaigns is straightforward, but understanding the interface options is essential. This step-by-step guide shows you exactly how to add keywords at campaign and ad group levels, with screenshots and practical examples.
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== STEP 1: NAVIGATE TO YOUR DISPLAY CAMPAIGN ==================== -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Step 1: Navigate to Your Display Campaign</h4>
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-12">
                    <div class="card">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                            <h5 class="mb-0">Accessing Your Campaign</h5>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ol>
                                <li><strong>Log into Google Ads</strong> at ads.google.com</li>
                                <li>Click on <strong>"Campaigns"</strong> in the left navigation menu</li>
                                <li>Find and click on your <strong>Display Campaign</strong> (e.g., "Cloud-Computing-Display-Ads")</li>
                            </ol>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-3 mb-0">
                                <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Keywords can be added at both the <strong>Campaign level</strong> (applies to all ad groups) and the <strong>Ad Group level</strong> (applies to specific themes). Choose your level based on how granular you want your targeting to be.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== STEP 1A: ADD KEYWORDS AT CAMPAIGN LEVEL ==================== -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Step 1A: Adding Keywords at the Campaign Level</h4>
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header bg-secondary text-white">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Campaign-Level Content Targeting (Settings)</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <p><strong>When to use Campaign Level:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>When all ad groups share the same core theme.</li>
                                <li>When you want to apply broad targeting rules (or negative keywords) across the entire campaign.</li>
                                <li>Simplifies management if you don't need ad-group-level granularity.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p><strong>How to access Campaign Settings:</strong></p>
                            <ol>
                                <li>From the <strong>Campaigns</strong> overview, click on your campaign name.</li>
                                <li>Click on <strong>"Settings"</strong> in the left navigation menu.</li>
                                <li>Scroll down to the <strong>"Content targeting"</strong> section.</li>
                                <li>Click the <strong>"Edit settings" icon</strong> (pencil icon) next to "Content targeting".</li>
                                <li>A panel will open on the right. Click on <strong>"Keywords"</strong> to enter your campaign-level keywords.</li>
                            </ol>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="alert alert-light border small h-100">
                                <strong>Campaign Settings Panel Example:</strong>
                                <p>When you click "Edit settings" in the Settings tab, the right-side panel displays targeting options:</p>
                                <ul class="mb-0">
                                    <li><strong>Audience Segments:</strong> Add/remove audiences</li>
                                    <li><strong>Demographics:</strong> Gender, Age, Household</li>
                                    <li><strong>Keywords:</strong> Enter campaign-level content keywords here</li>
                                    <li><strong>Topics:</strong> Add topic targets</li>
                                    <li><strong>Placements:</strong> Add specific URLs</li>
                                </ul>
                                <hr>
                                <p class="mb-0"><strong>Note:</strong> Keywords added here will apply to <em>every</em> ad group within this campaign. If an ad group also has its own keywords, Google will use the combined targeting (Intersection).</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== STEP 1B: ADD KEYWORDS AT AD GROUP LEVEL ==================== -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Step 1B: Adding Keywords at the Ad Group Level</h4>
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Ad-Group-Level Content Targeting</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <p><strong>When to use Ad Group Level:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>When you have different themes within the same campaign (e.g., "AWS Cloud Practitioner" vs "AWS Associate Architect").</li>
                                <li>When you want specific keywords to trigger specific ad creatives.</li>
                                <li><strong>Most common practice</strong> for granular control and optimization.</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p><strong>How to access Ad Group Settings:</strong></p>
                            <ol>
                                <li>From the Campaign view, click on <strong>"Ad groups"</strong> in the left menu.</li>
                                <li>Select the ad group where you want to add keywords (e.g., "AWS - Associate - Architect").</li>
                                <li>Click on the <strong>"Edit settings" icon</strong> (pencil/settings icon next to the ad group name).</li>
                                <li>In the settings panel, navigate to <strong>"Content targeting"</strong> and click <strong>"Keywords"</strong>.</li>
                            </ol>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <p><strong>How to access via Ad Group Dashboard:</strong></p>
                            <ol>
                                <li>Click on your Ad Group name.</li>
                                <li>Click on <strong>"Audiences, keywords, and content"</strong> in the left sub-menu.</li>
                                <li>Select the <strong>"Keywords"</strong> tab.</li>
                                <li>Click the <strong>"+"</strong> (blue plus) button to add keywords to this specific ad group.</li>
                            </ol>
                            <div class="alert alert-warning small mt-3 mb-0">
                                <strong>Important Targeting Rule:</strong> If you add keywords at BOTH the Campaign level and the Ad Group level, Google Ads will use AND logic. The page content must match the Campaign keyword AND the Ad Group keyword for your ad to show.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== STEP 2: ACCESS KEYWORD TARGETING (Updated Summary) ==================== -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Step 2: Access Keyword Targeting Interface</h4>
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Summary of Navigation Paths</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Level</th>
                                    <th>Navigation Path</th>
                                    <th>Scope of Impact</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Campaign Level</strong></td>
                                    <td>Campaigns → Click Campaign → Settings → Content Targeting → Edit Settings → Keywords</td>
                                    <td>Applies to ALL ad groups in the campaign</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Ad Group Level (Settings Panel)</strong></td>
                                    <td>Ad Groups → Hover Ad Group → Edit Settings Icon → Content Targeting → Keywords</td>
                                    <td>Applies to ONE specific ad group</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Ad Group Level (Keywords Tab)</strong></td>
                                    <td>Ad Groups → Click Ad Group → Audiences, keywords, and content → Keywords → "+"</td>
                                    <td>Applies to ONE specific ad group</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <div class="alert alert-info small mt-3 mb-0">
                        <strong>Best Practice:</strong> If you are just starting out, it is highly recommended to add keywords at the <strong>Ad Group Level</strong>. This allows you to write specific ads that closely match the keyword theme, resulting in higher engagement.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== STEP 3: ADD KEYWORDS ==================== -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Step 3: Add Your Keywords</h4>
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Entering and Selecting Keywords</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-12">
                            <p><strong>Keyword Input Methods:</strong></p>
                            <div class="table-responsive">
                                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                                    <thead class="table-dark">
                                        <tr>
                                            <th>Method</th>
                                            <th>Description</th>
                                            <th>When to Use</th>
                                        </tr>
                                    </thead>
                                    <tbody>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td><strong>Type Keywords Manually</strong></td>
                                            <td>Enter keywords one by one or in a list</td>
                                            <td>When you have a prepared keyword list</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td><strong>Use Keyword Ideas</strong></td>
                                            <td>Google suggests keywords based on your landing page</td>
                                            <td>When starting a new campaign without existing keywords</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td><strong>Upload from File</strong></td>
                                            <td>Import keywords from CSV or Excel</td>
                                            <td>When adding bulk keywords from external research</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td><strong>Copy and Paste</strong></td>
                                            <td>Paste a list of keywords from another source</td>
                                            <td>Quick addition of multiple keywords</td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </tbody>
                                </table>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="row g-4 mt-3">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="card h-100">
                                <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                                    <h6 class="mb-0">Manual Entry Example</h6>
                                </div>
                                <div class="card-body small">
                                    <p><strong>Enter keywords in the text box:</strong></p>
                                    <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code class="language-bash">
            running shoes
            best running shoes
            marathon training
            running techniques
            athletic footwear
            running shoe reviews
            buy running shoes online
                                    </code></pre>
                                    <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                        <strong>Tip:</strong> Press Enter after each keyword. Use one keyword per line.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="card h-100">
                                <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                                    <h6 class="mb-0">Selecting Match Types</h6>
                                </div>
                                <div class="card-body small">
                                    <p><strong>Choose match type for each keyword:</strong></p>
                                    <ul>
                                        <li><strong>Broad Match:</strong> [no symbol] - widest reach</li>
                                        <li><strong>Phrase Match:</strong> "keyword" - moderate reach</li>
                                        <li><strong>Exact Match:</strong> [keyword] - most targeted</li>
                                    </ul>
                                    <div class="table-responsive mt-2">
                                        <table class="table table-sm">
                                            <thead class="table-light">
                                                <tr>
                                                    <th>Match Type</th>
                                                    <th>Example Entry</th>
                                                    <th>Reach</th>
                                                </tr>
                                            </thead>
                                            <tbody>
                                                <tr>
                                                    <td>Broad</td>
                                                    <td>running shoes</td>
                                                    <td>Widest</td>
                                                </tr>
                                                <tr>
                                                    <td>Phrase</td>
                                                    <td>"running shoes"</td>
                                                    <td>Moderate</td>
                                                </tr>
                                                <tr>
                                                    <td>Exact</td>
                                                    <td>[running shoes]</td>
                                                    <td>Most targeted</td>
                                                </tr>
                                            </tbody>
                                        </table>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== STEP 4: USE KEYWORD IDEAS ==================== -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Step 4: Using Keyword Ideas (Google Suggestion Tool)</h4>
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header bg-info text-white">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Leveraging Google's Keyword Suggestions</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h6>How to Access Keyword Ideas</h6>
                            <ol>
                                <li>In the "Add keywords" interface, click <strong>"Get keyword ideas"</strong></li>
                                <li>Enter your <strong>website URL</strong> (Google analyzes your site)</li>
                                <li>Or enter a <strong>seed keyword</strong> related to your business</li>
                                <li>Google generates relevant keyword suggestions</li>
                                <li>Review the list and select relevant keywords</li>
                            </ol>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="alert alert-light border small">
                                <strong>Example: Keyword Ideas for a Running Shoe Store</strong>
                                <ul class="mb-0 mt-2">
                                    <li>best running shoes 2025</li>
                                    <li>running shoes for flat feet</li>
                                    <li>marathon training shoes</li>
                                    <li>trail running shoes</li>
                                    <li>running shoe reviews</li>
                                    <li>lightweight running shoes</li>
                                    <li>running shoe comparison</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                            <div class="alert alert-warning small mt-2 mb-0">
                                <strong>Caution:</strong> Review all suggestions before adding. Not all may be relevant to your campaign.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== STEP 5: SET BIDS FOR KEYWORDS ==================== -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Step 5: Set Bids for Display Keywords</h4>
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header bg-danger text-white">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Keyword Bidding Configuration</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-12">
                            <h6>Understanding Display Keyword Bidding</h6>
                            <p>Display keywords use the same bidding as your ad group. You can set specific bids at the keyword level for more control.</p>
            
                            <div class="table-responsive">
                                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                                    <thead class="table-dark">
                                        <tr>
                                            <th>Bidding Option</th>
                                            <th>Description</th>
                                            <th>When to Use</th>
                                        </tr>
                                    </thead>
                                    <tbody>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td><strong>Use Ad Group Default</strong></td>
                                            <td>Keywords inherit ad group bid</td>
                                            <td>Most campaigns, simplifies management</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td><strong>Set Custom Bid</strong></td>
                                            <td>Specific bid for individual keyword</td>
                                            <td>High-value keywords, competitive targeting</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td><strong>Auto Bidding</strong></td>
                                            <td>Google automatically adjusts bids</td>
                                            <td>Maximize conversions, smart campaigns</td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </tbody>
                                </table>
                            </div>
                            <div class="alert alert-info small mt-3">
                                <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Start with ad group default bids. After gathering data (2-3 weeks), adjust bids for top-performing keywords and reduce for underperformers.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== STEP 6: ADD NEGATIVE KEYWORDS ==================== -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Step 6: Adding Negative Keywords (Protect Your Budget)</h4>
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header bg-dark text-white">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Excluding Irrelevant Content</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h6>How to Add Negative Keywords</h6>
                            <ol>
                                <li>In the "Keywords" section, click the <strong>"Negative keywords"</strong> tab</li>
                                <li>Click the <strong>"+"</strong> button</li>
                                <li>Enter keywords to exclude (e.g., "free", "cheap", "download")</li>
                                <li>Select match type (broad, phrase, exact)</li>
                                <li>Click <strong>"Save"</strong></li>
                            </ol>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                <strong>Example Negative Keywords:</strong>
                                <ul class="mb-0">
                                    <li>free - Excludes pages with "free" content</li>
                                    <li>"discount" - Excludes exact phrase "discount"</li>
                                    <li>[cheap running shoes] - Excludes exact phrase</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h6>Where to Add Negative Keywords</h6>
                            <div class="table-responsive">
                                <table class="table table-sm">
                                    <thead class="table-light">
                                        <tr>
                                            <th>Level</th>
                                            <th>Scope</th>
                                            <th>Best For</th>
                                        </tr>
                                    </thead>
                                    <tbody>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td><strong>Ad Group Level</strong></td>
                                            <td>Applies to specific ad group</td>
                                            <td>Theme-specific exclusions</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td><strong>Campaign Level</strong></td>
                                            <td>Applies to all ad groups</td>
                                            <td>Broad exclusions (e.g., "free")</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td><strong>Account Level</strong></td>
                                            <td>Applies to all campaigns</td>
                                            <td>Brand safety exclusions</td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </tbody>
                                </table>
                            </div>
                            <div class="alert alert-warning small mt-2 mb-0">
                                <strong>Important:</strong> Add negative keywords at the highest level possible to save time and ensure consistency.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== STEP 7: REVIEW AND SAVE ==================== -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Step 7: Review and Save Keywords</h4>
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Final Review Before Activation</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-12">
                            <p><strong>Review Checklist:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Check all keywords for spelling and relevance</li>
                                <li>Verify match types are correctly assigned</li>
                                <li>Ensure negative keywords are in the right tab</li>
                                <li>Review keyword count (10-20 per ad group is optimal)</li>
                                <li>Confirm bids are set appropriately</li>
                                <li>Check for duplicate keywords</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-success small mt-3 mb-0">
                                <strong>Save Button:</strong> Click <strong>"Save"</strong> at the bottom of the page to add keywords to your campaign.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== STEP 8: MONITOR AND OPTIMIZE ==================== -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Step 8: Monitor and Optimize Keyword Performance</h4>
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Ongoing Keyword Management</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h6>Where to Find Performance Data</h6>
                            <ol>
                                <li>Go to your <strong>ad group</strong> or <strong>campaign</strong></li>
                                <li>Click <strong>"Keywords"</strong> in the left menu</li>
                                <li>Review metrics: Impressions, Clicks, CTR, Cost, Conversions</li>
                                <li>Sort by performance (e.g., highest CTR, lowest CPA)</li>
                            </ol>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h6>Optimization Actions</h6>
                            <div class="table-responsive">
                                <table class="table table-sm">
                                    <thead class="table-light">
                                        <tr>
                                            <th>Performance</th>
                                            <th>Action</th>
                                        </tr>
                                    </thead>
                                    <tbody>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>High CTR, High Conversions</td>
                                            <td>Increase bid, expand keywords</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Low CTR, High Conversions</td>
                                            <td>Improve ad creative</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>High CTR, Low Conversions</td>
                                            <td>Check landing page, refine targeting</td>
                                        </tr>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Low CTR, Low Conversions</td>
                                            <td>Pause or replace keyword</td>
                                        </tr>
                                    </tbody>
                                </table>
                            </div>
                            <div class="alert alert-info small mt-2 mb-0">
                                <strong>Review Schedule:</strong> Check keyword performance weekly for the first month, then monthly for ongoing optimization.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== STEP 9: PRACTICAL EXAMPLE ==================== -->
            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Practical Example: Adding Keywords to a Display Campaign</h4>
