                         <div class="section" id="topic-5">
    <div class="card mb-4 border">
        <div class="card-header bg-white py-3">
            <h2 class="mb-0">5 How Keywords Work in Google Display Campaigns</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <div class="alert alert-light border mb-4">
                <strong>Understanding how display keywords function is essential for campaign success.</strong> Unlike search campaigns where keywords trigger ads based on user queries, display keywords work through content matching. This fundamental difference affects everything from targeting strategy to performance optimization.
            </div>
            <p>Display keywords operate on a completely different principle than search keywords. In search campaigns, keywords represent what users are actively looking for. In display campaigns, keywords represent the content context where your ads appear. This distinction is crucial for understanding how to build effective display campaigns.</p>
            <!-- ==================== SECTION 1: THE MECHANICS OF DISPLAY KEYWORD MATCHING ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">The Mechanics of Display Keyword Matching</h3>
            <div class="alert alert-info mb-4">
                <strong>Content-Based Matching:</strong> Google analyzes webpage content and matches it against your keywords. If the page content is relevant to your keywords, your ad becomes eligible to appear on that page.
            </div>
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded mb-0"><code class="language-bash">
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    DISPLAY KEYWORD MATCHING PROCESS                     │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                         │
│  STEP 1: Google Bot Crawls a Webpage                                    │
│     ↓                                                                   │
│  STEP 2: Extracts Content from:                                         │
│     • Page title and headings                                           │
│     • Body text and paragraphs                                          │
│     • Meta descriptions and keywords                                    │
│     • Image alt text and captions                                       │
│     • URL structure and domain authority                                │
│     ↓                                                                   │
│  STEP 3: Natural Language Processing (NLP) Applied                      │
│     • Identifies main topics and themes                                 │
│     • Understands context and semantics                                 │
│     • Recognizes related concepts                                       │
│     ↓                                                                   │
│  STEP 4: Matches Against Your Display Keywords                          │
│     • Broad match: Related concepts                                     │
│     • Phrase match: Close variations                                    │
│     • Exact match: Exact phrases                                        │
│     ↓                                                                   │
│  STEP 5: Ad Auction Determines Placement                                │
│     • Ad rank based on bid and quality                                  │
│     • Ad shown if it wins the auction                                   │
│                                                                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                    </code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">How Google Analyzes Content</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h5>Content Analysis Factors</h5>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Keyword Density:</strong> Frequency of keywords in content</li>
                                <li><strong>Semantic Relevance:</strong> Related terms and concepts</li>
                                <li><strong>Content Structure:</strong> Headings, subheadings, formatting</li>
                                <li><strong>Page Authority:</strong> Domain authority and trustworthiness</li>
                                <li><strong>User Engagement:</strong> Time on page, bounce rate</li>
                                <li><strong>Content Freshness:</strong> Publication date and updates</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-3 mb-0">
                                <strong>Key Insight:</strong> Google doesn't just look for exact matches. It understands context and related concepts, making broad match more sophisticated in display campaigns.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Keyword Matching in Action</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h5>Practical Example</h5>
                            <p><strong>Your Keyword:</strong> "Digital Marketing Course"</p>
                            <p><strong>Matching Pages:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Article: "Top 10 Digital Marketing Skills for 2025"</li>
                                <li>Blog: "How to Start a Career in Digital Marketing"</li>
                                <li>Video: "Complete Digital Marketing Tutorial"</li>
                                <li>Website: "Best Online Marketing Courses and Training"</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-3 mb-0">
                                <strong>Result:</strong> Your ad appears on all these pages because they contain relevant content about digital marketing.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 2: DISPLAY KEYWORD MATCH TYPES EXPLAINED ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Display Keyword Match Types Explained</h3>

            <div class="alert alert-warning mb-4">
                <strong>Important:</strong> Display keyword match types work differently than search match types. They focus on content relevance rather than search query matching.
            </div>

            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Match Type</th>
                            <th>Symbol</th>
                            <th>How It Works</th>
                            <th>Reach</th>
                            <th>Relevance</th>
                            <th>Best Use Case</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Broad Match</strong></td>
                            <td>None</td>
                            <td>Matches pages containing related concepts and themes</td>
                            <td>Very High</td>
                            <td>Low</td>
                            <td>Awareness campaigns, broad reach</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Phrase Match</strong></td>
                            <td>"Keyword"</td>
                            <td>Matches pages containing the phrase or close variations</td>
                            <td>Medium</td>
                            <td>Medium</td>
                            <td>Consideration campaigns, balanced approach</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Exact Match</strong></td>
                            <td>[Keyword]</td>
                            <td>Matches pages containing the exact phrase</td>
                            <td>Low</td>
                            <td>High</td>
                            <td>Conversion campaigns, precision targeting</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Automatic Match</strong></td>
                            <td>N/A</td>
                            <td>Google automatically finds related content</td>
                            <td>Variable</td>
                            <td>Variable</td>
                            <td>Discovery campaigns, testing new audiences</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <h4 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Detailed Match Type Comparison</h4>
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                            <h5 class="mb-0">Broad Match Example</h5>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Keyword:</strong> running shoes</p>
                            <p><strong>Matching Pages:</strong></p>
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li>Article: "Best Sports Equipment for Beginners"</li>
                                <li>Blog: "How to Train for a Marathon"</li>
                                <li>Video: "Running Techniques and Tips"</li>
                                <li>Website: "Fitness and Exercise Guide"</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                <strong>Reach:</strong> Very broad. May include less relevant content.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                            <h5 class="mb-0">Exact Match Example</h5>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Keyword:</strong> [buy running shoes online]</p>
                            <p><strong>Matching Pages:</strong></p>
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li>Article: "Where to Buy Running Shoes Online"</li>
                                <li>Blog: "Best Online Stores for Running Shoes"</li>
                                <li>Website: "Buy Running Shoes - Official Store"</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                <strong>Reach:</strong> Very specific. High relevance and intent alignment.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 3: SEARCH VS DISPLAY KEYWORD BEHAVIOR ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Search vs Display: Key Behavioral Differences</h3>

            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Aspect</th>
                            <th>Search Keywords</th>
                            <th>Display Keywords</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Trigger Mechanism</strong></td>
                            <td>User search queries</td>
                            <td>Page content and context</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>User Intent</strong></td>
                            <td>Active - users are looking for something</td>
                            <td>Passive - users are consuming content</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Match Types</strong></td>
                            <td>Broad, phrase, exact, BMM</td>
                            <td>Broad, phrase, exact, automatic</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Volume</strong></td>
                            <td>Lower - only when users search</td>
                            <td>Higher - content pages are abundant</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Cost</strong></td>
                            <td>Higher - competition for keywords</td>
                            <td>Lower - more inventory available</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Best For</strong></td>
                            <td>Capturing existing demand</td>
                            <td>Creating demand and building awareness</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 4: KEYWORD MATCHING ALGORITHM DEEP DIVE ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Understanding the Display Keyword Matching Algorithm</h3>

            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h4 class="fw-semibold">How Google Determines Content Relevance</h4>

                    <div class="row g-4 mt-3">
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <div class="card h-100">
                                <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                                    <h5 class="mb-0">Keyword Presence</h5>
                                </div>
                                <div class="card-body small">
                                    <p>Google checks for:</p>
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>Exact keyword matches</li>
                                        <li>Keyword variations and synonyms</li>
                                        <li>Keyword density in content</li>
                                        <li>Keyword placement (headlines, body, meta)</li>
                                    </ul>
                                    <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                        <strong>Weight:</strong> High - direct matches are prioritized
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <div class="card h-100">
                                <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                                    <h5 class="mb-0">Semantic Relevance</h5>
                                </div>
                                <div class="card-body small">
                                    <p>Google understands:</p>
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>Related concepts and themes</li>
                                        <li>Industry terminology</li>
                                        <li>Topic clusters and categories</li>
                                        <li>User search behavior patterns</li>
                                    </ul>
                                    <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                        <strong>Weight:</strong> Medium - broadens reach while maintaining relevance
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <div class="card h-100">
                                <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
                                    <h5 class="mb-0">Content Quality</h5>
                                </div>
                                <div class="card-body small">
                                    <p>Google evaluates:</p>
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>Content depth and length</li>
                                        <li>Domain authority and trust</li>
                                        <li>User engagement signals</li>
                                        <li>Content freshness and updates</li>
                                    </ul>
                                    <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                        <strong>Weight:</strong> Low to Medium - quality affects ad rank
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 5: AUTO-TARGETING VS MANUAL KEYWORD TARGETING ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Auto-Targeting vs Manual Keyword Targeting</h3>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Auto-Targeting</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h5>How It Works</h5>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Google automatically analyzes your landing page</li>
                                <li>Extracts relevant topics and themes</li>
                                <li>Finds related content across the web</li>
                                <li>Shows ads on automatically matched pages</li>
                            </ul>
                            <h5 class="mt-3">Advantages</h5>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Minimal setup required</li>
                                <li>Discovers new targeting opportunities</li>
                                <li>Adapts to content trends</li>
                                <li>Reduces management overhead</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-warning small mt-3 mb-0">
                                <strong>Limitation:</strong> Less control over where ads appear. May include irrelevant placements.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Manual Keyword Targeting</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h5>How It Works</h5>
                            <ul>
                                <li>You specify keywords for targeting</li>
                                <li>Google matches ads to relevant content</li>
                                <li>You control which topics to target</li>
                                <li>Full control over keyword selection</li>
                            </ul>
                            <h5 class="mt-3">Advantages</h5>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Complete control over targeting</li>
                                <li>Ability to exclude irrelevant topics</li>
                                <li>Fine-tuned to specific audience segments</li>
                                <li>Better ROI through precision targeting</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-warning small mt-3 mb-0">
                                <strong>Limitation:</strong> Requires research and ongoing optimization. May miss new opportunities.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 6: OPTIMUM KEYWORD STRATEGY BY FUNNEL STAGE ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Keyword Strategy by Funnel Stage</h3>

            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
