                         <!---->
                         <div class="section" id="topic-10">
    <div class="card mb-4 border">
        <div class="card-header bg-white py-3">
            <h2 class="mb-0">10 Negative Keywords for Display Campaigns</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            <div class="alert alert-light border mb-4">
                <strong>Negative keywords are one of the most powerful yet underutilized tools in display advertising.</strong> They prevent your ads from appearing on irrelevant content, saving budget, improving campaign performance, and protecting your brand reputation.
            </div>
            <p>Negative keywords tell Google which topics, content, or placements you want to avoid. In display campaigns, they prevent your ads from showing on pages that contain certain words or themes. This is crucial for maintaining relevance, reducing wasted spend, and ensuring your brand appears in appropriate contexts.</p>
            <!-- ==================== SECTION 1: UNDERSTANDING NEGATIVE KEYWORDS IN DISPLAY ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Understanding Negative Keywords in Display</h3>
            <div class="alert alert-info mb-4">
                <strong>Definition:</strong> Negative keywords are words or phrases that tell Google not to show your ads on pages containing those terms. They act as filters to exclude irrelevant or low-quality placements.
            </div>
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded mb-0"><code class="language-bash">
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    NEGATIVE KEYWORDS IN DISPLAY                         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                         │
│  WHY NEGATIVE KEYWORDS MATTER                                           │
│  └── Save budget by avoiding irrelevant traffic                         │
│  └── Improve campaign relevance and CTR                                 │
│  └── Protect brand reputation                                           │
│  └── Increase conversion rates                                          │
│  └── Better audience targeting                                          │
│                                                                         │
│  HOW THEY WORK                                                          │
│  └── You add words/phrases to exclude                                   │
│  └── Google analyzes page content                                       │
│  └── If page contains negative term → ad not shown                      │
│  └── Works alongside positive keywords                                  │
│                                                                         │
│  KEY DIFFERENCE FROM SEARCH                                             │
│  └── Search: Excludes search queries                                    │
│  └── Display: Excludes page content                                     │
│                                                                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                    </code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== SECTION 2: WHY NEGATIVE KEYWORDS ARE CRITICAL FOR DISPLAY ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Why Negative Keywords Are Critical for Display</h3>
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Budget Protection</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h5>How It Works</h5>
                            <p>Without negative keywords, your ads may appear on irrelevant pages, wasting budget on users who are not your target audience.</p>
                            <h5 class="mt-3">Real Example</h5>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small">
                                <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> You sell premium business software</p>
                                <p><strong>Without Negatives:</strong> Ads appear on "free software" articles</p>
                                <p><strong>With Negatives:</strong> Ads excluded from "free" content</p>
                                <p><strong>Result:</strong> Budget saved for qualified traffic</p>
                            </div>
                            <div class="alert alert-success small mt-2 mb-0">
                                <strong>Impact:</strong> Can reduce wasted spend by 20-40% in display campaigns.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Relevance Improvement</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h5>How It Works</h5>
                            <p>Negative keywords ensure your ads appear on content that's truly relevant to your offering, improving CTR and engagement.</p>
                            <h5 class="mt-3">Key Benefits</h5>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Higher click-through rates</li>
                                <li>Better quality scores</li>
                                <li>More engaged users</li>
                                <li>Improved conversion rates</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-info small mt-2 mb-0">
                                <strong>Tip:</strong> More relevant placements lead to 50-100% higher CTR on average.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Brand Safety</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <h5>How It Works</h5>
                            <p>Negative keywords prevent your brand from appearing next to inappropriate, controversial, or low-quality content.</p>
                            <h5 class="mt-3">Protection Areas</h5>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Controversial topics</li>
                                <li>Negative brand sentiment</li>
                                <li>Competitor-related content</li>
                                <li>Low-quality or spammy sites</li>
                                <li>Inappropriate material</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-danger small mt-2 mb-0">
                                <strong>Warning:</strong> One inappropriate placement can damage years of brand reputation.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== SECTION 3: TYPES OF NEGATIVE KEYWORDS FOR DISPLAY ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Types of Negative Keywords for Display</h3>
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Category</th>
                            <th>Description</th>
                            <th>Examples</th>
                            <th>When to Use</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>General Exclusions</strong></td>
                            <td>Broad terms that indicate low-quality or irrelevant content</td>
                            <td>free, cheap, download, torrent, cracked</td>
                            <td>Always, especially if offering premium products</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Content Quality</strong></td>
                            <td>Terms indicating low-quality or spam content</td>
                            <td>clickbait, spam, malware, virus</td>
                            <td>To protect brand reputation</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Competitor Related</strong></td>
                            <td>Terms related to competitor brands or alternatives</td>
                            <td>[competitor name], alternative, vs, compare</td>
                            <td>To avoid funding competitor awareness</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Inappropriate Content</strong></td>
                            <td>Terms indicating adult, violent, or controversial content</td>
                            <td>adult, violence, hate, political, religious</td>
                            <td>Brand safety protection</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>User Intent Mismatch</strong></td>
                            <td>Terms that don't match your target audience</td>
                            <td>student, beginner, tutorial, how-to</td>
                            <td>If targeting professionals or experts</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Location Irrelevant</strong></td>
                            <td>Location-specific terms outside your target market</td>
                            <td>[city/region not targeted]</td>
                            <td>When targeting specific geographic areas</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== SECTION 4: HOW NEGATIVE KEYWORDS WORK IN DISPLAY ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">How Negative Keywords Work in Display</h3>
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h4 class="fw-semibold">The Matching Process</h4>
                    <div class="row g-4 mt-3">
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <div class="card h-100">
                                <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                                    <h5 class="mb-0">Match Types</h5>
                                </div>
                                <div class="card-body">
                                    <div class="table-responsive">
                                        <table class="table table-sm">
                                            <thead class="table-light">
                                                <tr>
                                                    <th>Type</th>
                                                    <th>Excludes</th>
                                                    <th>Example</th>
                                                </tr>
                                            </thead>
                                            <tbody>
                                                <tr>
                                                    <td>Broad</td>
                                                    <td>Pages containing all terms</td>
                                                    <td>"free software" excludes pages with both terms</td>
                                                </tr>
                                                <tr>
                                                    <td>Phrase</td>
                                                    <td>Pages containing the exact phrase</td>
                                                    <td>"free software" excludes that exact phrase</td>
                                                </tr>
                                                <tr>
                                                    <td>Exact</td>
                                                    <td>Pages with the exact phrase only</td>
                                                    <td>[free software] excludes only that phrase</td>
                                                </tr>
                                            </tbody>
                                        </table>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <div class="card h-100">
                                <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                                    <h5 class="mb-0">Practical Example</h5>
                                </div>
                                <div class="card-body">
                                    <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> You sell premium project management software</p>
                                    <p><strong>Negative Keyword:</strong> "free project management"</p>
                                    <p><strong>Excluded Pages:</strong></p>
                                    <ul>
                                        <li>Articles about free software</li>
                                        <li>Blog posts listing free alternatives</li>
                                        <li>Comparison pages with free tools</li>
                                    </ul>
                                    <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                        <strong>Result:</strong> Your ads avoid users looking for free solutions, saving budget for qualified prospects.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <div class="card h-100">
                                <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
                                    <h5 class="mb-0">Display vs Search Behavior</h5>
                                </div>
                                <div class="card-body">
                                    <div class="table-responsive">
                                        <table class="table table-sm">
                                            <thead class="table-light">
                                                <tr>
                                                    <th>Aspect</th>
                                                    <th>Search</th>
                                                    <th>Display</th>
                                                </tr>
                                            </thead>
                                            <tbody>
                                                <tr>
                                                    <td>Trigger</td>
                                                    <td>Search queries</td>
                                                    <td>Page content</td>
                                                </tr>
                                                <tr>
                                                    <td>Exclusion</td>
                                                    <td>No search with negative</td>
                                                    <td>No page with negative content</td>
                                                </tr>
                                                <tr>
                                                    <td>Relevance</td>
                                                    <td>High precision</td>
                                                    <td>Content context</td>
                                                </tr>
                                            </tbody>
                                        </table>
                                    </div>
                                    <div class="alert alert-info small mt-2 mb-0">
                                        <strong>Key:</strong> Display negative keywords are about content, not search intent.
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <!-- ==================== SECTION 5: BUILDING YOUR NEGATIVE KEYWORD LIST ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Building Your Negative Keyword List</h3>
