                         <!-- ========== 12 DISPLAY CAMPAIGN OPTIMIZATION & BEST PRACTICES ========== -->
<div class="section" id="topic-12">
    <div class="card mb-4 border">
        <div class="card-header bg-white py-3">
            <h2 class="mb-0">12 Display Campaign Optimization & Best Practices </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            
            <div class="alert alert-light border mb-4">
                <strong> Turn average campaigns into top performers.</strong> Optimising display campaigns requires a mix of creative testing, placement management, audience layering, and bid adjustments. This section covers everything you need to know to maximize ROI from your Display campaigns.
            </div>

            <p>Display campaigns are different from Search campaigns. Optimization requires different strategies, metrics, and thinking. While Search campaigns focus on keywords and intent, Display campaigns focus on audiences, placements, and creative performance.</p>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 1: WEEKLY OPTIMIZATION CHECKLIST ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Weekly Optimization Checklist (30-Minute Routine)</h3>
            
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h4 class="text-primary"> Day 1-2: Data Analysis</h4>
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li>□ Review Campaign performance (impressions, clicks, CTR)</li>
                                <li>□ Check Conversion tracking is working</li>
                                <li>□ Analyze audience performance reports</li>
                                <li>□ Identify top/bottom performing ad groups</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h4 class="text-success"> Day 3-4: Targeting Optimization</h4>
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li>□ Review Placement reports → exclude poor sites</li>
                                <li>□ Check Audience reports → shift budget to top segments</li>
                                <li>□ Add negative keywords for irrelevant searches</li>
                                <li>□ Adjust demographic bids based on performance</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="row mt-3">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h4 class="text-warning"> Day 5-6: Creative Optimization</h4>
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li>□ Review Asset performance → pause low CTR assets</li>
                                <li>□ Check Ad strength → improve if needed</li>
                                <li>□ Add new headlines/descriptions to winning ad groups</li>
                                <li>□ Test new image variations</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h4 class="text-danger"> Day 7: Bidding & Budget</h4>
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li>□ Review CPA/ROAS against targets</li>
                                <li>□ Adjust bids for top-performing placements/audiences</li>
                                <li>□ Reallocate budget to winning campaigns</li>
                                <li>□ Check impression share lost due to budget</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 2: AUDIENCE LAYERING (DETAILED) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Audience Layering (Targeting + Observation) - Deep Dive</h3>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white"> Targeting (AND Logic)</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Restricts reach</strong> - Only shows ads to users who match ALL selected criteria.</p>
                            <p><strong>Use when:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>You know exactly who your customer is</li>
                                <li>Budget is limited (need high efficiency)</li>
                                <li>Running remarketing campaigns</li>
                                <li>Testing a specific hypothesis</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-secondary small mt-2">
                                <strong>Example:</strong> In-Market "Running Shoes" + Topic "Sports"<br>
                                = Only running shoe buyers on sports websites
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">👁 Observation (AND NOT Logic)</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Collects data without limiting reach</strong> - Shows ads normally, but tracks how specific audiences perform.</p>
                            <p><strong>Use when:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Launching a new campaign (data collection)</li>
                                <li>Testing new audience segments</li>
                                <li>You have sufficient budget for exploration</li>
                                <li>Unsure which audiences will convert</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-secondary small mt-2">
                                <strong>Example:</strong> Add 5 different affinity audiences as observation<br>
                                = See which one performs best, then switch that to targeting
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">🔁 Layering Strategy (AND + OR)</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Combine multiple methods</strong> for precision targeting.</p>
                            <p><strong>Recommended layering approach:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Broad audience (affinity/in-market) → OR logic</li>
                                <li>Keyword targeting (contextual) → AND logic</li>
                                <li>Demographic filters → AND logic</li>
                                <li>Placement targeting → AND logic (for premium sites)</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-secondary small mt-2">
                                <strong>Example:</strong> In-Market "Laptops" + Topic "Technology" + Age 25-44
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 3: PLACEMENT OPTIMIZATION (DETAILED) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Placement Optimization - Complete Guide</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h4> Where to Find Placement Report:</h4>
                    <p>Google Ads → Campaigns → [Your Campaign] → Placements tab</p>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> How to Analyze Placements:</h4>
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Scenario</th>
                                    <th>CTR</th>
                                    <th>Conversion Rate</th>
                                    <th>Cost</th>
                                    <th>Action</th>
                                    <th>Bid Adjustment</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Dream Placement</td>
                                    <td>High (>1%)</td>
                                    <td>High (>avg)</td>
                                    <td>Medium</td>
                                    <td>Keep + increase bids</td>
                                    <td>+20% to +50%</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Brand Safe, Low Performance</td>
                                    <td>Low (<0.2%)</td>
                                    <td>Low</td>
                                    <td>Low-Medium</td>
                                    <td>Reduce bids, test creative</td>
                                    <td>-20% to -30%</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>High Cost, No Conversions</td>
                                    <td>Low-Medium</td>
                                    <td>0%</td>
                                    <td>High</td>
                                    <td>Exclude immediately</td>
                                    <td>N/A (exclude)</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Irrelevant Content</td>
                                    <td>Very Low</td>
                                    <td>N/A</td>
                                    <td>Any</td>
                                    <td>Exclude (brand safety)</td>
                                    <td>N/A (exclude)</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Automatic Placement (New)</td>
                                    <td>Unknown</td>
                                    <td>Unknown</td>
                                    <td>Low</td>
                                    <td>Monitor for 1-2 weeks</td>
                                    <td>No change</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> How to Exclude Placements:</h4>
                    <ol>
                        <li><strong>At Campaign Level:</strong> Campaign → Placements → Select checkbox → Exclude</li>
                        <li><strong>At Account Level (Shared Library):</strong> Tools → Shared library → Placement exclusion lists → Create list</li>
                        <li><strong>Using Bulk Actions:</strong> Export placement report, add URLs to exclusion list, upload via Google Ads Editor</li>
                    </ol>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-warning mt-3">
                        <strong> Important:</strong> Don't exclude placements too early (first 7-10 days). Let the campaign gather data first - some placements need time to perform.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 4: AUDIENCE OPTIMIZATION ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Audience Optimization - Find Your Best Customers</h3>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white"> How to Analyze Audience Performance</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Where to find:</strong> Campaign → Audiences → View details</p>
                            <p><strong>Key metrics to analyze:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>CTR by audience:</strong> Which segments engage with your ads?</li>
                                <li><strong>Conversion rate:</strong> Which audiences actually convert?</li>
                                <li><strong>CPA by audience:</strong> Which segments are most cost-effective?</li>
                                <li><strong>Impression share:</strong> Are you reaching enough of this audience?</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-info small mt-2">
                                <strong> Pro Tip:</strong> Sort by conversion rate highest to lowest. The top 3-5 audiences should get 80% of your budget.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white"> Audience Optimization Actions</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>For top-performing audiences:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li> Increase bids by 20-50%</li>
                                <li> Create dedicated ad groups for them</li>
                                <li> Tailor creative messaging to their interests</li>
                                <li> Extend membership duration (e.g., 90 days → 180 days)</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p><strong>For underperforming audiences:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li> Decrease bids by 20-30%</li>
                                <li> Move to observation mode (don't target directly)</li>
                                <li> Pause if zero conversions after 30 days</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 5: CREATIVE OPTIMIZATION IN DEPTH ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Creative Optimization - Maximize CTR & Conversions</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h4> How to Find Creative Performance Data:</h4>
                    <p>Google Ads → Campaign → Ads & assets → Click on ad → "View asset details" → "Combinations" tab</p>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> Asset Performance Analysis Table:</h4>
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Asset Type</th>
                                    <th>Good Performance</th>
                                    <th>Poor Performance</th>
                                    <th>Action for Poor</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Short Headlines</td>
                                    <td>CTR > 0.5%</td>
                                    <td>CTR < 0.2%</td>
                                    <td>Replace with new angle (benefit vs urgency vs question)</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Long Headlines</td>
                                    <td>CTR > 0.4%</td>
                                    <td>CTR < 0.15%</td>
                                    <td>Make more descriptive or add social proof</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Descriptions</td>
                                    <td>CTR > 0.3%</td>
                                    <td>CTR < 0.1%</td>
                                    <td>Add CTA, urgency, or value proposition</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Images (Landscape)</td>
                                    <td>CTR > 0.4%</td>
                                    <td>CTR < 0.15%</td>
                                    <td>Test different style (lifestyle vs product vs text overlay)</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Images (Square)</td>
                                    <td>CTR > 0.4%</td>
                                    <td>CTR < 0.15%</td>
                                    <td>Focus on product close-up vs scene shots</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> Creative Testing Framework:</h4>
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-3 text-center">
                            <div class="bg-light p-2 rounded">
                                <strong>Week 1-2</strong><br>
                                Launch with 5+ headlines, 5+ descriptions, 10+ images
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3 text-center">
                            <div class="bg-light p-2 rounded">
                                <strong>Week 3</strong><br>
                                Identify top 20% assets<br>
                                Pause bottom 30%
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3 text-center">
                            <div class="bg-light p-2 rounded">
                                <strong>Week 4</strong><br>
                                Add 5 new variations<br>
                                Test new image styles
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3 text-center">
                            <div class="bg-light p-2 rounded">
                                <strong>Week 6</strong><br>
                                Full refresh<br>
                                Replace bottom 40%
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 6: BIDDING STRATEGY OPTIMIZATION ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Bidding Strategy Optimization - Step by Step</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h4> Bidding Strategy Maturity Model:</h4>
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Stage</th>
                                    <th>Minimum Conversions</th>
                                    <th>Recommended Strategy</th>
                                    <th>Goal</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Stage 1: Launch (Day 1-14)</strong></td>
                                    <td>0-15</td>
                                    <td><strong>Maximize Clicks</strong> or <strong>Manual CPC</strong></td>
                                    <td>Collect data, learn CTR patterns, identify top placements</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Stage 2: Learning (Day 15-30)</strong></td>
                                    <td>15-30</td>
                                    <td><strong>Maximize Conversions</strong> (no target)</td>
                                    <td>Let Google learn conversion patterns</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Stage 3: Optimizing (Day 30-60)</strong></td>
                                    <td>30-50</td>
                                    <td><strong>Target CPA</strong> (set realistic target)</td>
                                    <td>Stabilize CPA at profitable level</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Stage 4: Scaling (Day 60+)</strong></td>
                                    <td>50+</td>
                                    <td><strong>Target ROAS</strong> (e-commerce) or <strong>Portfolio bid strategies</strong></td>
                                    <td>Scale budget while maintaining efficiency</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> How to Set Realistic CPA Targets:</h4>
                    <div class="alert alert-info">
                        <strong>Formula:</strong> Average CPA Target = (Average Order Value × Target ROAS) ÷ 100<br>
                        <strong>Example:</strong> AOV $100, Target ROAS 400% → CPA Target = ($100 × 400%) ÷ 100 = $40
                    </div>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> Bid Adjustment Recommendations:</h4>
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Adjustment Type</th>
                                    <th>When to Increase (+) </th>
                                    <th>When to Decrease (-)</th>
                                    <th>Recommended Range</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Device: Mobile</td>
                                    <td>Mobile converts better</td>
                                    <td>Mobile has high bounce rate</td>
                                    <td>+10% to +50%</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Device: Desktop</td>
                                    <td>Desktop converts better</td>
                                    <td>Desktop underperforms</td>
                                    <td>-10% to -30%</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Location</td>
                                    <td>High-performing cities/regions</td>
                                    <td>Poor-performing areas</td>
                                    <td>+10% to +30%</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Ad Schedule</td>
                                    <td>Peak conversion hours</td>
                                    <td>Low conversion hours</td>
                                    <td>+15% to +25%</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Audience (Remarketing)</td>
                                    <td>Past converters, cart abandoners</td>
                                    <td>Low-intent audiences</td>
                                    <td>+20% to +50%</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 7: AUTOMATED RULES FOR DISPLAY ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Automated Rules - Save Time & Scale Optimization</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p><strong>Where to find:</strong> Tools → Automated rules</p>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-3"> Essential Automated Rules for Display Campaigns:</h4>
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Rule Name</th>
                                    <th>Condition</th>
                                    <th>Action</th>
                                    <th>Frequency</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Pause Low CTR Placements</td>
                                    <td>Placement CTR < 0.1% AND Impressions > 1000</td>
                                    <td>Pause placement</td>
                                    <td>Weekly</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Increase Bids for Top Placements</td>
                                    <td>Placement CTR > 1% AND Conversions > 5</td>
                                    <td>Increase bids by 20%</td>
                                    <td>Daily</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Pause Expensive Placements</td>
                                    <td>Cost > $100 AND Conversions = 0</td>
                                    <td>Pause placement</td>
                                    <td>Daily</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Budget Alert</td>
                                    <td>Spend > 80% of daily budget</td>
                                    <td>Send email alert</td>
                                    <td>Hourly</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Scale Winning Campaigns</td>
                                    <td>CPA < Target AND Impression share lost > 20%</td>
                                    <td>Increase budget by 20%</td>
                                    <td>Weekly</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> How to Create an Automated Rule:</h4>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Go to Tools & Settings → Automated rules</li>
                        <li>Click "+" button</li>
                        <li>Select "Placement" as rule type</li>
                        <li>Set conditions (e.g., CTR < 0.1%)</li>
                        <li>Choose action (e.g., Pause placement)</li>
                        <li>Set frequency (e.g., Weekly, every Monday at 9 AM)</li>
                        <li>Add email recipients for notifications</li>
                        <li>Preview results before saving</li>
                        <li>Save and activate</li>
                    </ol>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-warning mt-3">
                        <strong> Caution:</strong> Test rules with "Preview" or "Send email only" before activating automatic changes. Poorly configured rules can pause profitable placements or overspend budget.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 8: BUDGET OPTIMIZATION ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Budget Optimization - Spend Smart</h3>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white"> Budget Allocation Strategy</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Rule of Thumb:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>70% Budget:</strong> Top-performing campaigns (positive ROI)</li>
                                <li><strong>20% Budget:</strong> Testing new audiences/creatives</li>
                                <li><strong>10% Budget:</strong> Experimental channels/formats</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-info small mt-2">
                                <strong> Tip:</strong> Use shared budgets for campaigns with similar goals to optimize across campaigns automatically.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white"> When to Increase Budget</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Signs you should increase budget:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li> Impression share lost due to budget > 20%</li>
                                <li> Campaign consistently hitting daily budget</li>
                                <li> CPA below target</li>
                                <li> Conversion volume increasing daily</li>
                                <li> ROAS above target (e-commerce)</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p><strong>Increase increment:</strong> 20-30% at a time</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark"> When to Decrease Budget</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Signs you should decrease budget:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li> CPA above target for 14+ days</li>
                                <li> ROAS below target (e-commerce)</li>
                                <li> Declining CTR week over week</li>
                                <li> High impression share lost due to rank (not budget)</li>
                                <li> Seasonal demand drop</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p><strong>Decrease increment:</strong> 30-50% if serious, 10-20% for minor issues</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 9: DEMOGRAPHIC BID ADJUSTMENTS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Demographic Bid Adjustments - Target Your Audience</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p><strong>Where to find:</strong> Campaign → Audiences → Demographics</p>
                    
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Demographic</th>
                                    <th>How to Analyze</th>
                                    <th>Recommended Action</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Age</strong></td>
                                    <td>Compare conversion rate by age group</td>
                                    <td>Increase bids for top 2-3 age groups (+20%), decrease for bottom 1-2 (-30%)</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Gender</strong></td>
                                    <td>Check if product is gender-specific or balanced</td>
                                    <td>If 70%+ conversions from one gender, decrease other by 50-70%</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Household Income</strong></td>
                                    <td>Higher income often = higher AOV</td>
                                    <td>Increase bids for Top 10-30% for premium products</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Parental Status</strong></td>
                                    <td>Parent vs Non-parent (critical for baby/children products)</td>
                                    <td>Target parents (+30%) if product is kid-related</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                        <strong> Pro Tip:</strong> Use "Observation" mode for demographics first (don't exclude). Collect 2-3 weeks of data, then adjust bids based on actual conversion performance.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 10: DEVICE BID ADJUSTMENTS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Device Bid Adjustments - Mobile vs Desktop vs Tablet</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="alert alert-success">
                                <strong> When to increase Mobile bids:</strong>
                                <ul class="mb-0">
                                    <li>Mobile-friendly website</li>
                                    <li>App install campaign</li>
                                    <li>Local business (users searching nearby)</li>
                                    <li>Younger target audience (18-34)</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="alert alert-warning">
                                <strong> When to decrease Mobile bids:</strong>
                                <ul class="mb-0">
                                    <li>Complex forms (long lead forms)</li>
                                    <li>High-value B2B purchases</li>
                                    <li>Older target audience (55+)</li>
                                    <li>High bounce rate on mobile</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-3"> Device Bid Adjustment Recommendations:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Mobile:</strong> Start at 0% (no adjustment), increase +10-30% after data shows better CPA</li>
                        <li><strong>Desktop:</strong> Often converts better for B2B/complex products, try +10-20%</li>
                        <li><strong>Tablet:</strong> Usually lowest volume, consider -20-30% unless data shows otherwise</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 11: AD SCHEDULING OPTIMIZATION ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Ad Scheduling - Show Ads When It Matters</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p><strong>Where to find:</strong> Campaign Settings → Ad schedule</p>
                    
                    <h4> How to Analyze Best Performing Hours:</h4>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Enable "Day & hour" column in Campaign reports</li>
                        <li>Run report for last 30 days</li>
                        <li>Sort by conversion rate or CPA (not just clicks)</li>
                        <li>Identify top 20% of hours</li>
                        <li>Schedule ads only during those hours</li>
                    </ol>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                        <strong> Pro Tip:</strong> Use ad scheduling with bid adjustments. Increase bids by 20-30% during peak conversion hours, decrease by 30-50% during off-hours.
                    </div>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> Ad Scheduling Best Practices:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>B2B:</strong> Focus on business hours (9 AM - 5 PM, Monday-Friday)</li>
                        <li><strong>E-commerce:</strong> Peak evenings (7 PM - 11 PM) and weekends</li>
                        <li><strong>Local business:</strong> Match your store hours + 1 hour before/after</li>
                        <li><strong>Lead generation:</strong> Test both business hours and evening (people research after work)</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 12: PERFORMANCE METRICS TO TRACK ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Key Display Campaign Metrics - What to Track</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Metric</th>
                            <th>What It Measures</th>
                            <th>Good Benchmark</th>
                            <th>Action if Low</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>CTR (Click-Through Rate)</strong></td>
                            <td>Ad engagement</td>
                            <td>0.3% - 0.6%</td>
                            <td>Improve creative, test new headlines/images</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Conversion Rate</strong></td>
                            <td>Action completion rate</td>
                            <td>0.5% - 2% (prospecting), 2-5% (remarketing)</td>
                            <td>Improve landing page, refine targeting</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>CPA (Cost Per Acquisition)</strong></td>
                            <td>Cost to get conversion</td>
                            <td>Varies by industry/avg order value</td>
                            <td>Reduce bids, exclude poor placements, improve creative</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>ROAS (Return on Ad Spend)</strong></td>
                            <td>Revenue per $1 spent</td>
                            <td>400%+ (4:1) is healthy</td>
                            <td>Increase bids on profitable segments, pause unprofitable</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>CTR</strong></td>
                            <td>Impression share captured</td>
                            <td>Aim for 60%+ on brand terms</td>
                            <td>Increase budget, improve Quality Score</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 13: COMMON OPTIMIZATION MISTAKES ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> 12 Common Display Campaign Optimization Mistakes</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Mistake</th>
                            <th>Consequence</th>
                            <th>How to Fix</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Optimizing too early (first 3-5 days)</td>
                            <td>Making decisions based on insufficient data</td>
                            <td>Wait at least 2 weeks before significant changes</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Only looking at CTR, not conversions</td>
                            <td>High CTR but low conversion = wrong audience</td>
                            <td>Optimize for conversion rate, not just CTR</td>
                        </tr>
                        </tr>
                            <td>Excluding placements too aggressively</td>
                            <td>Missing potential high-performers</td>
                            <td>Exclude only after 1000+ impressions with zero conversions</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Using same bids for all devices</td>
                            <td>Wasting budget on poor-performing devices</td>
                            <td>Analyze device performance, adjust bids accordingly</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No frequency caps</td>
                            <td>Ad fatigue, brand hatred, wasted impressions</td>
                            <td>Set 3-5 impressions per user/day</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Targeting too broadly</td>
                            <td>Low relevance, high cost, low CTR</td>
                            <td>Layer multiple targeting methods (audience + topic + keyword)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Ignoring placement reports</td>
                            <td>Wasting budget on low-quality sites</td>
                            <td>Review placement reports weekly</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Not testing enough creative variations</td>
                            <td>Missed optimization opportunities</td>
                            <td>Run A/B tests continuously</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No negative keywords</td>
                            <td>Ads showing on irrelevant pages</td>
                            <td>Add negative keywords regularly</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Using only automatic placements</td>
                            <td>Missing high-performing manual placements</td>
                            <td>Add top automatic placements as managed placements</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 14: QUICK REFERENCE OPTIMIZATION CHEAT SHEET ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Display Campaign Optimization Cheat Sheet</h3>
            
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h4 class="text-primary"> Weekly Tasks:</h4>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>□ Review placement reports → exclude poor sites</li>
                                <li>□ Check audience performance → shift budget</li>
                                <li>□ Analyze creative performance → pause low CTR assets</li>
                                <li>□ Review conversion rate by device/location</li>
                                <li>□ Check impression share lost due to budget</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h4 class="text-success"> Monthly Tasks:</h4>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>□ Full creative refresh (add 5+ new headlines/images)</li>
                                <li>□ Review and update negative keywords list</li>
                                <li>□ Analyze demographic performance → adjust bids</li>
                                <li>□ Test new audience segments (observation mode)</li>
                                <li>□ Review automated rules performance</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="row mt-3">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h4 class="text-warning"> Bidding Strategy:</h4>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>• Start: Maximize clicks (data collection)</li>
                                <li>• After 30 conversions: Target CPA</li>
                                <li>• E-commerce: Target ROAS after 50+ conversions</li>
                                <li>• Increase budget when impression share lost > 20%</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h4 class="text-danger"> Creative Testing:</h4>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>• Test 5+ headlines simultaneously</li>
                                <li>• Test 4-5 descriptions</li>
                                <li>• Test 10+ images (lifestyle vs product vs text)</li>
                                <li>• Refresh creative every 4-6 weeks</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Summary Alert -->
            <div class="alert alert-success mt-4">
                <strong> Himanshu Shekhar's Summary for Section 10.5:</strong>
                <ul class="mb-0 mt-2">
                    <li> Optimization is a continuous process - weekly reviews are essential</li>
                    <li> Always optimize based on conversions (not just clicks or impressions)</li>
                    <li> Use audience layering (targeting + observation) to improve relevance</li>
                    <li> Review placement reports weekly - exclude poor performers</li>
                    <li> Test creative variations continuously - refresh every 4-6 weeks</li>
                    <li> Start with Maximize clicks, switch to Target CPA/Target ROAS after 30+ conversions</li>
                    <li> Use automated rules to save time on repetitive optimization tasks</li>
                    <li> Don't optimize too early - wait 2 weeks for sufficient data</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-primary mt-2">
                <strong> Remember:</strong> Display campaigns take time to mature. Be patient, use data-driven decisions, and continuously test new audiences, creatives, and placements. The campaigns that perform best are those that are optimized consistently over weeks and months, not days.
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</div>
