            <!-- ==================== SECTION 5: HOW YOUTUBE ADS WORK ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> How YouTube Ads Work: The Auction System</h3>
            
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded mb-0" style="font-family: monospace;">
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    YOUTUBE AD AUCTION FLOW                              │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                                         │
│  1. User watches a video on YouTube                                     │
│         ↓                                                               │
│  2. Ad slot becomes available (pre-roll, mid-roll, or post-roll)       │
│         ↓                                                               │
│  3. Google runs an auction with eligible advertisers:                   │
│     • Ad Rank = (Max CPV bid) × (Ad Quality Score)                     │
│     • Quality Score factors: expected CTR, relevance, landing page     │
│         ↓                                                               │
│  4. Winner's ad is displayed                                            │
│         ↓                                                               │
│  5. If skippable in-stream:                                            │
│     • User watches 30 seconds OR clicks on ad → you pay                 │
│     • User skips before 30 seconds → you pay $0                         │
│         ↓                                                               │
│  6. Your CPV = (next highest bid / Ad Rank) + $0.01                    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</pre>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                <strong> Key Insight:</strong> For skippable in-stream ads, you only pay when a viewer watches at least 30 seconds (or the full ad if shorter) OR clicks on the ad. This means you're only paying for engaged viewers who actually watch your message!
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 6: YOUTUBE VIEWER MINDSET ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Understanding YouTube Viewer Mindset</h3>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white"> Entertainment Mode</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Most users are on YouTube for entertainment, education, or information. They're not actively looking to buy.</p>
                            <p><strong>Implication:</strong> Your ads need to be entertaining or educational first, promotional second.</p>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2">
                                <strong>Example:</strong> Instead of "Buy our software", try "5 ways to save 10 hours per week" (educational hook)
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white"> Short Attention Span</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>Viewers can skip ads after 5 seconds. You have <strong>5 seconds to hook them</strong> or they're gone.</p>
                            <p><strong>Implication:</strong> Front-load your best message in the first 5 seconds.</p>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2">
                                <strong>Example:</strong> "Tired of expensive software? Meet the $9 alternative..." (hook in 3 seconds)
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark"> Mobile-First</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p>70%+ of YouTube watch time is on mobile devices. Videos play vertically or horizontally.</p>
                            <p><strong>Implication:</strong> Design for mobile with large text, clear visuals, and vertical-friendly framing.</p>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2">
                                <strong>Example:</strong> Text should be at least 24pt, use high-contrast colors
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 7: VIDEO AD SPECIFICATIONS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Complete Video Ad Technical Specifications</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Specification</th>
