                         <!-- ========== 14 HOW TO CREATE A VIDEO CAMPAIGN (ULTRA-ENHANCED) ========== -->
<div class="section" id="topic-14">
    <div class="card mb-4 border">
        <div class="card-header bg-white py-3">
            <h2 class="mb-0">14 How to Create a Video Campaign </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">
            
            <div class="alert alert-light border mb-4">
                <strong> Step‑by‑step walkthrough for YouTube video campaigns.</strong> Follow these instructions to launch your first video ad campaign. This guide covers everything from campaign setup to advanced optimization techniques.
            </div>

            <p>Creating a YouTube video campaign requires careful planning. Unlike search or display campaigns, video campaigns need video assets, thoughtful targeting, and bidding strategies optimized for engagement. This comprehensive guide will walk you through every step.</p>

            <!-- ==================== PRE-LAUNCH CHECKLIST ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Pre-Launch Checklist (Must Complete Before Starting)</h3>
            
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong> Account Setup:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>□ Google Ads account created and verified</li>
                                <li>□ YouTube channel created (required for video uploads)</li>
                                <li>□ Conversion tracking installed (if goal is conversions)</li>
                                <li>□ Google Analytics 4 linked to Google Ads</li>
                                <li>□ Billing information added and verified</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong> Video Assets:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>□ Video uploaded to YouTube (unlisted or public)</li>
                                <li>□ Video optimized for mobile (large text, clear visuals)</li>
                                <li>□ Captions/subtitles added (SRT file or YouTube auto-captions edited)</li>
                                <li>□ Companion banner created (300x60 or 300x250)</li>
                                <li>□ Thumbnail image prepared (for discovery ads)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong> Targeting Plan:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>□ Target audience defined (demographics, interests)</li>
                                <li>□ Remarketing lists created (website visitors, YouTube engagers)</li>
                                <li>□ Negative keywords identified</li>
                                <li>□ Placement exclusions planned</li>
                                <li>□ Budget allocation determined</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 1: CAMPAIGN GOAL SELECTION ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 1: Choose Your Campaign Goal</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>In Google Ads, click <strong>"+ New Campaign"</strong>. You'll see several goal options. Choose based on your business objective:</p>
                    
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Goal</th>
                                    <th>Best For</th>
                                    <th>Optimization Target</th>
                                    <th>Recommended Format</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Sales</strong></td>
                                    <td>E-commerce, product sales</td>
                                    <td>Conversions, ROAS</td>
                                    <td>Video Action, Skippable In-Stream</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Leads</strong></td>
                                    <td>B2B, service businesses, form fills</td>
                                    <td>Conversions (lead form fills)</td>
                                    <td>Video Action, Discovery Ads</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Website Traffic</strong></td>
                                    <td>Driving visitors to site</td>
                                    <td>Clicks, CPC</td>
                                    <td>Discovery Ads, Skippable In-Stream</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Brand Awareness</strong></td>
                                    <td>New products, brand building</td>
                                    <td>Impressions, reach, CPM</td>
                                    <td>Non-skippable, Bumper, Skippable</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Product & Brand Consideration</strong></td>
                                    <td>Middle-of-funnel, education</td>
                                    <td>Views, watch time</td>
                                    <td>Skippable In-Stream, Discovery</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                        <strong> Himanshu's Recommendation:</strong> For beginners, select <strong>"Create a campaign without a goal's guidance"</strong>. This gives you full control over all settings without Google's automatic optimizations that may not align with your specific goals.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 2: CAMPAIGN TYPE SELECTION ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 2: Select Campaign Type & Subtype</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>Select <strong>"Video"</strong> as your campaign type. Then choose the appropriate subtype:</p>
                    
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Campaign Subtype</th>
                                    <th>Best For</th>
                                    <th>Key Features</th>
                                    <th>When to Use</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Video Reach</strong></td>
                                    <td>Maximum impressions & reach</td>
                                    <td>Uses bumper + skippable ads, optimizes for CPM</td>
                                    <td>Brand awareness campaigns, large budgets</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Video Views</strong></td>
                                    <td>Cost-effective views</td>
                                    <td>Optimizes for CPV, best for testing</td>
                                    <td>Testing multiple creatives, limited budget</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Video Action</strong></td>
                                    <td>Conversions & website actions</td>
                                    <td>Optimizes for conversions, uses Target CPA/ROAS</td>
                                    <td>E-commerce, lead generation (requires conversion tracking)</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Video Order</strong></td>
                                    <td>Premium placements</td>
                                    <td>YouTube Reserve inventory, contact sales required</td>
                                    <td>Enterprise campaigns, guaranteed placements</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-success mt-3">
                        <strong> Himanshu's Pro Tip:</strong> Start with <strong>Video Views</strong> if you're new to YouTube advertising. It's the most cost-effective for testing. After you have conversion data (30+ conversions), switch to <strong>Video Action</strong> for direct response campaigns.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 3: CAMPAIGN NAMING & BASIC SETTINGS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 3: Campaign Naming & Basic Settings</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h4> Campaign Naming Convention:</h4>
                    <p>Use a consistent naming convention for easy reporting and management:</p>
                    <div class="alert alert-secondary">
                        <strong>Format:</strong> [Platform] - [Goal] - [Targeting] - [Format] - [Date]
                        <br>
                        <strong>Examples:</strong>
                        <ul class="mb-0 mt-2">
                            <li><code>YouTube - Awareness - InMarket_Fitness - Skippable - Q1_2025</code></li>
                            <li><code>YouTube - Conversions - Remarketing_Cart - VideoAction - Jan2025</code></li>
                            <li><code>YouTube - Views - Keywords_RunningShoes - Discovery - Test_1</code></li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> Location Targeting:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Countries:</strong> Select target countries (e.g., India, USA, UK)</li>
                        <li><strong>States/Regions:</strong> Narrow to specific states for local campaigns</li>
                        <li><strong>Cities:</strong> Target metropolitan areas</li>
                        <li><strong>Radius:</strong> Target areas around your business (e.g., 10km radius)</li>
                        <li><strong>Location Options:</strong>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Presence:</strong> People physically in your targeted location → <span class="badge bg-success">Recommended</span></li>
                                <li><strong>Interest:</strong> People interested in your location (e.g., someone in Delhi searching for "flats in Mumbai")</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> Language Targeting:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Select the language of your video content</li>
                        <li><strong>Recommendation:</strong> Start with "All languages", then narrow based on performance data</li>
                        <li>For local campaigns, select the local language (Hindi, Tamil, Bengali, etc.)</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 4: CONTENT EXCLUSIONS (BRAND SAFETY) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 4: Content Exclusions - Protect Your Brand</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>Content exclusions prevent your ads from appearing next to inappropriate or irrelevant content.</p>
                    
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Exclusion Type</th>
                                    <th>What It Blocks</th>
                                    <th>Recommended Setting</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Digital Content Labels</strong></td>
                                    <td>DL-G (General), DL-PG (Parental Guidance), DL-MA (Mature Audiences)</td>
                                    <td>Exclude DL-MA for family-friendly brands</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Inventory Type</strong></td>
                                    <td>Live streaming, embedded videos, YouTube Shorts</td>
                                    <td>Exclude live streaming for brand safety</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Sensitive Content Categories</strong></td>
                                    <td>Tragedy & conflict, sexual content, profanity, sensitive social issues</td>
                                    <td>Exclude based on your brand's risk tolerance</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Excluded Placements</strong></td>
                                    <td>Specific YouTube channels, videos, or apps</td>
                                    <td>Add after analyzing placement reports (1-2 weeks in)</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        <tr>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-warning mt-3">
                        <strong> Important:</strong> Don't over-exclude content categories when starting. Too many exclusions can drastically reduce your reach. Let the campaign run for 1-2 weeks, then exclude based on actual placement data.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 5: BUDGET & BIDDING STRATEGY ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 5: Budget & Bidding Strategy (Most Critical)</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h4> Budget Settings:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Daily Budget:</strong> Start with $10-50/day for testing, increase based on performance</li>
                        <li><strong>Campaign Budget Optimization:</strong> Distribute budget across ad groups automatically</li>
                        <li><strong>Shared Budget:</strong> Use for multiple campaigns with similar goals</li>
                    </ul>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> Bidding Strategies Explained:</h4>
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Strategy</th>
                                    <th>Payment Model</th>
                                    <th>Best For</th>
                                    <th>When to Use</th>
                                    <th>Typical Bid</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Target CPV</strong> (Cost Per View)</td>
                                    <td>Pay when user watches 30s or clicks</td>
                                    <td>Video views, awareness</td>
                                    <td>Starting out, testing creatives</td>
                                    <td>$0.01-0.05</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Target CPM</strong> (Cost Per Thousand Impressions)</td>
                                    <td>Pay per 1,000 impressions</td>
                                    <td>Impressions, reach, brand awareness</td>
                                    <td>Non-skippable, bumper ads</td>
                                    <td>$3-8</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Maximize Conversions</strong></td>
                                    <td>Automatic bidding for conversions</td>
                                    <td>Lead generation, sales</td>
                                    <td>After conversion tracking set up (30+ conversions)</td>
                                    <td>Varies</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Target CPA</strong> (Cost Per Action)</td>
                                    <td>Set target cost per conversion</td>
                                    <td>E-commerce, lead gen with targets</td>
                                    <td>After 50+ conversions, stable performance</td>
                                    <td>Varies</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Target ROAS</strong> (Return on Ad Spend)</td>
                                    <td>Set target revenue per $1 spent</td>
                                    <td>E-commerce with cart values</td>
                                    <td>After 100+ conversions, high volume</td>
                                    <td>300-500%</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                        <strong> Himanshu's Bidding Recommendation for Beginners:</strong>
                        <ul class="mb-0">
                            <li><strong>Week 1-2:</strong> Use Target CPV ($0.02-0.03) to collect data</li>
                            <li><strong>Week 3-4:</strong> Switch to Maximize Conversions (after conversion tracking)</li>
                            <li><strong>Week 5+:</strong> Use Target CPA after 50+ conversions</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 6: AD GROUP & TARGETING ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 6: Ad Group Creation & Audience Targeting</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h4> Ad Group Naming Convention:</h4>
                    <div class="alert alert-secondary">
                        <strong>Format:</strong> [Targeting Type] - [Theme] - [Intent Level]
                        <br>
                        <strong>Examples:</strong>
                        <ul class="mb-0 mt-2">
                            <li><code>Audience - InMarket_RunningShoes - HighIntent</code></li>
                            <li><code>Keywords - RunningShoesReview - Consideration</code></li>
                            <li><code>Remarketing - CartAbandoners - 30Days - HighestIntent</code></li>
                            <li><code>Placement - CompetitorChannel - Conquesting</code></li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> Audience Targeting Options:</h4>
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="bg-light p-3 rounded mb-3">
                                <strong> Demographics</strong>
                                <ul class="small mb-0">
                                    <li>Age ranges (18-24, 25-34, 35-44, 45-54, 55-64, 65+)</li>
                                    <li>Gender (Male, Female, Unknown)</li>
                                    <li>Parental status (Parent, Not a parent)</li>
                                    <li>Household income (Top 10%, 11-20%, etc.)</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                            <div class="bg-light p-3 rounded mb-3">
                                <strong>❤ Affinity & In-Market</strong>
                                <ul class="small mb-0">
                                    <li>Affinity: Long-term interests (Fitness Buffs, Techies, Gamers)</li>
                                    <li>In-Market: Active purchase intent (Buying a car, Booking travel)</li>
                                    <li>Life Events: Moving, graduation, wedding</li>
                                    <li>Custom Affinity: Build from keywords, URLs, apps</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="bg-light p-3 rounded mb-3">
                                <strong> Keywords & Placements</strong>
                                <ul class="small mb-0">
                                    <li>Keywords: Target YouTube search terms</li>
                                    <li>Video keywords: Content of videos being watched</li>
                                    <li>Placements: Specific YouTube channels or videos</li>
                                    <li>Topics: Content categories (e.g., "Sports", "Technology")</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                            <div class="bg-light p-3 rounded mb-3">
                                <strong> Remarketing (Highest Converting)</strong>
                                <ul class="small mb-0">
                                    <li>Website visitors (30-540 days)</li>
                                    <li>YouTube viewers (25%, 50%, 75%, 100% watched)</li>
                                    <li>YouTube channel visitors</li>
                                    <li>Customer Match (email lists)</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 7: FREQUENCY CAPPING ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 7: Frequency Capping - Prevent Ad Fatigue</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p><strong>Frequency capping</strong> limits how many times a user sees your ad. Without caps, users see your ad 20+ times → negative brand sentiment.</p>
                    
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Campaign Type</th>
                                    <th>Recommended Frequency Cap</th>
                                    <th>Time Period</th>
                                    <th>Why?</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Prospecting (Cold Audience)</td>
                                    <td>3-5 impressions</td>
                                    <td>Per week</td>
                                    <td>Enough to create awareness without annoyance</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Remarketing (Warm Audience)</td>
                                    <td>2-3 impressions</td>
                                    <td>Per week</td>
                                    <td>Higher intent, less frequency needed</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Brand Awareness</td>
                                    <td>1-2 impressions</td>
                                    <td>Per day</td>
                                    <td>Avoid over-saturation, protect brand perception</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Bumper Ads (6 seconds)</td>
                                    <td>5-7 impressions</td>
                                    <td>Per week</td>
                                    <td>Short format, less intrusive, more frequency acceptable</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-warning mt-3">
                        <strong> Warning:</strong> Not setting frequency caps is one of the most common mistakes! Users seeing your ad 20+ times = ad fatigue = brand hatred = wasted budget.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 8: VIDEO AD CREATION ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 8: Creating Your Video Ad (Detailed)</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h4> Step 8.1: Upload Video to YouTube</h4>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Go to YouTube Studio (studio.youtube.com)</li>
                        <li>Click "Create" → "Upload videos"</li>
                        <li>Select your video file (MP4 recommended)</li>
                        <li>Add title, description, and tags (helps with discovery)</li>
                        <li>Set visibility to <strong>Unlisted</strong> or <strong>Public</strong> (required for ads)</li>
                        <li>Add captions/subtitles (SRT file or use YouTube's auto-caption)</li>
                    </ol>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> Step 8.2: Create Ad in Google Ads</h4>
                    <ol start="7">
                        <li>In Google Ads, go to your video campaign</li>
                        <li>Click "Create ad group" or edit existing</li>
                        <li>Select "Video" as ad type</li>
                        <li>Choose your uploaded video from YouTube</li>
                    </ol>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> Step 8.3: Companion Banner (Optional but Recommended)</h4>
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Placement</th>
                                    <th>Dimensions</th>
                                    <th>File Size</th>
                                    <th>Best Practice</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Standard banner</td>
                                    <td>300x250</td>
                                    <td>150KB max</td>
                                    <td>Show logo + CTA, consistent with video</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Leaderboard</td>
                                    <td>728x90</td>
                                    <td>150KB max</td>
                                    <td>Use for desktop placements</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> Step 8.4: Call-to-Action (CTA) Overlay</h4>
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="bg-light p-3 rounded">
                                <strong>CTA Fields:</strong>
                                <ul>
                                    <li><strong>Headline:</strong> Max 15 characters</li>
                                    <li><strong>Description:</strong> Max 35 characters</li>
                                    <li><strong>Final URL:</strong> Landing page URL</li>
                                    <li><strong>Display URL:</strong> Shown in ad (max 20 chars)</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <div class="alert alert-info">
                                <strong>CTA Examples:</strong>
                                <ul class="mb-0">
                                    <li>"Shop Now" → "Limited Time Sale"</li>
                                    <li>"Learn More" → "Free Consultation"</li>
                                    <li>"Sign Up" → "Get Free Trial"</li>
                                    <li>"Download" → "Free Ebook"</li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> Step 8.5: End Screens & Cards (For Skippable In-Stream)</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>End screens:</strong> Appear in last 5-20 seconds, drive clicks</li>
                        <li><strong>Cards:</strong> Notifications that appear during video (timed)</li>
                        <li><strong>Best practice:</strong> Add end screen with "Learn more" button</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 9: AD SCHEDULING ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 9: Ad Scheduling - Show Ads at the Right Time</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p><strong>Ad scheduling</strong> lets you choose specific days and times to run your ads. Use data from Google Analytics to identify peak conversion hours.</p>
                    
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Business Type</th>
                                    <th>Best Days</th>
                                    <th>Best Hours</th>
                                    <th>Bid Adjustment</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>B2B / SaaS</td>
                                    <td>Monday-Friday</td>
                                    <td>9 AM - 5 PM (business hours)</td>
                                    <td>+20% during peak hours, -50% off-hours</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>E-commerce / Retail</td>
                                    <td>Daily</td>
                                    <td>7 PM - 11 PM (evening browsing)</td>
                                    <td>+30% evenings, -30% early mornings</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Local Business</td>
                                    <td>Monday-Saturday</td>
                                    <td>Match store hours + 1 hour before/after</td>
                                    <td>+15% during open hours</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Lead Generation</td>
                                    <td>Tuesday-Thursday</td>
                                    <td>10 AM - 2 PM (lunch research)</td>
                                    <td>+25% during peak, -40% weekends</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                        <strong> Pro Tip:</strong> Start with 24/7 scheduling for the first 2 weeks to collect data. Then analyze the "Day & hour" report in Google Ads to identify your best-performing time slots.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 10: REVIEW & PUBLISH ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step 10: Review & Publish Campaign</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h4> Final Review Checklist:</h4>
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li>□ Campaign name follows naming convention</li>
                                <li>□ Daily budget set correctly</li>
                                <li>□ Bidding strategy appropriate for goal</li>
                                <li>□ Location targeting correct (Presence vs Interest)</li>
                                <li>□ Language targeting set correctly</li>
                                <li>□ Content exclusions configured (brand safety)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li>□ Ad group targeting selected</li>
                                <li>□ Frequency caps set (3-5 impressions/week)</li>
                                <li>□ Ad scheduling configured (if needed)</li>
                                <li>□ Video uploaded and accessible</li>
                                <li>□ CTA overlay text optimized</li>
                                <li>□ Conversion tracking active (if goal is conversions)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> Common Errors That Prevent Publishing:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li> No video selected or video not uploaded to YouTube</li>
                        <li> Video set to "Private" (must be unlisted or public)</li>
                        <li> Missing or invalid final URL</li>
                        <li> Budget too low (minimum $5-10/day recommended)</li>
                        <li> No location targeting selected</li>
                        <li> Ad group has no targeting methods</li>
                    </ul>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-success mt-3">
                        <strong> After Publishing:</strong>
                        <ul class="mb-0">
                            <li>Wait 2-3 days before making changes (allow learning phase)</li>
                            <li>Monitor daily for first week, weekly thereafter</li>
                            <li>Check placement reports after 1-2 weeks</li>
                            <li>Review "Video ad sequence" report for drop-off points</li>
                            <li>Use Google Ads "Recommendations" page for optimization ideas</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 11: ADVANCED OPTIMIZATION TIPS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Advanced Optimization Tips (After Campaign is Live)</h3>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white"> Week 1-2: Data Collection</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li>Don't make major changes</li>
                                <li>Monitor for delivery issues only</li>
                                <li>Check that conversion tracking is working</li>
                                <li>Review placement report for brand safety</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white"> Week 3-4: Optimization</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li>Pause bottom 20% of placements</li>
                                <li>Increase bids on top-performing audiences</li>
                                <li>Add negative keywords</li>
                                <li>Test new ad variations</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark"> Week 5+: Scaling</div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li>Increase budget by 20-30%</li>
                                <li>Switch to Target CPA (if 50+ conversions)</li>
                                <li>Add new audience segments</li>
                                <li>Create lookalike audiences from converters</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 12: COMMON MISTAKES ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> 10 Common Video Campaign Setup Mistakes</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Mistake</th>
                            <th>Consequence</th>
                            <th>How to Fix</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No hook in first 5 seconds</td>
                            <td>80%+ skip rate, wasted spend</td>
                            <td>Hook in first 3-5 seconds with question or bold statement</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Targeting too broad</td>
                            <td>Low relevance, high CPV</td>
                            <td>Start with custom intent or in-market audiences</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No frequency caps</td>
                            <td>Ad fatigue, negative brand sentiment</td>
                            <td>Set 3-5 impressions per user/week</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Not using remarketing lists</td>
                            <td>Missing high-intent audience</td>
                            <td>Create website visitor and YouTube engagement lists</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Wrong bidding strategy</td>
                            <td>Overpaying or under-delivering</td>
                            <td>Start with Target CPV, switch to Target CPA after conversions</td>
                        </tr>
                        <td>
                            <td>No companion banner</td>
                            <td>Missed ad placements (desktop only)</td>
                            <td>Create 300x250 banner with logo and CTA</td>
                        </tr>
                        </tr>
                            <td>No clear CTA overlay</td>
                            <td>Users don't know what to do next</td>
                            <td>Add CTA with action verb and urgency</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Video too long without value</td>
                            <td>High drop-off rate</td>
                            <td>Keep under 30 seconds, deliver value in first 10</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No captions/subtitles</td>
                            <td>85% of mobile viewers miss message</td>
                            <td>Add YouTube captions or burned-in subtitles</td>
                        </tr>
                        </tr>
                            <td>Ignoring placement reports</td>
                            <td>Wasting budget on irrelevant channels</td>
                            <td>Review and exclude poor placements weekly</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 13: QUICK REFERENCE CHEAT SHEET ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> YouTube Campaign Setup Cheat Sheet</h3>
            
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong> Campaign Level:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>• Budget: $10-50/day</li>
                                <li>• Bidding: Target CPV $0.02-0.03 (start)</li>
                                <li>• Location: Presence targeting</li>
                                <li>• Frequency cap: 3-5/week</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong> Ad Group Level:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>• Targeting: 1-2 methods per ad group</li>
                                <li>• Start with in-market + remarketing</li>
                                <li>• Separate ad groups by audience intent</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong> Ad Level:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>• Hook in first 5 seconds</li>
                                <li>• Add captions</li>
                                <li>• Include CTA overlay</li>
                                <li>• Companion banner (300x250)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
     </div>
</div>
