            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> When to Use Which Format? (Decision Flowchart)</h3>
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <p><strong> Choose Skippable In-Stream when:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>✓ Your goal is brand awareness or consideration</li>
                                <li>✓ You have a compelling story that needs 15-30 seconds</li>
                                <li>✓ You want to pay only for engaged viewers</li>
                                <li>✓ You plan to remarket to video viewers later</li>
                                <li>✓ You need to demonstrate product features</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <p><strong> Choose Non-Skippable In-Stream when:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>✓ Your message is short and punchy (≤15 seconds)</li>
                                <li>✓ Message completion is critical (e.g., legal disclaimers, safety info, flash sale)</li>
                                <li>✓ You have high brand recall goals</li>
                                <li>✓ Budget allows for CPM model</li>
                                <li>✓ You want guaranteed reach</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="row mt-3">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <p><strong> Choose In-Feed (Discovery) Ads when:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>✓ Your goal is <strong>leads or conversions</strong> (direct response)</li>
                                <li>✓ Users are actively searching for solutions like yours</li>
                                <li>✓ You have a <strong>compelling thumbnail and headline</strong></li>
                                <li>✓ You want to capture high-intent traffic at lower CPC</li>
                                <li>✓ You're promoting educational content or tutorials</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <p><strong> Choose Shorts Ads when:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>✓ Your target audience is <strong>Gen Z or young millennials</strong></li>
                                <li>✓ You want the <strong>lowest possible CPV</strong> for awareness</li>
                                <li>✓ You have vertical, fast-paced video content</li>
                                <li>✓ You're promoting <strong>app installs or mobile-first offers</strong></li>
                                <li>✓ You can follow trends and create reactive content</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

