            <!-- ==================== SECTION 6: COMMON MISTAKES & FIXES ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> 12 Common YouTube Format Mistakes & How to Fix Them</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Mistake</th>
                            <th>Consequence</th>
                            <th>How to Fix</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Using non-skippable for complex messages</strong></td>
                            <td>High drop-off (can't skip), negative brand perception</strong></td>
                            <td>Switch to skippable in-stream + end screen CTA</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No hook in first 5 seconds (skippable/Shorts)</strong></td>
                            <td>80%+ skip rate, wasted ad spend</strong></td>
                            <td>Start with question, bold statement, or visual hook in first 3 seconds</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>In-feed without custom thumbnail</strong></td>
                            <td>CPC increases 40-60%, low CTR (1-2% vs 4-6%)</strong></td>
                            <td>A/B test 4 custom thumbnails before launch</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Shorts ad with horizontal assets</strong></td>
                            <td>70% of frame is black bars → rejected or poor performance</strong></td>
                            <td>Reshoot vertical or use YouTube's Smart Crop tool</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No captions on any format</strong></td>
                            <td>85% of mobile viewers watch without sound → miss message</strong></td>
                            <td>Add burned-in captions or upload SRT file to YouTube</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Targeting only broad audiences for all formats</strong></td>
                            <td>Low relevance, high CPV/CPC, poor conversion rates</strong></td>
                            <td>Use remarketing for in-feed; use layered targeting for in-stream</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No frequency caps</strong></td>
                            <td>Ad fatigue, brand hatred, wasted impressions</strong></td>
                            <td>Set 3-5 impressions per user/week (prospecting), 2-3/week (remarketing)</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        </tr>
                            <td>Using the same creative for 3+ months</strong></td>
                            <td>Declining CTR, ad fatigue, lower conversion rates</strong></td>
                            <td>Refresh creative every 4-6 weeks; test new hooks and CTAs</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No end screen or cards on skippable in-stream</strong></td>
                            <td>Missed opportunity for clicks (CTR 50% lower)</strong></td>
                            <td>Always add end screen with CTA and companion banner</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Skipping A/B testing</strong></td>
                            <td>Never finding winning creative, leaving money on table</strong></td>
                            <td>Run 2-3 creative variations simultaneously; let Google optimize</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 7: QUICK REFERENCE CHEAT SHEET ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> YouTube Format Quick Reference Cheat Sheet</h3>
            
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <strong> Skippable In-Stream</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>Hook in <strong>5 sec</strong></li>
                                <li><strong>15-30 sec</strong> length</li>
                                <li>CPV <strong>$0.01-0.03</strong></li>
                                <li>Add end screen + CTA</li>
                                <li>Remarket to 25%+ viewers</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <strong>⛔ Non-Skippable</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li><strong>≤15 sec</strong> only</li>
                                <li>Single punchy message</li>
                                <li>CPM <strong>$4-8</strong></li>
                                <li>Brand recall goal</li>
                                <li>No mid-roll placement</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <strong> In-Feed (Discovery)</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li><strong>Custom thumbnail</strong> is critical</li>
                                <li>CPC <strong>$0.10-0.30</strong></li>
                                <li>High-intent users</li>
                                <li>Leads & conversions goal</li>
                                <li>60-120 sec video</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3">
                            <strong>📲 Shorts Ads</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li><strong>9:16 vertical</strong> only</li>
                                <li><strong>15-30 sec</strong> optimal</li>
                                <li>CPV <strong>$0.005-0.02</strong></li>
                                <li>Gen Z audience</li>
                                <li>Fast pacing (cut every 2-3s)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 8: SUMMARY ==================== -->
            <div class="alert alert-success mt-4">
                <h3 class="fw-bold"> Himanshu Shekhar's Summary for Section 10.8</h3>
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="col-md-3">
                        <strong> Skippable In-Stream</strong>
                        <ul class="small mb-0">
                            <li>Awareness + Consideration</li>
                            <li>Pay only for engaged viewers</li>
                            <li>Hook in first 5 seconds</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-3">
                        <strong>⛔ Non-Skippable</strong>
                        <ul class="small mb-0">
                            <li>Guaranteed delivery</li>
                            <li>Keep under 15 seconds</li>
                            <li>Best for brand recall</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-3">
                        <strong> In-Feed</strong>
                        <ul class="small mb-0">
                            <li>Highest intent format</li>
                            <li>Thumbnail is everything</li>
                            <li>Best for leads/conversions</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-3">
                        <strong>📲 Shorts Ads</strong>
                        <ul class="small mb-0">
                            <li>Lowest CPV</li>
                            <li>Gen Z reach</li>
                            <li>Vertical, fast-paced</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <hr>
                <p class="mb-0"><strong> Pro Strategy:</strong> Combine all three in a funnel: <strong>Awareness (Skippable + Shorts) → Consideration (In-Feed) → Conversion (Non-Skippable)</strong>. This 3-layer approach delivers <strong>2.8x higher ROAS</strong> than single-format campaigns.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-primary mt-2">
                <strong> Himanshu's Final Word:</strong> The biggest mistake advertisers make is using the wrong format for their goal. Before launching any YouTube campaign, ask yourself: <strong>"What is the user's mindset right now?"</strong> 
                <ul class="mt-2 mb-0">
                    <li> Passively watching entertainment? → <strong>Skippable In-Stream or Shorts</strong></li>
                    <li>🔍 Actively searching for solutions? → <strong>In-Feed Ads</strong></li>
                    <li> Ready to buy but need a reminder? → <strong>Non-Skippable (6-10 sec)</strong></li>
                </ul>
                <strong class="mt-2 d-block">Match format to mindset, and you'll win.</strong>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</div>
                         <hr class="border border-dark border-5">
                         @include('frontend.service.partials.in-article-ads')
                         <!-- ========== 16 YOUTUBE TARGETING STRATEGIES (AUTHORITY DEEP DIVE) ========== -->
<div class="section" id="topic-16">
    <div class="card mb-4 border">
        <div class="card-header bg-white py-3">
            <h2 class="mb-0">16 YouTube Targeting Strategies (Audience, Keyword, Topic & Placement) </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">

            <div class="alert alert-light border mb-4">
                <strong> Four powerful layers to pinpoint your ideal viewers.</strong> Combine them for precision or use one at a time for broader reach. This authoritative guide covers every targeting method, when to use each, and how to layer them for maximum ROI.
            </div>

            <p>YouTube offers multiple targeting layers that can be used individually or combined. The key to success is understanding which targeting method matches your campaign goal and user intent. Using the wrong targeting—like broad affinity audiences for a conversion campaign—will drain your budget with zero ROI.</p>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 1: TARGETING TIERS & INTENT LEVELS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Targeting Tiers by User Intent (From Broadest to Highest Intent)</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Intent Tier</th>
                            <th>Targeting Method</th>
                            <th>User Mindset</th>
                            <th>Best For</th>
                            <th>Expected Conversion Rate</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-secondary">Tier 5 (Broadest)</span></td>
                            <td><strong>Demographics + Geography</strong></td>
                            <td>Passive browsing</td>
                            <td>Brand awareness, reach campaigns</td>
                            <td>0.1-0.5%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-info">Tier 4</span></td>
                            <td><strong>Affinity Audiences</strong></td>
                            <td>Long-term interest (hobby/passion)</td>
                            <td>Top-of-funnel awareness</td>
                            <td>0.3-1%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-primary">Tier 3</span></td>
                            <td><strong>Topic Targeting</strong></td>
                            <td>Contextual relevance (what they're watching)</td>
                            <td>Contextual brand safety + relevance</td>
                            <td>0.5-1.5%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-warning">Tier 2</span></td>
                            <td><strong>Custom Intent / Custom Affinity</strong></td>
                            <td>Actively consuming related content</td>
                            <td>Consideration, mid-funnel</td>
                            <td>1-3%</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-success">Tier 1 (Highest Intent)</span></td>
                            <td><strong>In-Market Audiences + Remarketing + Placement (Competitor)</strong></td>
                            <td>Ready to buy / already engaged</td>
                            <td>Conversions, bottom-of-funnel</td>
                            <td>3-10% (remarketing 5-15%)</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 2: AUDIENCE TARGETING (DEEP DIVE) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Audience Targeting - Complete Deep Dive</h3>
            
            <div class="alert alert-info mb-3">
                <strong> Definition:</strong> Target users based on who they are, what they're interested in, and how they've behaved online.
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0"> Demographics Targeting</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>What you can target:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Age:</strong> 13-17, 18-24, 25-34, 35-44, 45-54, 55-64, 65+</li>
                                <li><strong>Gender:</strong> Male, Female, Unknown</li>
                                <li><strong>Parental Status:</strong> Parent, Not a parent</li>
                                <li><strong>Household Income:</strong> Top 10%, 11-20%, 21-30%, 31-40%, 41-50%, Bottom 50%</li>
                                <li><strong>Education:</strong> In college, College graduate, Some college, etc.</li>
                                <li><strong>Employment:</strong> Employed, Unemployed, Student, Retired</li>
                            </ul>
                            <hr>
                            <p><strong>Best Practice:</strong> Start with broad age ranges (e.g., 18-65), then narrow based on performance data after 2-3 weeks.</p>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Example:</strong> A retirement planning service → Target Age 55+, Income Top 30%
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">❤ Affinity Audiences (Long-term Interests)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>What it is:</strong> People with a <strong>passionate, long-term interest</strong> in a topic. These are lifestyle-based audiences.</p>
                            <p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li> Fitness Buffs & Health Nuts</li>
                                <li> Foodies & Home Chefs</li>
                                <li> Tech Enthusiasts</li>
                                <li> Frequent Travelers</li>
                                <li> Gamers</li>
                                <li> Business Professionals</li>
                                <li> Home & Garden Enthusiasts</li>
                                <li> Auto Enthusiasts</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p><strong>Best For:</strong> Top-of-funnel brand awareness, reaching new audiences who may not know your product yet.</p>
                            <div class="alert alert-warning small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Caution:</strong> Affinity audiences have lower intent. Don't expect direct conversions. Use for awareness then remarket.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
                            <h4 class="mb-0"> In-Market Audiences (Purchase Intent)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>What it is:</strong> Users actively researching products/services and <strong>showing strong purchase intent</strong> (searching, comparing, reading reviews).</p>
                            <p><strong>Examples:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li> Running Shoes & Apparel</li>
                                <li> Laptops & Computers</li>
                                <li> New Vehicles</li>
                                <li> Real Estate (Buying)</li>
                                <li> Credit Cards</li>
                                <li> Investment & Trading</li>
                                <li> Health Insurance</li>
                                <li> Vacation Packages</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p><strong>Best For:</strong> <span class="badge bg-success">Bottom-of-funnel conversions</span> – highest intent non-remarketing audience.</p>
                            <div class="alert alert-success small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> In-market audiences convert 2-5x better than affinity audiences.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-danger text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0"> Custom Audiences (Your Own Segments)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>What it is:</strong> Build your own audience based on <strong>keywords, URLs, apps, or YouTube content</strong> your ideal customer engages with.</p>
                            <p><strong>Types of Custom Audiences:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Custom Intent:</strong> Keywords people search + URLs they visit → Highest intent</li>
                                <li><strong>Custom Affinity:</strong> Keywords + URLs + apps → Broader interest-based</li>
                                <li><strong>YouTube Custom Audience:</strong> Specific channels, videos, or keywords</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p><strong>How to Build (Custom Intent):</strong></p>
                            <pre class="bg-light p-2 small rounded">Keywords: "best CRM software", "CRM for small business", "Salesforce alternative"
URLs: competitor websites, review sites, comparison pages
Apps: business-related apps your audience uses</pre>
                            <div class="alert alert-info small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Custom intent audiences often outperform in-market by 20-40% because you define exactly what signals matter.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-secondary text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0"> Remarketing (Highest Intent - Your Own Data)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>What it is:</strong> Target users who have <strong>already interacted with your brand</strong> – website, YouTube channel, or app.</p>
                            <p><strong>YouTube Remarketing Audience Types (by intent level):</strong></p>
                            <div class="table-responsive">
                            <table class="table table-sm">
                                <thead class="table-light">
                                    <tr><th>Audience</th><th>Intent Level</th><th>Best Use</th></tr>
                                </thead>
                                <tbody>
                                    <tr><td>Cart Abandoners (website)</td><td><span class="badge bg-success">Highest</span></td><td>Discount codes, urgency ads</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Website Purchasers (exclude!)</td><td><span class="badge bg-secondary">Exclude</span></td><td>Don't show ads to converters</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Website Visitors (All)</td><td><span class="badge bg-warning">High</span></td><td>Brand reinforcement</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>YouTube 100% Viewers</td><td><span class="badge bg-warning">High</span></td><td>Full offer, testimonial</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>YouTube 75% Viewers</td><td><span class="badge bg-info">Medium-High</span></td><td>Second video in sequence</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>YouTube 25% Viewers</td><td><span class="badge bg-secondary">Medium</span></td><td>Broad remarketing</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>YouTube Channel Visitors</td><td><span class="badge bg-secondary">Medium</span></td><td>Promote new videos</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-dark text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0"> Customer Match & Similar Audiences</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Customer Match:</strong> Upload your own customer email list (hashed). Target existing customers for upsell/cross-sell.</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Requirements:</strong> List of 1,000+ email addresses</li>
                                <li><strong>Best For:</strong> Loyalty campaigns, repeat purchases, win-back offers</li>
                            </ul>
                            <hr>
                            <p><strong>Similar Audiences (Lookalike):</strong> YouTube finds users with similar behaviours to your existing customers or remarketing lists.</p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Source:</strong> Any remarketing list of 1,000+ users</li>
                                <li><strong>Best For:</strong> Scaling successful remarketing campaigns to new prospects</li>
                                <li><strong>Size control:</strong> 1% (most similar) to 10% (broadest)</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-success small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Create a "Similar to Converters" audience from your purchase remarketing list. This is often the highest-performing prospecting audience.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 3: KEYWORD TARGETING (DEEP DIVE) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">🔍 Keyword Targeting - Complete Deep Dive</h3>
            
            <div class="alert alert-info mb-3">
                <strong> Definition:</strong> Show your video ads when users search for specific terms on YouTube (just like Google Search ads, but for YouTube search results and suggested videos).
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>How Keyword Targeting Works on YouTube:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Your ad appears in <strong>YouTube search results</strong> (when someone searches) and <strong>suggested videos</strong> (based on video content matching keywords)</li>
                                <li><strong>NOT:</strong> Showing ads based on the viewer's Google web searches (that's different)</li>
                                <li><strong>Match Types:</strong> Broad match, Phrase match, Exact match (same as Google Search)</li>
                            </ul>
                            <hr>
                            <p><strong>Match Type Examples:</strong></p>
                            <div class="table-responsive">
                            <table class="table table-sm">
                                <thead class="table-light"><tr><th>Match Type</th><th>Example</th><th>Matches</th></tr></thead>
                                <tbody>
                                    <tr><td>Broad</td><td><code>running shoes</code></td><td>best running shoes, buy running shoes online</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Phrase</td><td><code>"running shoes"</code></td><td>best running shoes, cheap running shoes</td></tr>
                                    <tr><td>Exact</td><td><code>[running shoes]</code></td><td>running shoes (only)</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Best Practices for YouTube Keywords:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li> Use <strong>phrase match</strong> for most campaigns (balance of reach + relevance)</li>
                                <li> Include <strong>long-tail keywords</strong> (4+ words) for lower CPC</li>
                                <li> Add <strong>negative keywords</strong> to exclude irrelevant searches (e.g., "free", "cheap", "review" if you're selling premium)</li>
                                <li> Target <strong>intent-based keywords</strong> not just informational</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-warning small mt-2">
                                 <strong>Important:</strong> Keyword targeting on YouTube is <strong>lower volume than Google Search</strong> but has <strong>higher intent than affinity audiences</strong>. Best for consideration campaigns.
                            </div>
                            <hr>
                            <p><strong>Example Keyword Groups for "Project Management Software":</strong></p>
                            <pre class="bg-light p-2 small rounded">"best project management software"
"project management tools comparison"
"how to manage remote teams"
"asana vs trello vs jira"
"project management for small business"</pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 4: TOPIC TARGETING (DEEP DIVE) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Topic Targeting - Complete Deep Dive</h3>
            
            <div class="alert alert-info mb-3">
                <strong> Definition:</strong> Target entire content categories on YouTube. Your ads will appear on any video that Google classifies under that topic.
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>How Topic Targeting Works:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Google analyzes video <strong>title, description, tags, and transcript</strong> to assign topics</li>
                                <li>Your ad appears on <strong>all videos within that topic category</strong> (can be millions of videos)</li>
                                <li><strong>No control over specific videos</strong> – you get the whole category</li>
                            </ul>
                            <hr>
                            <p><strong>Example Topics (Hierarchical):</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Sports → Cricket → IPL</li>
                                <li>Technology → Software → Project Management</li>
                                <li>Travel → Adventure Travel → Trekking</li>
                                <li>Education → Online Learning → Digital Marketing</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Best For:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li> <strong>Brand awareness campaigns</strong> (broad reach within relevant content)</li>
                                <li> <strong>Contextual relevance</strong> – your ad appears in the right environment</li>
                                <li> <strong>Brand safety</strong> – avoid controversial channels while staying relevant</li>
                                <li> <strong>Video discovery</strong> – get your brand in front of engaged viewers</li>
                            </ul>
                            <hr>
                            <p><strong>Limitations:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li> <strong>No placement control</strong> – you can't exclude specific videos (only topics)</li>
                                <li> <strong>Broad targeting</strong> – lower intent than keywords or in-market</li>
                                <li> <strong>Topic assignment isn't perfect</strong> – some videos may be misclassified</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Use topic targeting as a <strong>layer</strong> with other targeting methods (e.g., In-Market + Topic = higher relevance).
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 5: PLACEMENT TARGETING (DEEP DIVE) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Placement Targeting - Complete Deep Dive</h3>
            
            <div class="alert alert-info mb-3">
                <strong> Definition:</strong> Manually select specific YouTube channels, individual videos, or mobile apps where you want your ads to appear. <strong>Maximum control, highest precision.</strong>
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Types of Placements You Can Target:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong> YouTube Channels:</strong> <code>youtube.com/channel/UCxxx</code> or <code>youtube.com/@channelname</code></li>
                                <li><strong> Individual YouTube Videos:</strong> <code>youtube.com/watch?v=VIDEO_ID</code></li>
                                <li><strong> Mobile Apps:</strong> Specific apps on the Google Display Network</li>
                                <li><strong> Websites:</strong> Specific websites (for video partners)</li>
                            </ul>
                            <hr>
                            <p><strong>Best For:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li> <strong>Competitor conquesting</strong> – target competitor YouTube channels</li>
                                <li> <strong>Influencer partnerships</strong> – advertise on your sponsored creator's videos</li>
                                <li> <strong>Highly targeted B2B</strong> – target industry-specific channels</li>
                                <li> <strong>Brand safety control</strong> – only show ads on channels you trust</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>How to Find Placements:</strong></p>
                            <ol>
                                <li>Search YouTube for relevant channels/videos in your niche</li>
                                <li>Use tools like <strong>VidIQ, TubeBuddy, or Social Blade</strong> to find top channels</li>
                                <li>Run an <strong>automatic placement campaign</strong> first, then add top performers as managed placements</li>
                                <li>Check <strong>placement reports</strong> weekly for new opportunities</li>
                            </ol>
                            <hr>
                            <p><strong>Competitor Channel Targeting Example:</strong></p>
                            <pre class="bg-light p-2 small rounded"># If you sell CRM software, target:
youtube.com/@Salesforce
youtube.com/@HubSpot
youtube.com/@ZohoCRM
youtube.com/@Pipedrive</pre>
                            <div class="alert alert-success small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Start with <strong>automatic placements</strong> for 1-2 weeks to collect data, then add top 10-20 placements as <strong>managed placements</strong> and increase bids by 20-50%.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 6: TARGETING LAYERING STRATEGIES ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Targeting Layering Strategies (How to Combine for Maximum Precision)</h3>
            
            <div class="alert alert-primary mb-3">
                <strong> Understanding "AND" vs "OR" Logic:</strong>
                <ul class="mb-0 mt-2">
                    <li><strong>AND logic (Layered targeting):</strong> User must match <strong>ALL</strong> criteria → <strong>Narrower reach, higher relevance</strong></li>
                    <li><strong>OR logic (Separate ad groups):</strong> User matches <strong>ANY</strong> criteria → <strong>Broader reach, collect data</strong></li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Strategy 1: Layered (AND) - High Precision</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Formula:</strong> Audience + Topic + Keyword/Placement</p>
                            <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-2 small rounded">In-Market "Running Shoes" 
+ Topic "Sports & Fitness" 
+ Keyword "marathon training"</pre>
                            <p><strong>Result:</strong> Ads only shown to running shoe buyers watching sports/fitness videos about marathon training.</p>
                            <p><strong>Best For:</strong> Limited budgets, high-value products, B2B</p>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Expected Reach:</strong> Small (1,000-100,000)
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Strategy 2: Observation (Test First)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Formula:</strong> Set audiences as "Observation" (not targeting)</p>
                            <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-2 small rounded">Campaign targeting: Broad (Topic only)
Observation audiences:
- In-Market Running Shoes
- Affinity Fitness Buffs
- Custom Intent (competitors)</pre>
                            <p><strong>Result:</strong> Campaign runs broadly, but you collect performance data on each audience segment.</p>
                            <p><strong>Best For:</strong> New campaigns, testing new audiences, data collection</p>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>After 2 weeks:</strong> Move top 1-2 audiences to targeting (AND logic) with increased bids.
