            <!-- ==================== SECTION 6: FREQUENCY CAPPING FOR REMARKETING ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Frequency Capping for Remarketing (Critical to Avoid Ad Fatigue)</h3>
            
            <div class="alert alert-warning mb-4">
                <strong> Warning:</strong> Remarketing without frequency caps is dangerous. Showing the same ad 20+ times creates <strong>negative brand sentiment</strong> and <strong>ad fatigue</strong>. Users will block your ads or develop hatred for your brand.
            </div>

            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Audience Type</th>
                            <th>Recommended Frequency Cap</th>
                            <th>Time Period</th>
                            <th>Why</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Cart Abandoners</td>
                            <td><strong>5-7 impressions</strong></td>
                            <td>Per week</strong></td>
                            <td>High intent needs reminders, but too many = annoying</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Product Page Viewers</td>
                            <td><strong>3-5 impressions</strong></td>
                            <td>Per week</strong></td>
                            <td>Enough to stay top-of-mind, not enough to annoy</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>All Website Visitors (Top Funnel)</td>
                            <td><strong>2-3 impressions</strong></td>
                            <td>Per week</strong></td>
                            <td>Lighter touch for cold remarketing</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Past Purchasers (Upsell)</td>
                            <td><strong>1-2 impressions</strong></td>
                            <td>Per week</strong></td>
                            <td>Very light touch – they already bought</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>YouTube Engagers</td>
                            <td><strong>3-5 impressions</strong></td>
                            <td>Per week</strong></td>
                            <td>Balanced reminder without overexposure</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 7: EXCLUSION LISTS (CRITICAL) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Exclusion Lists: The Most Overlooked Remarketing Strategy</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="alert alert-danger mb-3">
                        <strong> Critical Rule:</strong> <strong>Always exclude converters from your remarketing lists.</strong> If you don't, you'll keep showing ads to people who already bought – wasting budget and annoying your best customers.
                    </div>
                    
                    <h4> How to Create Exclusion Lists:</h4>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Create a remarketing list of <strong>converters</strong> (purchasers, form submitters)</li>
                        <li>Go to your remarketing campaign → Audiences → <strong>Exclusions</strong></li>
                        <li>Add the converter list as an <strong>exclusion</strong></li>
                        <li>Repeat for all remarketing campaigns</li>
                    </ol>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-3"> Recommended Exclusion Lists for Every Campaign:</h4>
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered">
                            <thead class="table-light">
                                <tr><th>Exclusion List</th><th>Membership Duration</th><th>Why Exclude</th></tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Past Purchasers (last 30 days)</strong></td>
                                    <td>30 days</strong></td>
                                    <td>Avoid showing ads to recent buyers (unless upsell)</strong></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Form Submitters</strong></td>
                                    <td>30 days</strong></td>
                                    <td>Don't ask for same lead twice</strong></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Low-Quality Traffic (bounced visitors)</strong></td>
                                    <td>7 days</strong></td>
                                    <td>Don't waste budget on users who left immediately</strong></td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 8: REMARKETING BID STRATEGIES ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Remarketing Bid Strategies (How Much to Spend)</h3>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Recommended Bid Adjustments by Audience</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <div class="table-responsive">
                                <table class="table table-sm">
                                    <thead class="table-light">
                                        <tr><th>Audience</th><th>Bid Adjustment (vs Prospecting)</th></tr>
                                    </thead>
                                    <tbody>
                                        <tr>
                                            <td>Cart Abandoners</strong></td>
