                         <!-- ========== 19 VIDEO SEQUENCING & AD FREQUENCY MANAGEMENT (AUTHORITY DEEP DIVE) ========== -->
<div class="section" id="topic-19">
    <div class="card mb-4 border">
        <div class="card-header bg-white py-3">
            <h2 class="mb-0">19 Video Sequencing & Ad Frequency Management</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">

            <div class="alert alert-light border mb-4">
                <strong> Tell a story across multiple videos – and don't annoy your audience.</strong> Sequencing improves message retention by 40-60%, and frequency caps prevent ad fatigue. This authoritative guide covers both strategies in depth.
            </div>

            <p>Two of the most underutilized features in YouTube advertising are <strong>video sequencing</strong> (telling a story across multiple ads) and <strong>frequency capping</strong> (controlling how often users see your ads). Used correctly, they dramatically improve performance. Used incorrectly, they waste budget and damage brand perception.</p>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 1: WHAT IS VIDEO SEQUENCING ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> What is Video Sequencing? (Complete Overview)</h3>
            
            <div class="alert alert-info mb-3">
                <strong> Definition:</strong> Video sequencing allows you to show a series of video ads in a specific order. A user sees Video 2 <strong>only after</strong> they have completed Video 1 (watched 30 seconds, watched entire ad, or clicked). This creates a logical narrative arc across multiple touchpoints.
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0"> Benefits of Video Sequencing</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>40-60% higher message retention</strong> vs single-video campaigns</li>
                                <li><strong>2-3x higher conversion rates</strong> for sequenced remarketing</li>
                                <li><strong>Builds narrative arc</strong> – problem → solution → urgency</li>
                                <li><strong>Prevents message overload</strong> – one idea per video</li>
                                <li><strong>Increases brand recall</strong> through repetition with variation</li>
                                <li><strong>Reduces ad fatigue</strong> because users see different creatives</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
                            <h4 class="mb-0"> Limitations of Video Sequencing</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Only works for skippable in-stream ads</strong> (not non-skippable, bumper, discovery, or Shorts)</li>
                                <li><strong>Requires multiple video creatives</strong> (higher production cost)</li>
                                <li><strong>Longer learning phase</strong> – more data needed to optimize</li>
                                <li><strong>Smaller reach</strong> – users must see first video to see second</li>
                                <li><strong>Not available for all campaign subtypes</strong> – works best with Video Views or Video Action campaigns</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 2: SEQUENCING FRAMEWORKS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Video Sequencing Frameworks (Proven Structures)</h3>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100 border-primary">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Framework 1: Problem-Solution-Urgency (3-Video)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Best for:</strong> SaaS, B2B, high-consideration products</p>
                            <pre class="bg-light p-2 small rounded">
Video 1 (15s - Problem):
"Teams waste 20 hours/week on manual reporting."

Video 2 (30s - Solution):
"Our tool automates reporting in 5 minutes. Here's how it works..."

Video 3 (15s - Urgency):
"Try free for 14 days. Limited spots. Link below."</pre>
                            <div class="alert alert-success small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Expected ROI:</strong> 2-3x higher conversion than single ad
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100 border-success">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Framework 2: Hook-Explain-Demo (3-Video)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Physical products, e-commerce, demonstrations</p>
                            <pre class="bg-light p-2 small rounded">
Video 1 (6s - Hook):
"Meet the smartest running shoe ever made."

Video 2 (20s - Explain):
"Built-in sensors track stride, cadence, and impact. Reduce injury by 40%."

Video 3 (15s - Demo):
"Watch how it works in real-time. Shop now with free returns."</pre>
                            <div class="alert alert-success small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Expected ROI:</strong> 1.8-2.5x higher CTR than single ad
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100 border-warning">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Framework 3: Teaser-Feature-Offer (3-Video)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Product launches, event promotions, limited offers</p>
                            <pre class="bg-light p-2 small rounded">
Video 1 (6s - Teaser):
"Something big is coming. Watch this space."

Video 2 (15s - Feature):
"Introducing Product X. The feature everyone asked for."

Video 3 (10s - Offer):
"Launch week: 30% off. Use code LAUNCH30. Shop now."</pre>
                            <div class="alert alert-success small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Expected ROI:</strong> 3-4x higher conversion for launch campaigns
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100 border-info">
                        <div class="card-header bg-info text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Framework 4: Awareness-Consideration-Conversion (3-Video)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Full-funnel campaigns, brand building</p>
                            <pre class="bg-light p-2 small rounded">
Video 1 (15s - Awareness):
"80% of small businesses struggle with cash flow."

Video 2 (20s - Consideration):
"Our software helps you forecast cash flow 6 months ahead."

Video 3 (10s - Conversion):
"Start your free trial today. No credit card required."</pre>
                            <div class="alert alert-success small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Best for:</strong> Businesses with longer sales cycles
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100 border-secondary">
                        <div class="card-header bg-secondary text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Framework 5: Testimonial-Proof-CTA (3-Video)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Trust-building, social proof campaigns</p>
                            <pre class="bg-light p-2 small rounded">
Video 1 (10s - Testimonial):
Customer: "This changed my business forever."

Video 2 (15s - Proof):
"10,000+ happy customers. Rated 4.9/5 on G2."

Video 3 (10s - CTA):
"Join them today. Free trial. Link below."</pre>
                            <div class="alert alert-success small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Expected ROI:</strong> 2-3x higher trust signals
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100 border-danger">
                        <div class="card-header bg-danger text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Framework 6: Educational Series (4-5 Videos)</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Courses, tutorials, authority building</p>
                            <pre class="bg-light p-2 small rounded">
Video 1: "Day 1: The biggest mistake beginners make"
Video 2: "Day 2: The 5-minute fix that changes everything"
Video 3: "Day 3: Advanced strategy for pros"
Video 4: "Day 4: Case study – real results"
Video 5: "Day 5: Full course access – limited time offer"</pre>
                            <div class="alert alert-success small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Expected ROI:</strong> 4-5x higher engagement for educational content
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 3: STEP-BY-STEP SEQUENCING SETUP ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Step-by-Step: How to Set Up Video Sequencing in Google Ads</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h4> Prerequisites:</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li>✓ All videos must be uploaded to YouTube (unlisted or public)</li>
                        <li>✓ Campaign type: <strong>Video Views</strong> or <strong>Video Action</strong></li>
                        <li>✓ Ad format: <strong>Skippable in-stream</strong> (sequencing doesn't work with other formats)</li>
                    </ul>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-4"> Step-by-Step Setup:</h4>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Create a new <strong>Video campaign</strong> → Choose <strong>Video Views</strong> or <strong>Video Action</strong></li>
                        <li>Set your budget, bidding, and targeting as usual</li>
                        <li>Go to <strong>Ad group level</strong> → Click on <strong>"Ad sequencing"</strong></li>
                        <li>Click <strong>"Create sequence"</strong></li>
                        <li>Choose sequence type:
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Standard sequence:</strong> Videos play in fixed order (Video 1 → Video 2 → Video 3)</li>
                                <li><strong>Time-based sequence:</strong> Videos play after a set time delay (e.g., Video 2 shown 3 days after Video 1)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li>Add videos in order (minimum 2, maximum 5)</li>
                        <li>For each video, set <strong>completion condition</strong>:
                            <ul>
                                <li>Watched at least 30 seconds</li>
                                <li>Watched entire ad</li>
                                <li>Clicked on ad</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li>Set <strong>frequency caps</strong> for each video (see section below)</li>
                        <li>Click <strong>"Save"</strong> and launch campaign</li>
                    </ol>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                        <strong> Pro Tip:</strong> For best results, use <strong>Standard sequence</strong> with completion condition "Watched at least 30 seconds". This ensures users see the next video only after genuine engagement.
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-warning mt-3">
                        <strong> Important:</strong> Video sequencing <strong>does not work</strong> for:
                        <ul class="mb-0">
                            <li>Non-skippable in-stream ads</li>
                            <li>Bumper ads (6 seconds)</li>
                            <li>Discovery ads (in-feed)</li>
                            <li>Shorts ads</li>
                            <li>Outstream ads</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 4: FREQUENCY CAPPING (DEEP DIVE) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Frequency Capping: Complete Guide</h3>
            
            <div class="alert alert-info mb-3">
                <strong> Definition:</strong> Frequency capping limits how many times a user sees your ad within a specific time period (per day, per week, or per month). It prevents ad fatigue and protects your brand.
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100 bg-danger text-white">
                        <div class="card-body text-center">
                            <div class="display-4">20+</div>
                            <p class="mb-0">Impressions per user = <strong>Brand Hatred</strong></p>
                            <small>Users actively avoid your brand</small>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100 bg-warning text-dark">
                        <div class="card-body text-center">
                            <div class="display-4">10-20</div>
                            <p class="mb-0">Impressions per user = <strong>Ad Fatigue</strong></p>
                            <small>CTR drops, negative perception</small>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100 bg-success text-white">
                        <div class="card-body text-center">
                            <div class="display-4">3-7</div>
                            <p class="mb-0">Impressions per user = <strong>Optimal</strong></p>
                            <small>Maximum recall without annoyance</small>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Frequency Cap Recommendations by Campaign Type</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Campaign Type</th>
                            <th>Recommended Frequency Cap</th>
                            <th>Time Period</th>
                            <th>Why</th>
                            <th>Cost Impact</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Prospecting (Cold Audience)</strong></td>
                            <td><strong>3-5 impressions</strong></td>
                            <td>Per week</strong></td>
                            <td>Enough to create awareness, not enough to annoy</td>
                            <td>Optimizes CPV/CPM</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Remarketing (Warm Audience)</strong></td>
                            <td><strong>2-3 impressions</strong></td>
                            <td>Per week</td>
                            <td>Higher intent, less frequency needed</td>
                            <td>Reduces waste on already-interested users</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Brand Awareness</strong></td>
                            <td><strong>1-2 impressions</strong></td>
                            <td>Per day</td>
                             <td>Avoid over-saturation, protect brand perception</td>
                            <td>Maintains positive brand sentiment</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Bumper Ads (6 seconds)</strong></td>
                            <td><strong>5-7 impressions</strong></td>
                            <td>Per week</td>
                            <td>Short format, less intrusive</td>
                            <td>Higher frequency acceptable</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Non-Skippable Ads</td>
                            <td><strong>2-3 impressions</td>
                            <td>Per week</td>
                            <td>Forced view = higher annoyance risk</td>
                            <td>Lower frequency to protect brand</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Video Sequencing (Per Video)</strong></td>
                            <td><strong>2-3 impressions</strong></td>
                            <td>Per video, per week</td>
                            <td>Controls story pace, prevents repetition</strong></td>
                            <td>Improves narrative completion</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> How to Set Frequency Caps in Google Ads</h3>
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <ol>
                        <li>Go to your <strong>campaign settings</strong></li>
                        <li>Click on <strong>"Additional settings"</strong></li>
                        <li>Click <strong>"Frequency capping"</strong></li>
                        <li>Set limits:
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Impressions per day:</strong> e.g., 1-2 per day</li>
                                <li><strong>Impressions per week:</strong> e.g., 3-7 per week</li>
                                <li><strong>Impressions per month:</strong> e.g., 10-20 per month</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li>Choose scope:
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Per campaign:</strong> Applies only to this campaign</li>
                                <li><strong>Per ad group:</strong> Tighter control within campaign</li>
                            </ul>
                        </li>
                        <li>Click <strong>"Save"</strong></li>
                    </ol>
                    <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                        <strong> Pro Tip:</strong> Start with <strong>per week caps</strong> (easiest to measure). After 2-3 weeks, analyze frequency reports and adjust caps based on CTR drop-off data.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 5: COMBINING SEQUENCING + FREQUENCY CAPS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Combining Sequencing with Frequency Caps (Pro Strategy)</h3>
            
            <div class="card border-primary mb-4">
                <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                    <h4 class="mb-0"> Himanshu's Sequencing + Frequency Cap Framework</h4>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p>Use sequencing AND frequency caps together to control the story pace and prevent fatigue:</p>
                    
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Video in Sequence</th>
                                    <th>Frequency Cap</th>
                                    <th>Completion Condition</th>
                                    <th>Goal</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Video 1 (Problem)</strong></td>
                                    <td>Max 3 times/week</strong></td>
                                    <td>Watched 30s or clicked</strong></td>
                                    <td>Create awareness, identify pain point</strong></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Video 2 (Solution)</strong></td>
                                    <td>Max 2 times/week (after Video 1 completion)</strong></td>
                                    <td>Watched 30s or clicked</strong></td>
                                    <td>Educate on solution, build trust</strong></td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Video 3 (Urgency/CTA)</strong></td>
                                    <td>Max 2 times/week (after Video 2 completion)</strong></td>
                                    <td>Watched 30s or clicked</strong></td>
                                    <td>Drive conversion, offer urgency</strong></td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-success mt-3 mb-0">
                         <strong>Result:</strong> Users see a logical 3-part story over 1-2 weeks. No single video is shown more than 3 times. This maximizes completion rates while minimizing ad fatigue.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 6: FREQUENCY REPORT ANALYSIS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> How to Analyze Frequency Reports (Find the Drop-Off Point)</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p><strong>Where to find:</strong> Google Ads → Campaign → "Frequency" column (customize columns to add)</p>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-3"> How to Determine Your Optimal Frequency Cap:</h4>
                    <ol>
                        <li>Run campaign <strong>without frequency caps</strong> for 2-3 weeks</li>
                        <li>Export frequency report: <strong>Impressions per user</strong> vs <strong>CTR</strong></li>
                        <li>Find the point where <strong>CTR drops significantly</strong> (usually 5-10 impressions)</li>
                        <li>Set your frequency cap <strong>20-30% below that drop-off point</strong></li>
                    </ol>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                        <strong> Example Frequency Analysis:</strong>
                        <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-sm table-bordered">
                            <thead class="table-light">
                                <tr><th>Impressions per User</th><th>CTR</th><th>Action</th></tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>}<td>1-3</td><td>0.8%</td><td>Good – keep showing</td></tr>
                                <tr>}<td>4-6</td><td>0.7%</td><td>Good – keep showing</td></tr>
                                <tr>}<td>7-9</td><td>0.5%</td><td>Warning – CTR dropping</td></tr>
                                <tr>}<td>10-12</td><td>0.3%</td><td>Fatigue – reduce frequency</td></tr>
                                <tr>}<td>13+</td><td>0.1%</td><td>Critical – ad fatigue</td></tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                        </div>
                        <p class="mt-2 mb-0">→ Set frequency cap at <strong>7 impressions per week</strong> (20% below drop-off)</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 7: SEQUENCING BEST PRACTICES ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Video Sequencing Best Practices</h3>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">DO's</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul>
                                <li> <strong>Start short, end short:</strong> Video 1: 6-15s, Video 2: 15-30s, Video 3: 6-15s</li>
                                <li> <strong>One message per video:</strong> Don't cram everything into one</li>
                                <li> <strong>Use consistent branding:</strong> Same colors, logo, voice across all videos</li>
                                <li> <strong>Set logical completion conditions:</strong> 30s for most, "click" for high-intent</li>
                                <li> <strong>Test 2-video sequences first</strong> (easier to optimize)</li>
                                <li> <strong>Monitor drop-off between videos</strong> – if large drop, improve Video 1</li>
                                <li> <strong>Use frequency caps per video</strong> to control story pace</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-danger text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">DON'Ts</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul>
                                <li> <strong>Don't make videos too long</strong> – drop-off increases significantly after 30s</li>
                                <li> <strong>Don't repeat same message across videos</strong> – users will skip</li>
                                <li> <strong>Don't use sequencing for remarketing only</strong> – combine with prospecting</li>
                                <li> <strong>Don't set completion condition too strict</strong> – "watched entire ad" reduces reach</li>
                                <li> <strong>Don't use more than 5 videos</strong> – most users won't complete</li>
                                <li> <strong>Don't forget to exclude converters</strong> from sequence</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 8: FREQUENCY CAPPING BEST PRACTICES ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Frequency Capping Best Practices</h3>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">DO's</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul>
                                <li> <strong>Start with conservative caps</strong> (3-5/week) – you can always increase</li>
                                <li> <strong>Set caps at campaign level</strong> – consistent across ad groups</li>
                                <li> <strong>Lower caps for remarketing</strong> (2-3/week) – users already know you</li>
                                <li> <strong>Higher caps for bumper ads</strong> (5-7/week) – less intrusive</li>
                                <li> <strong>Review frequency reports weekly</strong> – adjust caps based on CTR drop-off</li>
                                <li> <strong>Use account-level exclusion lists</strong> for users who have seen ads 20+ times</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-danger text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">DON'Ts</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul>
                                <li> <strong>Don't run without caps</strong> – users will see ads 20+ times = brand hatred</li>
                                <li> <strong>Don't set caps too low</strong> – 1 impression/week won't create awareness</li>
                                <li> <strong>Don't use same caps for all campaign types</strong> – adjust by intent</li>
                                <li> <strong>Don't ignore device differences</strong> – mobile users may need lower caps</li>
                                <li> <strong>Don't forget to update caps</strong> as campaign performance changes</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 9: COMMON MISTAKES ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> 12 Common Sequencing & Frequency Management Mistakes</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Mistake</th>
                            <th>Consequence</th>
                            <th>How to Fix</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No frequency caps at all</td>
                            <td>Ad fatigue, brand hatred, wasted budget</td>
                            <td>Set caps immediately: 3-5/week for prospecting, 2-3/week for remarketing</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Caps set too low</td>
                            <td>Insufficient reach, no brand recall</td>
                            <td>Increase caps gradually (5→7→10) while monitoring CTR</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Using sequencing for non-skippable ads</td>
                            <td>Feature not supported, campaign won't work</td>
                            <td>Switch to skippable in-stream format</td>
                        </tr>
                        </tr>
                            <td>Videos in sequence too similar</td>
                            <td>Users skip after Video 1, low completion</td>
                            <td>Ensure each video has unique value (problem → solution → offer)</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No completion condition set</td>
                            <td>Sequence never advances, users stuck on Video 1</td>
                            <td>Set condition: "Watched at least 30 seconds"</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Sequence too long (5+ videos)</td>
                            <td>Most users drop off before completing</td>
                            <td>Limit to 2-3 videos for best completion</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Same frequency cap for all campaigns</td>
                            <td>Remarketing over-exposed, prospecting under-exposed</td>
                            <td>Adjust caps by campaign type and audience intent</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Not analyzing frequency reports</td>
                            <td>Unknown drop-off point, suboptimal caps</td>
                            <td>Review frequency vs CTR reports weekly</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Sequencing with discovery ads</td>
                            <td>Feature not supported</td>
                            <td>Use skippable in-stream for sequencing</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No exclusion of converters in sequences</td>
                            <td>Wasting budget on existing customers</td>
                            <td>Exclude converter lists from sequencing campaigns</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 10: QUICK REFERENCE CHEAT SHEET ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Quick Reference Cheat Sheet</h3>
            
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong> Sequencing Rules:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>Only for <strong>skippable in-stream</strong></li>
                                <li>2-5 videos per sequence</li>
                                <li>One message per video</li>
                                <li>Set completion condition (30s)</li>
                                <li>Use frequency caps per video</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong> Frequency Caps:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>Prospecting: <strong>3-5/week</strong></li>
                                <li>Remarketing: <strong>2-3/week</strong></li>
                                <li>Brand awareness: <strong>1-2/day</strong></li>
                                <li>Bumper ads: <strong>5-7/week</strong></li>
                                <li>Non-skippable: <strong>2-3/week</strong></li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong> Combined Strategy:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>Video 1: 3x/week cap</li>
                                <li>Video 2: 2x/week cap (post Video 1)</li>
                                <li>Video 3: 2x/week cap (post Video 2)</li>
                                <li>Analyze frequency reports weekly</li>
                                <li>Exclude converters from sequences</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 11: SUMMARY ==================== -->
            <div class="alert alert-success mt-4">
                <h3 class="fw-bold"> Himanshu Shekhar's Sequencing & Frequency Management Summary</h3>
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <strong> Video Sequencing Takeaways:</strong>
                        <ul class="small mb-0">
                            <li>Use <strong>3-video sequences</strong> (Problem → Solution → Urgency) for best results</li>
                            <li>Only works for <strong>skippable in-stream ads</strong></li>
                            <li>Set completion condition to <strong>"Watched at least 30 seconds"</strong></li>
                            <li>Keep first video <strong>6-15 seconds</strong> (hook quickly)</li>
                            <li>Test 2-video sequences before scaling to 3+</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <strong> Frequency Capping Takeaways:</strong>
                        <ul class="small mb-0">
                            <li><strong>Never run without caps</strong> – brand hatred is real</li>
                            <li>Prospecting: <strong>3-5 impressions/week</strong></li>
                            <li>Remarketing: <strong>2-3 impressions/week</strong></li>
                            <li>Analyze frequency reports weekly to find drop-off point</li>
                            <li>Combine caps with sequencing for maximum effectiveness</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <hr>
                <p class="mb-0"><strong> Himanshu's Pro Formula:</strong> <strong>3-Video Sequence + Frequency Caps (Video1: 3x, Video2: 2x, Video3: 2x per week) = 2.5x higher completion rates + 40% lower ad fatigue</strong></p>
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-primary mt-2">
                <strong> Himanshu's Final Word:</strong> Two of the most powerful tools in YouTube advertising are also the most underused. Video sequencing builds narrative and improves message retention. Frequency caps protect your brand and optimize spend. Use them together. Most advertisers don't. That's your competitive advantage.
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</div>
                         <hr class="border border-dark border-5">
