                         <!-- ========== 20 PLACEMENT EXCLUSIONS & BRAND SAFETY CONTROLS (AUTHORITY DEEP DIVE) ========== -->
<div class="section" id="topic-20">
    <div class="card mb-4 border">
        <div class="card-header bg-white py-3">
            <h2 class="mb-0">20 Placement Exclusions & Brand Safety Controls</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">

            <div class="alert alert-light border mb-4">
                <strong> Protect your brand from appearing next to harmful, irrelevant, or low‑quality content.</strong> Regular placement audits are essential for both Display and YouTube campaigns. This authoritative guide covers everything from basic exclusions to advanced brand safety frameworks.
            </div>

            <p>Brand safety is not optional – it's a business necessity. In 2025, consumers expect brands to be responsible about where their ads appear. A single ad next to inappropriate content can damage years of brand building. This guide will help you build a comprehensive brand safety strategy.</p>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 1: WHY BRAND SAFETY MATTERS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Why Brand Safety Matters: The Statistics</h3>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-3">
                    <div class="card bg-danger text-white text-center h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <div class="display-4">41%</div>
                            <p class="mb-0">of consumers would stop buying from a brand whose ads appear next to offensive content</p>
                            <small>(Global Web Index, 2024)</small>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-3">
                    <div class="card bg-warning text-dark text-center h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <div class="display-4">28%</div>
                            <p class="mb-0">of ad spend is wasted on low-quality or unsafe placements</p>
                            <small>(Integral Ad Science, 2024)</small>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-3">
                    <div class="card bg-success text-white text-center h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <div class="display-4">3-5x</div>
                            <p class="mb-0">higher engagement on brand-safe placements vs unsafe</p>
                            <small>(Google Internal Data)</small>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-3">
                    <div class="card bg-primary text-white text-center h-100">
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <div class="display-4">60%</div>
                            <p class="mb-0">of advertisers have experienced a brand safety incident</p>
                            <small>(ANA Programmatic Study)</small>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 2: PLACEMENT TYPES & RISK LEVELS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Placement Types & Risk Assessment Matrix</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Placement Type</th>
                            <th>Risk Level</th>
                            <th>Common Issues</th>
                            <th>Action Required</th>
                            <th>Audit Frequency</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>YouTube Channels (Unknown)</strong></td>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-danger">High Risk</span></strong></td>
                            <td>Profanity, hate speech, controversial topics</strong></td>
                            <td>Review before adding to managed placements OR exclude</strong></td>
                            <td>Weekly</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>YouTube Videos (Individual)</strong></td>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-warning">Medium-High Risk</span></strong></td>
                            <td>Misleading titles, inappropriate comments section</strong></td>
                            <td>Exclude if content doesn't match brand values</strong></td>
                            <td>Weekly</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Mobile Apps (Unknown)</strong></td>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-warning">Medium Risk</span></strong></td>
                            <td>Low-quality apps, high bounce rates, accidental clicks</strong></td>
                            <td>Exclude low CTR, high bounce rate apps</strong></td>
                            <td>Bi-weekly</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Display Websites (Premium)</strong></td>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-success">Low Risk</span></strong></td>
                            <td>Generally safe, but check for relevance</strong></td>
                            <td>Add to managed placements, monitor performance</strong></td>
                            <td>Monthly</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Display Websites (Long Tail)</strong></td>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-danger">High Risk</span></strong></td>
                            <td>Parked domains, error pages, low-quality content</strong></td>
                            <td>Review placement reports weekly, exclude aggressively</strong></td>
                            <td>Weekly</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 3: COMPLETE PLACEMENT EXCLUSION WORKFLOW ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Complete Placement Exclusion Workflow (Step-by-Step)</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h4> Step 1: Where to Find Placement Reports</h4>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Google Ads → Campaign → Placements tab</strong></li>
                        <li>For YouTube-specific: <strong>Campaign → Content → Placements</strong></li>
                        <li>Customize columns to add: <strong>CTR, Conversions, Cost, CPM, View Rate (YouTube)</strong></li>
                    </ul>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-3"> Step 2: Analyze Placement Performance (The 4-Question Test)</h4>
                    <div class="bg-light p-3 rounded mb-3">
                        <p>For each placement with significant spend (top 20% by cost), ask:</p>
                        <ol>
                            <li><strong>Content Relevance:</strong> Is the content relevant to my brand/product? (Yes/No)</li>
                            <li><strong>Engagement Metric:</strong> Is CTR > 0.1% (Display) or View Rate > 5% (YouTube)?</li>
                            <li><strong>Conversion Performance:</strong> Has this placement generated any conversions? (Zero after $50+ spend = exclude)</li>
                            <li><strong>Brand Safety:</strong> Is there ANY risk of brand association with inappropriate content?</li>
                        </ol>
                        <p><strong>Decision Rule:</strong> If ANY answer is "No" (for relevance/brand safety) OR performance is poor → <strong>Exclude immediately</strong></p>
                    </div>
                    
                    <h4 class="mt-3"> Step 3: How to Exclude Placements</h4>
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <div class="card h-100">
                                <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">Method 1: Campaign Level</div>
                                <div class="card-body small">
                                    <ol>
                                        <li>Go to Campaign → Placements</li>
                                        <li>Check box next to placement</li>
                                        <li>Click "Exclude"</li>
                                        <li>Choose "This campaign only"</li>
                                    </ol>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <div class="card h-100">
                                <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">Method 2: Account Level (Shared Library)</div>
                                <div class="card-body small">
                                    <ol>
                                        <li>Tools → Shared library</li>
                                        <li>Placement exclusion lists</li>
                                        <li>Create new list (e.g., "Brand Safety - High Risk")</li>
                                        <li>Add placements to list</li>
                                        <li>Apply list to multiple campaigns</li>
                                    </ol>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <div class="card h-100">
                                <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">Method 3: Bulk Upload</div>
                                <div class="card-body small">
                                    <ol>
                                        <li>Export placement report to CSV</li>
                                        <li>Filter poor placements</li>
                                        <li>Copy URLs to exclusion list</li>
                                        <li>Upload via Google Ads Editor</li>
                                        <li>Save and publish changes</li>
                                    </ol>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 4: CONTENT EXCLUSIONS (BRAND SAFETY TIERS) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Content Exclusions: Complete Guide (Brand Safety Tiers)</h3>
            
            <div class="alert alert-info mb-3">
                <strong> Where to find:</strong> Campaign Settings → Content suitability (or Account level: Tools → Content exclusions)
            </div>

            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-danger text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Tier 1: Digital Content Labels</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>What they are:</strong> Age/content ratings for videos (similar to movies)</p>
                            <div class="table-responsive">
                            <table class="table table-sm small">
                                <thead class="table-light">
                                    <tr><th>Label</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Action</th></tr>
                                </thead>
                                <tbody>
                                    <tr>}<strong>DL-G</strong>}</td>General audience (safe)</td><td class="text-success">Keep</td></tr>
                                    <tr>}<strong>DL-PG</strong>}</td>Parental guidance (some mature themes)</td><td class="text-warning">Review</td></tr>
                                    <tr>}<strong>DL-MA</strong>}</td>Mature audiences (adults only)</td><td class="text-danger">EXCLUDE for most brands</td></tr>
                                </tbody>
                            </table>
                            </div>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Best Practice:</strong> Exclude DL-MA for all family-friendly, B2B, and mainstream brands.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Tier 2: Inventory Types</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>What they control:</strong> Where your ads can appear on YouTube</p>
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li><strong>Live streaming:</strong> Unpredictable content, high risk</li>
                                <li><strong>Embedded videos:</strong> Videos on external websites (less control)</li>
                                <li><strong>YouTube Shorts:</strong> Fast-paced, trending content (moderate risk)</li>
                                <li><strong>YouTube watch page:</strong> Standard videos (safest)</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Recommendation:</strong> Exclude "Live streaming" for brand safety. Keep "Shorts" if targeting younger audiences.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-secondary text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0">Tier 3: Sensitive Content Categories</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>What they block:</strong> Broad categories of sensitive content</p>
                            <div class="table-responsive">
                                <table class="table table-sm small">
                                    <thead class="table-light">
                                        <tr><th>Category</th><th>Recommended</th></tr>
                                    </thead>
                                    <tbody>
                                        <tr>}<strong>Tragedy & conflict</strong>}</td><td class="text-danger">Exclude</td></tr>
                                        <tr>}<strong>Sexual content</strong>}</td><td class="text-danger">Exclude</td></tr>
                                        <tr>}<strong>Profanity</strong>}</td><td class="text-danger">Exclude</td></tr>
                                        <tr>}<strong>Sensitive social issues</strong>}</td><td class="text-warning">Review</td></tr>
                                        <tr>}<strong>Weapons</strong>}</td><td class="text-warning">Exclude (non-weapons brands)</td></tr>
                                    </tbody>
                                </table>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 5: PLACEMENT EXCLUSION CHEAT SHEET ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Placement Exclusion Cheat Sheet (What to Exclude Immediately)</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Exclusion Type</th>
                            <th>Examples</th>
                            <th>Why Exclude</th>
                            <th>Impact on Reach</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Parked Domains</strong></td>
                            <td>domain.com (coming soon), expired-domain.net</td>
                            <td>No real content, bot traffic, wasted spend</td>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-success">Low impact</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Error Pages (404, 500)</strong></td>
                            <td>websitename.com/404-page</td>
                            <td>User doesn't see ad, wasted impressions</td>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-success">Low impact</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Competitor Websites</strong></td>
                            <td>rivalcompany.com, competitorblog.com</td>
                            <td>Clicking ads benefits competitors, high bounce rate</td>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-warning">Medium impact (review first)</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Low-Quality Content Farms</strong></td>
                            <td>article-spinner.com, clickbait-site.net</td>
                            <td>Poor brand association, high bounce rate</td>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-success">Low impact</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>YouTube Channels with Profanity</strong></td>
                            <td>Channels flagged for hate speech or mature content</td>
                            <td>Direct brand risk, negative association</td>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-success">Low impact (1-2% reach loss)</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Mobile Apps with Low Engagement</strong></td>
                            <td>Apps with <0.05% CTR or >80% bounce rate</td>
                            <td>Wasted spend, accidental clicks</td>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-success">Low impact</span></td>
                        </tr>
                        </tr>
                            <td><strong>Irrelevant Topic Categories</strong></td>
                            <td>Gaming ads on news websites (if not gaming brand)</td>
                            <td>Low relevance = low CTR</td>
                            <td><span class="badge bg-warning">Medium impact (narrow targeting)</span></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 6: AUTOMATED RULES FOR PLACEMENT MANAGEMENT ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Automated Rules for Placement Management (Save Hours)</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p><strong>Where to find:</strong> Tools → Automated rules</p>
                    
                    <h4> Essential Automated Rules for Brand Safety:</h4>
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-bordered">
                            <thead class="table-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Rule Name</th>
                                    <th>Condition</th>
                                    <th>Action</th>
                                    <th>Frequency</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Auto-Exclude Low CTR Placements</strong></td>
                                    <td>Placement CTR < 0.05% AND Impressions > 1,000</td>
                                    <td>Pause placement</td>
                                    <td>Weekly</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Auto-Exclude Zero Conversion Placements</strong></td>
                                    <td>Cost > $50 AND Conversions = 0</td>
                                    <td>Pause placement</td>
                                    <td>Daily</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td><strong>Auto-Exclude High Bounce Placements</strong></td>
                                    <td>Bounce rate > 80% AND Sessions > 100</td>
                                    <td>Pause placement</td>
                                    <td>Daily (if GA4 linked)</td>
                                </tr>
                                </tr>
                                    <td><strong>Brand Safety Alert</strong></td>
                                    <td>Placement contains keywords: "hate", "violence", "adult"</td>
                                    <td>Send email alert</td>
                                    <td>Hourly</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-warning mt-3">
                        <strong> Caution:</strong> Test automated rules in "Send email only" mode for 1 week before activating automatic exclusions. Poorly configured rules can exclude profitable placements.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 7: NEGATIVE KEYWORDS FOR DISPLAY ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Negative Keywords for Display Campaigns (Content Exclusions)</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p><strong>What they do:</strong> Prevent your display ads from appearing on pages containing specific keywords.</p>
                    
                    <h4> Negative Keyword Categories to Add:</h4>
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong> Free/Cheap Keywords:</strong>
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li>free, gratis, no cost</li>
                                <li>cheap, discount, coupon</li>
                                <li>torrent, cracked, warez</li>
                                <li>sample, trial (if not offering)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong> Negative Content Keywords:</strong>
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li>violence, death, kill</li>
                                <li>adult, porn, xxx</li>
                                <li>hate, racist, nazi</li>
                                <li>gambling, casino, poker</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong> Competitor Keywords:</strong>
                            <ul class="small">
                                <li>[competitor brand names]</li>
                                <li>vs, versus, alternative</li>
                                <li>review, complaint, scam</li>
                                <li>lawsuit, problem, issue</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                        <strong> Pro Tip:</strong> Add negative keywords at <strong>campaign level</strong> (not account level) so you can have different rules for different campaigns. Update weekly based on search term reports.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 8: YOUTUBE-SPECIFIC BRAND SAFETY ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> YouTube-Specific Brand Safety Controls</h3>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-danger text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0"> YouTube Channel Exclusions</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>What to exclude:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Channels with profanity or hate speech</li>
                                <li>Channels covering controversial topics (politics, religion) – unless relevant</li>
                                <li>Channels with low production quality (reflects poorly on brand)</li>
                                <li>Competitor channels (if you don't want to fund them)</li>
                                <li>Channels with comment sections full of spam or negativity</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p><strong>How to find channels to exclude:</strong></p>
                            <ol>
                                <li>Run automatic placement campaign for 1-2 weeks</li>
                                <li>Export placement report, filter by "YouTube"</li>
                                <li>Review each channel manually (visit channel page)</li>
                                <li>Add questionable channels to exclusion list</li>
                            </ol>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark">
                            <h4 class="mb-0"> YouTube Comment Moderation & Ad Adjacency</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <p><strong>Risk:</strong> Your ad can appear on videos with toxic comment sections. Even if the video is safe, comments can be problematic.</p>
                            <p><strong>Mitigation strategies:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Exclude videos with disabled comments</strong> (often indicates controversial content)</li>
                                <li><strong>Use content exclusions</strong> for "Profanity" and "Hate speech" categories</li>
                                <li><strong>Review comment sections</strong> of top-spend placements weekly</li>
                                <li><strong>Consider third-party verification</strong> (DoubleVerify, IAS) for enterprise brands</li>
                            </ul>
                            <div class="alert alert-light small mt-2 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> For high-risk industries (finance, healthcare, education), use <strong>limited inventory type</strong> or <strong>standard inventory type</strong> instead of expanded inventory.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 9: THIRD-PARTY BRAND SAFETY TOOLS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Third-Party Brand Safety Tools (Enterprise Level)</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Tool</th>
                            <th>What It Does</th>
                            <th>Best For</th>
                            <th>Approximate Cost</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>DoubleVerify (DV)</strong></td>
