- 5 headlines using 'price/savings' angle
- 5 headlines using 'quality/premium' angle
- 5 headlines using 'speed/convenience' angle
- 5 headlines using 'social proof/trust' angle
Each headline max 35 characters.
This will allow me to A/B test which angle converts best."</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 6: AI COPY TESTING METHODOLOGY ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> AI Copy Testing Methodology (How to Find Winners)</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-3 text-center">
                            <div class="bg-light p-3 rounded h-100">
                                <span class="badge bg-primary mb-2">Step 1</span>
                                <p><strong>Generate</strong></p>
                                <small>Use 5-10 prompts to generate 50-100 headline/description variations</small>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3 text-center">
                            <div class="bg-light p-3 rounded h-100">
                                <span class="badge bg-success mb-2">Step 2</span>
                                <p><strong>Filter & Edit</strong></p>
                                <small>Remove duplicates, fix grammar, ensure character limits, match brand voice</small>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3 text-center">
                            <div class="bg-light p-3 rounded h-100">
                                <span class="badge bg-warning mb-2">Step 3</span>
                                <p><strong>Test</strong></p>
                                <small>Load into responsive display ad (5+ headlines, 4+ descriptions). Run for 2 weeks</small>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-3 text-center">
                            <div class="bg-light p-3 rounded h-100">
                                <span class="badge bg-danger mb-2">Step 4</span>
                                <p><strong>Analyze & Scale</strong></p>
                                <small>Check asset performance report. Keep top 20%, pause bottom 40%. Add new variations</small>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <div class="alert alert-info mt-3">
                        <strong> Pro Tip:</strong> Use Google Ads' <strong>"Asset performance"</strong> report (Campaign → Ads & assets → View asset details). Sort by CTR and conversion rate. Pause assets with "Low" performance rating after 2 weeks.
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 7: AI COPY EDITING CHECKLIST ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> AI Copy Editing Checklist (Before Launch)</h3>
            
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <strong> Headline Checklist:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>□ All headlines under character limit (30 or 90)</li>
                                <li>□ No punctuation at end of short headlines</li>
                                <li>□ No clickbait or misleading claims</li>
                                <li>□ Brand name included where appropriate</li>
                                <li>□ No all-caps or excessive punctuation!!!</li>
                                <li>□ Test on mobile (readable on small screen)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <strong> Description Checklist:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>□ All descriptions under 90 characters</li>
                                <li>□ Each description ends with a CTA</li>
                                <li>□ No duplicate or near-duplicate descriptions</li>
                                <li>□ Clear value proposition in first 40 characters</li>
                                <li>□ No grammar or spelling errors</li>
                                <li>□ Landing page match (ad copy matches page offer)</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 8: COMMON AI COPY MISTAKES ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> 10 Common AI Copy Mistakes & How to Fix Them</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Mistake</th>
                            <th>Consequence</th>
                            <th>How to Fix</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Generic, bland copy</strong></td>
                            <td>Low CTR, no differentiation</strong></td>
                            <td>Add specificity: numbers, examples, audience details to prompts</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Character limit violations</strong></td>
                            <td>Headlines/descriptions cut off or rejected</strong></td>
                            <td>Add "max X characters" to every prompt; use character counter tool</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Repetitive variations</strong></td>
                            <td>Limited testing pool, missed opportunities</strong></td>
                            <td>Ask for "10 completely different angles" in prompt</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No CTA in descriptions</strong></td>
                            <td>Users watch but don't click</strong></td>
                            <td>Add "end each description with a CTA" to prompt</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Mismatched landing page</strong></td>
                            <td>High bounce rate, low conversion</strong></td>
                            <td>Include final URL offer in prompt context</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Ignoring brand voice</strong></td>
                            <td>Inconsistent brand perception</strong></td>
                            <td>Provide 3-5 existing brand copy examples in prompt</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Not testing variations</strong></td>
                            <td>Unknown what works, leaving performance on table</strong></td>
                            <td>Always test 5+ headlines and 4+ descriptions simultaneously</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Using AI copy without editing</strong></td>
                            <td>Grammar errors, awkward phrasing</strong></td>
                            <td>Always human-review and edit before launch</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 9: QUICK REFERENCE ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> Quick Reference: Best Prompts by Use Case</h3>
            
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong> For Display Ads:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>Short headlines: Prompt 1.1</li>
                                <li>Benefit descriptions: Prompt D1.1</li>
                                <li>PAS framework: Prompt D2.1</li>
                                <li>Urgency: Prompt 4.1</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong> For YouTube Discovery:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>Question headlines: Prompt 2.1</li>
                                <li>Curiosity descriptions: Prompt D3.1</li>
                                <li>Educational: Prompt D3.2</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong> For E-commerce:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>Social proof: Prompt 3.1</li>
                                <li>Product benefits: Prompt D4.1</li>
                                <li>Cart abandon: Prompt Ecom 2</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 10: SUMMARY ==================== -->
            <div class="alert alert-success mt-4">
                <h3 class="fw-bold"> AI Prompts Summary</h3>
                <div class="row">
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <strong> Key Takeaways:</strong>
                        <ul class="small mb-0">
                            <li><strong>Specific prompts = better output:</strong> Include character limits, examples, and frameworks</li>
                            <li><strong>Generate 50-100 variations</strong> – then filter to the best 10-20 for testing</li>
                            <li><strong>Always human-edit AI copy</strong> – check grammar, brand voice, and compliance</li>
                            <li><strong>Test systematically</strong> – 5+ headlines, 4+ descriptions per responsive ad</li>
                            <li><strong>Iterate your prompts</strong> – refine based on what performs well</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                        <strong> Himanshu's Prompt Formula:</strong>
                        <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-2 small rounded mt-2">High-Converting Prompt = 
  [Role/Persona]
  + [Audience Description]
  + [Specific Format & Limits]
  + [Framework (PAS/BAB/AIDA)]
  + [Examples]
  + [What to Avoid]</pre>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="alert alert-primary mt-2">
                <strong> Himanshu's Final Word:</strong> AI won't replace copywriters – but copywriters who use AI will replace those who don't. These prompts are your starting point. Customize them for your brand, your audience, and your offer. Test everything. Keep the winners. Refine your prompts. The more you use AI, the better your results will become.
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</div>
