                         <!-- ========== 22 AI PROMPT TEMPLATES FOR DISPLAY & VIDEO CAMPAIGN CREATION (AUTHORITY DEEP DIVE) ========== -->
<div class="section" id="topic-22">
    <div class="card mb-4 border">
        <div class="card-header bg-white py-3">
            <h2 class="mb-0">22 AI Prompt Templates for Display & Video Campaign Creation</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body p-4">

            <div class="alert alert-light border mb-4">
                <strong> Go from idea to campaign structure in minutes.</strong> Use these advanced prompts to generate targeting ideas, ad group themes, video scripts, optimization plans, and full campaign outlines. This guide includes 35+ prompts organized by campaign phase.
            </div>

            <p>AI can do more than write headlines – it can help you <strong>plan entire campaigns</strong>, from audience discovery to creative strategy to optimization. These advanced prompts will turn ChatGPT, Claude, or Gemini into your personal Google Ads strategist.</p>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 1: PROMPT ENGINEERING FOR CAMPAIGN STRATEGY ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4"> How to Use These Prompts (Best Practices)</h3>
            
            <div class="row g-4 mb-4">
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0"> How to Get Best Results</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Fill in ALL placeholders</strong> – [business type], [product], [location] – be specific</li>
                                <li><strong>Provide context first</strong> – Give AI background about your business, audience, and goals</li>
                                <li><strong>Use chain-of-thought</strong> – Ask AI to "think step by step" before answering</li>
                                <li><strong>Request structured output</strong> – Ask for tables, bullet points, or numbered lists</li>
                                <li><strong>Iterate based on output</strong> – Refine prompts with "Now make it more [specific/focused/creative]"</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-6">
                    <div class="card h-100">
                        <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white">
                            <h4 class="mb-0"> Information to Provide Before Prompts</h4>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-body">
                            <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Here is information about my business:
- Business name: [name]
- Product/service: [description]
- Target audience: [age, job title, pain points]
- Unique selling proposition: [what makes you different]
- Monthly ad budget: [$ amount]
- Campaign goal: [awareness/traffic/conversions/remarketing]
- Geographic target: [country/city/radius]
- Existing customer data: [what you know about buyers]"</code></pre>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 2: TARGETING STRATEGY PROMPTS (ACCORDION) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Targeting Strategy Prompts (Audience, Keywords, Placements)</h3>
            
            <div class="accordion mb-4" id="targetingAccordion">
                
                <!-- Audience Discovery -->
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h4 class="accordion-header" id="targetingOne">
                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#targetCollapseOne">
                             Prompt Category 1: Audience Discovery & Segmentation
                        </button>
                    </h4>
                    <div id="targetCollapseOne" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#targetingAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body bg-light">
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt A1 (Complete Audience Strategy):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"You are a Google Ads audience strategist. For a [business type] selling [product/service] to [target audience description] in [location], provide:

1. 5 In-Market audiences (people actively researching to buy) – explain why each fits
2. 5 Affinity audiences (people with long-term interests) – explain why each fits
3. 3 Custom Intent audiences – build each from 5-10 keywords, 3-5 competitor URLs, and 2-3 relevant apps
4. 3 Life Event audiences (graduation, moving, wedding, new job) – if relevant
5. Recommended audience layering combinations (2-3 methods combined)

Format as a table with columns: Audience Type, Name, Rationale, Expected Intent Level (High/Medium/Low)"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt A2 (B2B Account-Based Targeting):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"For a B2B [business type] selling [product/service] to [company size/industry], provide:

1. 5 Job title/role targeting ideas (e.g., 'IT Managers', 'Marketing Directors')
2. 3 Company-based custom audiences (using company URL lists)
3. 5 LinkedIn-like professional interest audiences available on GDN/YouTube
4. Recommended bid adjustments for each (percentage above baseline)

Format as a table with columns: Audience, Estimated Monthly Reach, Recommended Bid Adjustment (+X%), Expected CVR"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <strong>Prompt A3 (Demographic Layering):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"For [product/service], provide demographic targeting recommendations:

1. Age ranges to target (and which to exclude)
2. Gender recommendations (male/female/both) with reasoning
3. Household income brackets (top 10%, 20%, 30%, etc.) based on product price point
4. Parental status recommendations (parents only / non-parents / both)
5. Education level targeting (if relevant)

Format as bullet points with clear reasoning for each recommendation."</code></pre>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Keyword Targeting -->
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h4 class="accordion-header" id="targetingTwo">
                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#targetCollapseTwo">
                             Prompt Category 2: Keyword Targeting for YouTube
                        </button>
                    </h4>
                    <div id="targetCollapseTwo" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#targetingAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body bg-light">
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt K1 (YouTube Search Keywords):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"You are a YouTube SEO and ads expert. For [product/service] targeting [audience], provide:

1. 20 YouTube search keywords (what people type into YouTube search) categorized by intent:
   - Problem-aware keywords (e.g., 'why is my [problem] happening')
   - Solution-aware keywords (e.g., 'how to fix [problem]')
   - Product-aware keywords (e.g., '[product name] review')
   - Ready-to-buy keywords (e.g., 'buy [product] online')

2. For each keyword, suggest match type (broad/phrase/exact)
3. Identify 10 negative keywords to exclude (e.g., 'free', 'cheap', 'torrent', 'cracked')

Format as a table with columns: Keyword, Match Type, Intent Level, Search Volume Estimate"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt K2 (Video Content Keywords):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Generate 15 keyword phrases that describe the CONTENT of videos where my ideal audience watches.
For [product/service] targeting [audience], people would likely watch videos about:
- [topic 1]
- [topic 2]
- [topic 3]

Provide keywords as phrases (e.g., 'how to train for marathon' not just 'marathon').
Categorize by: Educational, Review/Comparison, Tutorial/How-to, Entertainment."</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <strong>Prompt K3 (Competitor Keyword Conquesting):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"For a [business type] selling [product/service], identify:
1. 10 competitor brand names to target as keywords
2. 15 'vs' or 'alternative' keywords (e.g., 'product vs competitor')
3. 10 'review' or 'comparison' keywords for competitor products
4. Suggested negative keywords to exclude your own brand from conquesting campaigns

Format each category as a bulleted list."</code></pre>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Placement Targeting -->
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h4 class="accordion-header" id="targetingThree">
                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#targetCollapseThree">
                             Prompt Category 3: Placement & Channel Targeting
                        </button>
                    </h4>
                    <div id="targetCollapseThree" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#targetingAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body bg-light">
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt P1 (YouTube Channel Placements):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Recommend 15 YouTube channels for placement targeting for [product/service] targeting [audience].

Include:
- 5 competitor channels (direct competitors)
- 5 complementary channels (related but not competing products)
- 3 influencer channels (creators with engaged audiences)
- 2 industry news/educational channels

For each channel, provide: Channel name, URL, Subscriber count (approx), Why it fits, Expected engagement level (High/Medium/Low)"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt P2 (Website Placements for Display):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Recommend 20 websites for display placement targeting for [product/service] targeting [audience].

Categorize by:
- Tier 1 (Premium, high authority): 5 sites
- Tier 2 (Industry-specific blogs/publications): 8 sites
- Tier 3 (Niche forums/communities): 4 sites
- Tier 4 (Review/comparison sites): 3 sites

For each, provide: Website URL, Category, Why audience visits, Expected CPM range"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <strong>Prompt P3 (Placement Exclusion Recommendations):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"For a [business type] running display/video campaigns, provide a list of placement exclusion categories to add immediately:

1. Content categories to exclude (e.g., tragedy, profanity, adult)
2. YouTube channel types to exclude (e.g., political commentary, clickbait)
3. App categories to exclude (e.g., gaming apps with accidental clicks)
4. Domain types to exclude (e.g., parked domains, error pages)

Provide as a categorized checklist with 'Exclude' or 'Review' recommendations."</code></pre>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 3: CAMPAIGN STRUCTURE PROMPTS (ACCORDION) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Campaign Structure & Ad Group Theming Prompts</h3>
            
            <div class="accordion mb-4" id="structureAccordion">
                
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h4 class="accordion-header" id="structureOne">
                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#structureCollapseOne">
                             Prompt Category 1: Complete Campaign Architecture
                        </button>
                    </h4>
                    <div id="structureCollapseOne" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#structureAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body bg-light">
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt C1 (Full Campaign Structure):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"You are a Google Ads expert. Create a complete campaign structure for [product/service] with a monthly budget of $[amount] targeting [location] and [audience].

Campaign goal: [awareness / consideration / conversions / remarketing]

Provide:
1. Campaign naming convention recommendation
2. Campaign-level settings: budget split across ad groups, bidding strategy, ad schedule, frequency cap
3. 4-6 ad groups with:
   - Ad group name
   - Targeting method (audience/keywords/placements/topics)
   - Specific targeting values
   - Suggested bid adjustment
   - Sample headlines (3-5 per ad group)
   - Sample descriptions (2-3 per ad group)
4. Recommended budget allocation (%) per ad group
5. Suggested A/B test to run first

Format as a structured campaign outline with tables for ad groups."</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt C2 (Funnel-Based Campaign Structure):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Create a full-funnel campaign structure for [product/service] with 3 campaigns:

Campaign 1 (Top of Funnel - Awareness):
- Campaign type: Video Views or Display Awareness
- Targeting: [suggest 2-3 methods]
- Budget allocation: 40%
- Key metrics to track: reach, CPM, VTR

Campaign 2 (Middle of Funnel - Consideration):
- Campaign type: Display or Video Action
- Targeting: [suggest 2-3 methods]
- Budget allocation: 30%
- Key metrics: CTR, CPC, view-through rate

Campaign 3 (Bottom of Funnel - Conversion/Remarketing):
- Campaign type: Remarketing or Video Action
- Targeting: [suggest 2-3 remarketing lists]
- Budget allocation: 30%
- Key metrics: CPA, ROAS, conversion rate

For each campaign, provide 3-4 ad groups with specific targeting."</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <strong>Prompt C3 (Budget & Bid Strategy Recommendations):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Based on a monthly budget of $[amount] for [product/service] with an average order value of $[AOV] and target ROAS of [X]%, provide:

1. Daily budget recommendation per campaign (assuming [number] campaigns)
2. Bid strategy recommendations for:
   - Prospecting display campaign
   - Prospecting video campaign
   - Remarketing campaign
3. Bid adjustment recommendations for:
   - Mobile devices (+X%)
   - Top 3 cities/regions (+X%)
   - Peak hours (+X%)
4. Impression share targets and budget adjustments needed

Show calculations where applicable."</code></pre>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Video Sequence Scripts -->
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h4 class="accordion-header" id="structureTwo">
                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#structureCollapseTwo">
                             Prompt Category 2: Video Sequence & Script Generation
                        </button>
                    </h4>
                    <div id="structureCollapseTwo" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#structureAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body bg-light">
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt V1 (3-Video Sequence Script):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Write a complete 3-video sequence script for a YouTube campaign promoting [product/service] to [audience].

Video 1 (15 seconds - Problem/Hook):
- Hook in first 3 seconds: [suggest a hook]
- Visual direction
- Voiceover script (word-for-word)
- On-screen text suggestions

Video 2 (30 seconds - Solution/Explanation):
- Transition from Video 1
- Product demonstration or feature explanation
- Voiceover script
- Visual/B-roll suggestions
- On-screen text

Video 3 (15 seconds - Urgency/CTA):
- Recap key benefit
- Urgency element (limited time, limited stock)
- Clear call-to-action
- End screen instructions

Each video should have captions burned in. Provide script in a table format with columns: Time, Visual, Audio, On-Screen Text."</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt V2 (6-Second Bumper Sequence):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Write a 3-part bumper ad sequence (6 seconds each) for [product/service].

Bumper 1 (Awareness): Quick problem statement + brand name
Bumper 2 (Consideration): Single key benefit + visual demonstration
Bumper 3 (Conversion): Urgency + CTA + brand logo

For each bumper, provide:
- 6-second script (word-for-word)
- Visual direction
- On-screen text (keep minimal, 3-4 words max)
- Color/brand guidelines"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <strong>Prompt V3 (Testimonial/Review Video Script):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Create a 30-second testimonial video script for [product/service] featuring a customer [name/generic].

Structure:
0-5s: Customer introduction + problem before
5-15s: How product solved the problem (specific results)
15-25s: Emotional benefit + recommendation
25-30s: CTA + brand logo

Include:
- Voiceover script
- B-roll suggestions (product in use, before/after)
- On-screen text for key stats (e.g., 'Saved 20 hours/week')
- Suggested customer quote for thumbnail"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 4: CREATIVE STRATEGY PROMPTS (ACCORDION) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Creative Strategy & Ad Copy Prompts</h3>
            
            <div class="accordion mb-4" id="creativeAccordion">
                
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h4 class="accordion-header" id="creativeOne">
                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#creativeCollapseOne">
                            Prompt Category 1: Responsive Display Ad Copy Packages
                        </button>
                    </h4>
                    <div id="creativeCollapseOne" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#creativeAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body bg-light">
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt R1 (Complete Display Ad Copy Package):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Generate a complete responsive display ad copy package for [product/service] targeting [audience] with [unique selling proposition].

Provide:
1. 10 short headlines (max 30 characters) using different angles:
   - 2 benefit-focused
   - 2 urgency/scarcity
   - 2 question-based
   - 2 social proof
   - 2 CTA-direct

2. 3 long headlines (max 90 characters) that are more descriptive

3. 8 descriptions (max 90 characters) each ending with a CTA:
   - 2 PAS framework
   - 2 feature-benefit
   - 2 offer/discount focused
   - 2 social proof

4. Business name (max 25 characters)

Format as organized lists by category."</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt R2 (Image Asset Recommendations):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"For a responsive display ad promoting [product/service], recommend:

1. 3 landscape image concepts (1.91:1, 1200x628) - describe visual elements, colors, text overlay suggestions
2. 3 square image concepts (1:1, 1200x1200) - describe visual elements
3. Logo placement and size recommendations
4. Color palette recommendations based on brand [existing brand colors or industry]

For each image concept, explain why it would resonate with [target audience]."</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <strong>Prompt R3 (A/B Test Creative Plan):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Create a 4-week creative A/B testing plan for [product/service].

Week 1-2: Test headline angles (test [X] variations)
Week 2-3: Test description frameworks (test [Y] variations)
Week 3-4: Test image styles (test [Z] variations)

For each test, provide:
- What to test (specific variations)
- Success metric (CTR, conversion rate, or CPA)
- Minimum sample size needed (impressions)
- Decision rule (which variation wins and by how much)

Provide a tracking spreadsheet template for results."</code></pre>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 5: OPTIMIZATION & REPORTING PROMPTS (ACCORDION) ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Optimization & Reporting Prompts</h3>
            
            <div class="accordion mb-4" id="optimizationAccordion">
                
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h4 class="accordion-header" id="optimizationOne">
                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#optimizationCollapseOne">
                            Prompt Category 1: Performance Diagnosis & Fixes
                        </button>
                    </h4>
                    <div id="optimizationCollapseOne" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#optimizationAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body bg-light">
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt O1 (Low CTR Diagnosis):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"My display campaign has a CTR of 0.15% (below 0.35% benchmark). Provide:

1. 8 possible reasons for low CTR (categorized by: creative, targeting, placement, settings)
2. For each reason, a diagnostic step to confirm (what to check in Google Ads)
3. Specific fix for each issue
4. Priority order (what to check first, second, third)

Include a checklist I can use to systematically diagnose the issue."</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt O2 (High CPA Diagnosis):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"My YouTube campaign has a CPA of $[amount], which is [X]% above my target of $[target]. Provide:

1. 10 possible causes organized by funnel stage:
   - Pre-click issues (targeting, creative, ad format)
   - Click issues (CTR, relevance)
   - Post-click issues (landing page, offer, CTA)

2. For each cause, specific data points to check in Google Ads and GA4
3. Recommended fix with expected impact (e.g., 'Improve CPA by 15-20%')
4. A/B test recommendation to validate the fix"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <strong>Prompt O3 (Placement Audit Action Plan):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Given a placement report with the following issues:
- 20% of spend on placements with CTR < 0.1%
- 35% of spend on placements with zero conversions
- Ads appearing on [list questionable site categories]

Provide:
1. Step-by-step placement audit process (30-minute workflow)
2. Decision matrix for when to exclude vs. reduce bids vs. keep
3. 5 automated rules to set up for ongoing placement management
4. Shared exclusion list strategy (campaign vs account level)
5. Template for weekly placement review documentation"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Creative Refresh -->
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h4 class="accordion-header" id="optimizationTwo">
                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#optimizationCollapseTwo">
                            Prompt Category 2: Creative Refresh & Testing
                        </button>
                    </h4>
                    <div id="optimizationCollapseTwo" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#optimizationAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body bg-light">
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt CR1 (Creative Refresh Ideas):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"My display campaign has been running for 6 weeks with CTR declining from 0.5% to 0.3%. Suggest:

1. 10 new headline angles to test (based on [product features] and [customer pain points])
2. 8 new description approaches (different offers, CTAs, or value props)
3. 5 new image style suggestions (e.g., lifestyle vs product-only vs text-heavy)
4. 3 new offer variations to test (discount %, free shipping, bundle, etc.)

For each suggestion, include:
- Why it might improve performance
- Which audience segment to test it with
- Estimated lift potential (low/medium/high)"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <strong>Prompt CR2 (Seasonal Creative Calendar):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Create a 12-month seasonal creative calendar for [product/service] including:

1. Major holidays/events relevant to [industry]
2. For each event: recommended ad angle, sample headline, sample description, offer type
3. Lead time needed for creative production before each event
4. Budget adjustment recommendations for peak periods

Events to include: [list relevant holidays like Black Friday, Christmas, Summer, Back to School, etc.]"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Budget Optimization -->
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h4 class="accordion-header" id="optimizationThree">
                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#optimizationCollapseThree">
                            Prompt Category 3: Budget & Bidding Optimization
                        </button>
                    </h4>
                    <div id="optimizationCollapseThree" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#optimizationAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body bg-light">
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt B1 (Budget Reallocation Strategy):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"My monthly ad budget is $[amount] across [X] campaigns. Current performance data:
- Campaign A (Prospecting): CPA $[X], Conv [Y], ROAS [Z]%
- Campaign B (Remarketing): CPA $[X], Conv [Y], ROAS [Z]%
- Campaign C (Awareness): CPM $[X], VTR [Y]%, Brand lift [Z]%

Provide:
1. Recommended budget reallocation (% change per campaign)
2. Expected impact on total conversions and CPA
3. Phased approach (how to shift budget without disrupting performance)
4. Impression share goals to aim for with adjusted budgets"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt B2 (Bid Strategy Transition Plan):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"My campaign currently uses Maximize Clicks bidding and has generated 50+ conversions in 30 days. Provide:

1. Step-by-step plan to transition to Target CPA bidding
2. Recommended Target CPA based on historical data (show calculation)
3. Learning phase expectations (how long, expected CPA fluctuation)
4. Backup plan if Target CPA underperforms
5. Timeline for evaluating success (7, 14, 30 days)"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <strong>Prompt B3 (Dayparting & Device Bid Adjustments):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Based on [product/service] with target audience [description], provide:

1. Recommended ad schedule (days and hours) with bid adjustments (+X% during peak)
2. Device bid adjustments for mobile, desktop, and tablet with reasoning
3. Geographic bid adjustments for top 5 locations based on [data or assumptions]
4. Audience bid adjustments for different remarketing lists

For each, explain the expected impact on CPA and conversion volume."</code></pre>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 6: COMPETITOR ANALYSIS PROMPTS ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Competitor Analysis & Conquesting Prompts</h3>
            
            <div class="accordion mb-4" id="competitorAccordion">
                
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h4 class="accordion-header" id="competitorOne">
                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#competitorCollapseOne">
                            Competitor Strategy Analysis
                        </button>
                    </h4>
                    <div id="competitorCollapseOne" class="accordion-collapse collapse" data-bs-parent="#competitorAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body bg-light">
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt COMP1 (Competitor Display Strategy Analysis):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Research [competitor name] (or provide known information about them). As a Google Ads strategist, analyze:

1. What display ad formats they're likely using (responsive, static, Gmail, discovery)
2. What audience targeting they might be using (in-market, affinity, custom intent)
3. What placement strategy they employ (competitor conquesting? premium sites?)
4. What creative angles and offers they test
5. Gaps in their strategy that you could exploit

Based on this analysis, provide:
- 3 targeting opportunities they're missing
- 2 creative angles they're not using
- 1 conquesting strategy to take market share"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <strong>Prompt COMP2 (Competitor Keyword Conquesting Plan):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Create a complete competitor conquesting campaign for [business type] against [competitor names]:

1. 20 competitor brand keywords to target (include misspellings)
2. 15 'vs' or 'comparison' keywords
3. 10 'alternative to [competitor]' keywords
4. Recommended ad copy angles for conquesting:
   - 5 headlines that highlight your advantages over competitor
   - 3 descriptions that address competitor weaknesses
5. Landing page recommendations for conquesting traffic
6. Exclusion strategy (negative keywords to avoid your own brand)
7. Budget recommendation as % of total spend"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                            <div>
                                <strong>Prompt COMP3 (Competitor Placement Conquesting):</strong>
                                <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>"Identify YouTube channels and websites where [competitor name] is likely advertising, and recommend a placement conquesting strategy:

1. 10 YouTube channels to target (competitor's own channel + channels they likely sponsor)
2. 15 websites where competitor display ads likely appear
3. Recommended bid adjustments for these placements (+X% vs standard)
4. Creative angles specifically for users seeing competitor ads
5. Tracking plan to measure conquesting performance"</code></pre>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 7: PROMPT LIBRARY SYSTEM ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Creating Your Own Prompt Library (Pro System)</h3>
            
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h4>Suggested Prompt Library Structure:</h4>
                            <pre class="bg-dark text-white p-3 rounded"><code>/Prompt Library/
├── 01_Strategy/
│   ├── audience_discovery.txt
│   ├── competitor_conquesting.txt
│   └── budget_allocation.txt
├── 02_Targeting/
│   ├── youtube_keywords.txt
│   ├── placements_channels.txt
│   └── demographics_layering.txt
├── 03_Creative/
│   ├── headlines_short.txt
│   ├── descriptions_pas.txt
│   ├── video_scripts_sequence.txt
│   └── image_concepts.txt
├── 04_Optimization/
│   ├── low_ctr_diagnosis.txt
│   ├── high_cpa_fixes.txt
│   └── placement_audit.txt
└── 05_Reporting/
    ├── weekly_dashboard.txt
    └── performance_analysis.txt</code></pre>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <h4>How to Use Your Prompt Library:</h4>
                            <ol>
                                <li>Save each prompt as a separate text file</li>
                                <li>Use placeholders in ALL CAPS like [PRODUCT], [AUDIENCE], [BUDGET]</li>
                                <li>Create a master template with your business context</li>
                                <li>When starting a new campaign, copy relevant prompts and fill placeholders</li>
                                <li>Save successful outputs as examples for future prompts</li>
                                <li>Review and refine prompts quarterly based on what works</li>
                            </ol>
                            <div class="alert alert-success mt-3 mb-0">
                                 <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Use a tool like Notion, Obsidian, or a simple Google Doc to store your prompt library with tags for quick searching.
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 8: COMMON MISTAKES ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">10 Common AI Campaign Planning Mistakes & How to Fix Them</h3>
            
            <div class="table-responsive mb-4">
                <table class="table table-bordered table-striped">
                    <thead class="table-dark">
                        <tr>
                            <th>Mistake</th>
                            <th>Consequence</th>
                            <th>How to Fix</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Not providing enough business context</strong></td>
                            <td>Generic, irrelevant recommendations</strong></td>
                            <td>Use the context template before every prompt</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Asking for too much in one prompt</strong></td>
                            <td>Overwhelming, unfocused output</strong></td>
                            <td>Break into 3-5 smaller, focused prompts</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Accepting AI output without editing</strong></td>
                            <td>Unrealistic or non-actionable recommendations</strong></td>
                            <td>Always review and adapt to your specific situation</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No iteration on prompts</strong></td>
                            <td>Suboptimal output quality</strong></td>
                            <td>Refine prompts: "Now make it more specific/focused"</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Not requesting structured output</strong></td>
                            <td>Hard-to-read text blocks</strong></td>
                            <td>Ask for tables, bullet points, or numbered lists</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Ignoring platform-specific constraints</strong></td>
                            <td>Recommendations that don't work in Google Ads</strong></td>
                            <td>Include platform name and character limits in prompts</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>No testing of AI recommendations</strong></td>
                            <td>Unknown if suggestions work</strong></td>
                            <td>Always A/B test AI suggestions against current best practices</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td>Using outdated prompt patterns</strong></td>
                            <td>Poor quality output</strong></td>
                            <td>Use chain-of-thought and persona-based prompting</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>

            <!-- ==================== SECTION 9: QUICK REFERENCE ==================== -->
            <h3 class="fw-semibold mt-4">Quick Reference: Best Prompts by Use Case</h3>
            
            <div class="card bg-light mb-4">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong>For Campaign Strategy:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
                                <li>Full campaign structure: Prompt C1</li>
                                <li>Audience discovery: Prompt A1</li>
                                <li>Budget allocation: Prompt B1</li>
                                <li>Competitor analysis: Prompt COMP1</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-4">
                            <strong>For Creative & Scripts:</strong>
                            <ul class="small mb-0">
